E["npc:archbishop-benedictus"] = {t="npc",n="Archbishop Benedictus",z="wetlands",s="Archbishop Benedictus is the supreme spiritual leader of the Church of the Holy Light, presiding over the faithful from the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City. Once the devoted student of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, he now guides the moral and religious heart of the Alliance during a time of immense uncertainty.",h="Archbishop Benedictus is the supreme spiritual leader of the Church of the Holy Light, presiding over the...",sec={{t="Shepherd of the Holy Light",b="Benedictus rose to leadership following the death of his revered mentor, Archbishop Alonsus Faol. Having witnessed the devastation of the First and Second Wars, Benedictus helped oversee the construction of the grand Cathedral of Light in Stormwind City, vowing to preserve the virtues of the faith. With the fall of Lordaeron and the rise of the Scourge during the Third War, the weight of the human kingdoms' spiritual guidance fell squarely on his shoulders. From his altar, he offers counsel to the royal court, trains newly initiated priests, and directs holy crusades against the undead and demonic forces threatening Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="A Burdened Conviction",b="Though regarded across the Alliance as a gentle, wise, and benevolent patriarch, Benedictus carries profound grief from the Third War. The slaughter of Lordaeron's people and the tragic fall of Prince Arthas Menethil deeply tested the Church's understanding of divine protection. Despite these hidden spiritual trials, Benedictus presents an unyielding beacon of hope to the public, rallying heroes to vanquish dark threats such as Amnennar the Coldbringer in Kalimdor and assisting in purifying cursed relics brought by faithful adventurers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archbishop Benedictus?",a="He is the reigning leader of the Church of the Holy Light and the highest religious authority in the Grand Alliance. Stationed in Stormwind City's Cathedral of Light, he guides the faithful and counsels the kingdom's leaders.",al={"benedictus","archbishop stormwind","leader of church of the holy light"}},{q="What is his relationship to Alonsus Faol?",a="Benedictus was the foremost pupil of the legendary Archbishop Alonsus Faol, who founded the Knights of the Silver Hand. Following Faol's death, Benedictus inherited the leadership of the Church to carry forward his mentor's work.",al={"faol student","alonsus faol benedictus"}},{q="What tasks does Benedictus oversee for adventurers?",a="Benedictus instructs Alliance heroes on missions against the Scourge, including sanctioning expeditions into Razorfen Downs to slay the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer. He also uses his holy power to cleanse powerful corrupted artifacts, such as the Cursed Eye of Paleth.",al={"benedictus quests","what does archbishop benedictus do"}},{q="What is his stance on the undead?",a="Benedictus views the undead as an unholy tragedy. While he preaches mercy, his followers interpret this as granting the restless dead—including the Forsaken and the Scourge—the mercy of a swift, final release through death.",al={"benedictus forsaken","benedictus views on scourge"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As the supreme shepherd of the Church of the Holy Light, Benedictus is the central figure overseeing the training, doctrines, and vows of all Alliance priests.",["faction:Alliance"]="Benedictus serves as the moral compass of Stormwind and the wider Alliance, providing spiritual solace to refugees and guiding high-ranking paladins and commanders."},kw={"alonsus faol","archbishop","benedictus","cathedral of light","church of the holy light","eye of paleth","priest","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:cathedral-of-light","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:light","zone:stormwind","quest:293","topic:varian-wrynn","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic"},src={"Archbishop Benedictus"}}
E["npc:brewmeister-bilger"] = {t="npc",n="Brewmeister Bilger",z="wetlands",s="Brewmeister Bilger is an intoxicated dwarven brewer residing in the cellar of the inn at Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once an upright, sober defender known as Bilger the Straight-laced, the passage of grueling years and the tragedies of Lordaeron have led him to trade his former discipline for the bottom of a barrel. Today, he whiles away his hours tasting potent spirits and waiting on deliveries from distant lands.",h="Brewmeister Bilger is an intoxicated dwarven brewer residing in the cellar of the inn at Southshore in the...",sec={{t="From the Light to the Barrel",b="Long before taking up the title of Brewmeister, Bilger was known across Southshore as Bilger the Straight-laced. Back during the height of the Knights of the Silver Hand and Lordaeron's proudest days, he carried himself with rigid, sober discipline among renowned figures in the town's tavern. The fall of Lordaeron, the Scourge plague, and the loss of so many comrades broke that stern resolve. Now, Bilger spends his days pacing the cool cellar beneath Southshore's inn, nursing hiccups and seeking out the strongest brews Azeroth can offer.",sp=0},{t="A Taste for Potent Imports",b="Despite his perpetual stupor, Bilger remains a discerning judge of spirits. He maintains an appetite for heavy dwarven moonshines and potent liquors crafted in the south, eagerly receiving special batches sent up the coast from distant ports like Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Brewmeister Bilger?",a="Brewmeister Bilger is located downstairs in the cellar of the inn at Southshore, the Alliance port town in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"bilger location","where is bilger","southshore cellar dwarf"}},{q="Why is he called 'Bilger the Straight-laced' in old stories?",a="Years ago, before the fall of Lordaeron, Bilger was a sober, strictly disciplined dwarf who associated with paladins and Alliance defenders in Southshore. The tragedies and wars that swept the region over the decades wore away his strict demeanor, leading him to abandon his old asceticism for heavy drinking.",al={"bilger the straight-laced","bilger history","bilger paladin"}},{q="What quests involve Brewmeister Bilger?",a="Bilger is the recipient of rare liquor delivered from the Wetlands, including strong spirits like MacKreel's Moonshine shipped north to Southshore.",al={"bilger quest","mackreel's moonshine quest"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Bilger shows that even the most stoic dwarf can be driven to excessive drinking by the grim horrors that fell upon the northern kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="Standing as a quiet relic of Southshore's past, Bilger watched the town shift from a staging post for heroes of the Alliance into a beleaguered frontier haven."},kw={"bilger","brewmeister bilger","hillsbrad foothills","inn cellar","mackreel","southshore"},rel={"subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","quest:647","topic:dwarf","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},src={"Brewmeister Bilger"}}
E["npc:captain-stoutfist"] = {t="npc",n="Captain Stoutfist",z="wetlands",s="Captain Stoutfist is the dwarven officer in charge of military defenses at Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. With the Dragonmaw clan pushing aggressively out of their marshland strongholds, Stoutfist coordinates defensive maneuvers and counter-offensives to ensure the vital Alliance port does not fall.",h="Captain Stoutfist is the dwarven officer in charge of military defenses at Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Defender of Menethil",b="Menethil Harbor serves as the principal deepwater port connecting Ironforge and Stormwind to the marshy lowlands of the Wetlands and the sea beyond. As the town's commanding officer, Captain Stoutfist bears the heavy burden of keeping its docks, civilian populace, and garrison secure against surrounding threats. The marshlands are notoriously hazardous, but the biggest peril to the settlement is an organized surge from renegade orcs.",sp=0},{t="The Dragonmaw Threat",b="The Dragonmaw clan, entrenched within the Wetlands since the Second War, has begun pushing their operations directly toward the roadways and passes. By infiltrating Dun Algaz, they threaten to sever the overland lifeline connecting Loch Modan and Ironforge to Menethil Harbor. Facing a severe shortage of troops, Captain Stoutfist relies on visiting Alliance volunteers recommended by Mountaineer Valstag Ironjaw to stem the tide.",sp=0},{t="Striking at Nek'rosh",b="Rather than waiting for a siege, Captain Stoutfist spearheads a aggressive campaign against the orc encampments. He directs allied forces to seize war banners near Whelgar's Excavation Site, sabotage Dragonmaw catapults preparing for an assault, and eliminate the clan's ruthless local chieftain, Nek'rosh Skullcrusher. By cutting down Nek'rosh, Stoutfist aims to break the spine of the orc offensive before Menethil Harbor is overwhelmed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Stoutfist?",a="Captain Stoutfist is the dwarf military commander tasked with defending Menethil Harbor. He coordinates garrison defenses, assesses regional threats, and recruits volunteers to push back enemies targeting the port.",al={"captain stoutfist","stoutfist menethil","menethil captain"}},{q="Where is Captain Stoutfist located?",a="He is stationed inside Menethil Harbor, the main Alliance hub on the western coast of the Wetlands.",al={"stoutfist location","where is captain stoutfist","find stoutfist"}},{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist need outside help?",a="The local garrison is stretched thin across the Wetlands. With Dragonmaw orcs seizing the mountain passes at Dun Algaz and encroaching on the town, Stoutfist lacks the regular manpower to launch offensive strikes and maintain harbor security simultaneously.",al={"why stoutfist need help","menethil defense problems"}},{q="Who is Nek'rosh Skullcrusher?",a="Nek'rosh Skullcrusher is the ruthless leader of the Dragonmaw orcs operating in the Wetlands. Captain Stoutfist orders his death to shatter the orcs' coordination and protect Menethil Harbor from an all-out assault.",al={"who is nekrosh","nekrosh skullcrusher","dragonmaw boss wetlands"}},{q="How does Dun Algaz connect to Captain Stoutfist's mission?",a="Dun Algaz is the vital mountain pass connecting Loch Modan and Ironforge to the Wetlands. When Dragonmaw orcs pushed into the pass, Mountaineer Valstag Ironjaw warned that Menethil was endangered, redirecting adventurers to Stoutfist to help reinforce the harbor.",al={"dun algaz stoutfist","algaz gauntlet connection"}},{q="What threat do the Dragonmaw catapults pose?",a="The Dragonmaw assembled siege weaponry to batter down fortifications and siege Menethil Harbor directly. Stoutfist directs champions to sabotage these catapults before they can be rolled into firing range.",al={"nekroshs gambit catapults","dragonmaw catapults"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Captain Stoutfist holds the line at one of the Alliance's most crucial maritime hubs, keeping naval routes open between Khaz Modan, Stormwind, and distant outposts.",["race:Dwarf"]="Stoutfist represents the rugged resolve of Ironforge's military, entrusted with safeguarding vital lowlands infrastructure far below the safety of the mountain peaks.",["class:Warrior"]="A no-nonsense dwarven tactician, Stoutfist values bold martial strikes over cautious fortification, putting warriors on the front line to dismantle enemy artillery and leadership."},kw={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw","dun algaz","dwarf","ironforge","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:474","quest:465","quest:464","quest:473","npc:valstag-ironjaw","subzone:dun-algaz","zone:wetlands"},src={"Captain Stoutfist"}}
E["npc:einar-stonegrip"] = {t="npc",n="Einar Stonegrip",z="wetlands",s="Einar Stonegrip is a dwarven trapper stationed along the main crossroads of the Wetlands. Rather than risk an uncomfortable reunion with his estranged wife in Menethil Harbor, he relies on passing adventurers to haul his crocolisk skins to town.",h="Einar Stonegrip is a dwarven trapper stationed along the main crossroads of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Trapper at the Crossroads",b="Perched at the central intersection connecting Dun Algaz, Dun Modr, and Menethil Harbor, Einar Stonegrip earns his living braving the sodden marshes of the Wetlands. He hunts the local crocolisks for their sturdy hides, supplying leatherworkers and merchants along the coast. Though rugged enough to wrestle reptiles out of the mire, he is thoroughly cowed by domestic strife. Embroiled in a bitter falling-out with his wife, Sida, Einar stays out on the road, hiring travelers to deliver his bundles of skins to his trading partner James Halloran rather than set foot in Menethil Harbor himself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Einar Stonegrip?",a="Einar Stonegrip is a dwarven skinner and hunter stationed at the crossroads in the Wetlands. He makes a living harvesting crocolisk hides to sell in Menethil Harbor.",al={"who is einar","einar stonegrip lore","wetlands dwarf crossroads"}},{q="Why won't Einar deliver his own goods to Menethil Harbor?",a="Einar is on terribly bad terms with his wife, Sida, who resides in Menethil Harbor. To avoid facing her wrath, he prefers to remain out in the swamplands and pay passing couriers to deliver his trade goods.",al={"why doesn't einar go to town","einar stonegrip wife","why hire adventurers"}},{q="Who does Einar work with in Menethil Harbor?",a="Einar gathers crocolisk skins on contract for James Halloran, a merchant in Menethil Harbor who handles the distribution and sale of leather goods.",al={"einar business partner","who buys einar skins","james halloran connection"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Einar reflects the rugged self-sufficiency common among dwarven mountaineers, even if his marital troubles drive him to sleep in the soggy marshes instead of a warm tavern.",["faction:Alliance"]="Travelers moving between Ironforge and Menethil Harbor often pass Einar's roadside post, providing easy courier work along the Alliance supply routes."},kw={"crocolisk","einar stonegrip","james halloran","menethil harbor","sida","skins","trapper","wetlands"},rel={"npc:james-halloran","npc:sida","quest:469","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:dwarf","subzone:dun-algaz","subzone:dun-modr"},src={"Einar Stonegrip"}}
E["npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons"] = {t="npc",n="First Mate Fitzsimmons",z="wetlands",s="First Mate Fitzsimmons is a ragged, reeking sailor who spends his days drinking outside the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Once the first mate aboard the Wave Mistress of the Kul Tiras Third Fleet, he is the sole known living survivor of the fleet's destruction during the Second War. Haunted by the tragedy, he seeks willing adventurers to face the restless spirits of his drowned comrades.",h="First Mate Fitzsimmons is a ragged, reeking sailor who spends his days drinking outside the Deepwater Tavern...",sec={{t="A Broken Sailor",b="Lounging outside the Deepwater Tavern amid the damp salt air of Menethil Harbor, First Mate Fitzsimmons is an easy man to overlook—or avoid entirely, given his unwashed stench. To most patrons, he is just another broken old salt drinking his memories away. Yet those willing to sit and listen will hear harrowing tales of a proud fleet brought low by fire and claw.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the Third Fleet",b="During the Second War, Fitzsimmons served as first mate aboard the Wave Mistress, part of the Kul Tiras Third Fleet dispatched to fight the Horde. Off the coast of the Wetlands, the fleet was ambushed and incinerated by enslaved red dragons flown by Dragonmaw orcs. The ships were shattered and sunk, leaving Fitzsimmons as the only man to drag himself ashore alive.",sp=0},{t="The Lingering Curse",b="Surviving the dragonfire did not bring Fitzsimmons peace. The remains of the ships, now remembered as the Lost Fleet, are haunted by his former crewmates, who rose as cursed undead unable to rest in their watery graves. Driven by guilt and terror, Fitzsimmons recruits travelers to put down the undead sailors and recover ancient relics that might finally lift the evil binding their souls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons?",a="He is an old Kul Tiran sailor and former first mate of the Wave Mistress. He survived the catastrophic sinking of Kul Tiras's Third Fleet during the Second War and now drinks his days away outside Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern.",al={"fitzsimmons lore","who is fitzsimmons","first mate fitzsimmons"}},{q="What happened to his ship?",a="The Wave Mistress and the rest of the Third Fleet were ambushed by enslaved red dragons ridden by the Dragonmaw clan during the Second War. The vessels were burned and broken upon the reef off the Wetlands coast.",al={"what happened to wave mistress","third fleet destruction","why did his ship sink"}},{q="Where is the Lost Fleet located?",a="The shattered hulls of the fleet lie submerged along the rocky coastline north of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, now guarded by murlocs and the restless spirits of drowned sailors.",al={"lost fleet location","where are the sunken ships","fitzsimmons ship location"}},{q="Why does he want adventurers to fight his old crew?",a="The drowned sailors of the Third Fleet rose as cursed, tormented undead rather than passing on. Fitzsimmons seeks brave travelers to put them to rest and retrieve the artifacts keeping their souls shackled.",al={"cursed crew quest lore","why kill his crew"}},{q="What is the Eye of Paleth?",a="It is an ancient, potent artifact carried aboard the Third Fleet. Its dark power is tied to the curse afflicting the sunken sailors, making its recovery crucial to granting the drowned fleet peace.",al={"eye of paleth","paleth relic"}},{q="Why does Fitzsimmons smell so bad?",a="Having lost everything when his fleet went down, Fitzsimmons has lived in drunken neglect outside the Deepwater Tavern for years, wearing sea-soaked rags and rarely washing.",al={"why does fitzsimmons smell","fitzsimmons stench"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Fitzsimmons represents a tragic chapter in Alliance naval history, reminding heroes of the catastrophic losses suffered against the Horde's enslaved dragon armada.",["race:Human"]="As a veteran of Kul Tiras, Fitzsimmons shares deep cultural ties with the seafaring human kingdom that sacrificed much to defend Lordaeron during the Second War."},kw={"deepwater tavern","eye of paleth","first mate fitzsimmons","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","lost fleet","menethil harbor","third fleet","wave mistress"},rel={"quest:288","quest:289","quest:290","quest:292","subzone:deepwater-tavern","subzone:lost-fleet","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:kul-tiras"},src={"First Mate Fitzsimmons"}}
E["npc:foggy-mackreel"] = {t="npc",n="Foggy MacKreel",z="wetlands",s="Foggy MacKreel is an intrepid dwarf stranded precariously on the ruined lower masonry of the Thandol Span. Despite the shattered stonework beneath his feet and the dizzying drop below, his only real concern is fulfilling his moonshine delivery north to Southshore.",h="Foggy MacKreel is an intrepid dwarf stranded precariously on the ruined lower masonry of the Thandol Span.",sec={{t="Stranded on the Span",b="Perched on the broken pylons beneath the shattered Thandol Span, Foggy MacKreel appears utterly unfazed by his perilous predicament. While Dark Iron sabotage and war damage have left the grand bridge between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands fractured, MacKreel treats his precarious footing as a minor inconvenience. His primary thought is not his rescue, but an undelivered batch of potent moonshine destined for the patrons of Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He readily hires passing adventurers nimble enough to reach his ledge to finish the courier run on his behalf.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foggy MacKreel?",a="Foggy MacKreel is an eccentric dwarven courier stranded on the ruined stone pillars underneath the broken bridge of the Thandol Span. Despite the drop, he remains completely calm and focused on getting his moonshine delivered.",al={"foggy mackreel","who is foggy","mackreel npc"}},{q="Where can I find Foggy MacKreel?",a="He is located on a stone platform midway down the broken central span of the Thandol Span, accessible by carefully jumping down from the bridge structure on the Arathi Highlands side.",al={"where is foggy mackreel","foggy mackreel location","how to find mackreel"}},{q="Why is Foggy MacKreel down there?",a="Foggy ended up stuck amid the wreckage of the Thandol Span during his travels. Yet instead of seeking rescue, his main concern is finding someone willing to carry his moonshine cargo the rest of the way to Southshore.",al={"why is foggy stranded","how did mackreel get there","why is he on the bridge"}},{q="What quest does Foggy MacKreel offer?",a="He offers 'MacKreel's Moonshine', asking travelers to deliver a jug of his potent brew to the tavern in Southshore across the Arathi Highlands.",al={"foggy quest","mackreel moonshine quest","what quest does foggy give"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="MacKreel embodies the stubborn grit—and peculiar priorities—of dwarven kind, valuing the timely delivery of strong liquor far above minor trifles like being marooned above a fatal chasm.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance couriers traveling between Ironforge and the northern outpost of Southshore often cross paths with Foggy, taking on his stranded cargo to help a fellow subject of the Alliance."},kw={"arathi","foggy","mackreel","moonshine","southshore","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:647","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:southshore","zone:arathi","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Foggy MacKreel"}}
E["npc:harlo-barnaby"] = {t="npc",n="Harlo Barnaby",z="wetlands",s="Harlo Barnaby is a wounded dwarven refugee residing in Menethil Harbor. Having barely escaped the slaughter when the Dark Iron clan seized Dun Modr, he now alerts travelers to the tragedy that unfolded in the northern marshes.",h="Harlo Barnaby is a wounded dwarven refugee residing in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="Escape from Dun Modr",b="Harlo Barnaby lived in Dun Modr until the northern stronghold fell to a sudden, savage assault by the Dark Iron dwarves. In the chaos of the ambush, Harlo fled south toward safety, only to catch a stray axe square in the back. Knocked unconscious by the blow, he somehow survived the trek across the marshland and awoke bandaged in Menethil Harbor. Though alive, his wounds and memories of the massacre leave him unable to return, prompting him to urge Alliance adventurers to investigate the smoking ruins of his former home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Harlo Barnaby?",a="Harlo Barnaby is an Ironforge dwarf living in Menethil Harbor who survived the brutal Dark Iron assault on the outpost of Dun Modr.",al={"harlo barnaby","who is harlo","menethil harbor dwarf"}},{q="How did Harlo Barnaby end up in Menethil Harbor?",a="While fleeing the invasion of Dun Modr, he was struck in the back by a thrown axe. He lost consciousness during his retreat and woke up safe in Menethil Harbor under the care of local healers.",al={"how did harlo get here","harlo barnaby back injury"}},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr was overrun and devastated by hostile Dark Iron dwarves pushing south from the Thandol Span, wiping out the local dwarven defenders and driving survivors into the wetlands.",al={"dun modr fall","what happened at dun modr"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Harlo represents a living reminder of the persistent and bloody clan war against the treacherous Dark Irons who seek to sever Khaz Modan from the north.",["faction:Alliance"]="The fall of Dun Modr threatens the critical land bridge between the marshlands and Arathi, making Harlo's warnings essential for Alliance forces."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","harlo barnaby","menethil harbor","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:dun-modr","quest:472","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Harlo Barnaby"}}
E["npc:james-halloran"] = {t="npc",n="James Halloran",z="wetlands",s="James Halloran is a human tanner working out of the Wetlands to supply fine hides across the eastern continents. Based in Menethil Harbor, he makes a living harvesting the tough, prized skins of the region's native crocolisks. He relies on passing travelers and nearby trade channels to gather raw materials and transport his finished leathers to market.",h="James Halloran is a human tanner working out of the Wetlands to supply fine hides across the eastern...",sec={{t="A Tanner in the Marshes",b="From his home in Menethil Harbor, James Halloran makes his living from the marshland just outside town. As an enterprising tanner, Halloran recognized that the perilous bogs offer a lucrative commodity: crocolisk skins. Transforming the rugged hide of marsh reptiles into high-quality leather requires rare craftsmanship, and Halloran's finished goods are shipped out through local trade channels to buyers all across Azeroth.",sp=0},{t="Hides, Apprentices, and Daily Trade",b="Operating so close to the marsh comes with constant danger. Halloran cannot easily hunt every beast himself while tending to curing vats and trade logistics. He frequently hires hardy travelers to handle the rougher chores of skinning young marsh beasts and managing routine deliveries between his work site and surrounding settlements, ensuring his bustling leather craft stays fully supplied.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a human tanner based in Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. He specializes in hunting and skinning the region's indigenous crocolisks, curing their tough hides into leather goods that are exported across the world.",al={"james halloran","halloran","who is halloran","wetlands tanner"}},{q="Where does James Halloran sell his leather?",a="Halloran processes raw crocolisk skins into fine leathers and ships them throughout Azeroth. He relies heavily on the maritime trade passing through Menethil Harbor to distribute his wares across the seas.",al={"halloran leather trade","where do crocolisk skins go","halloran business"}},{q="Why does Halloran need adventurers to collect young crocolisk skins?",a="Curing and tanning leather is time-consuming, labor-intensive work. Halloran employs traveling adventurers to cull the local marsh crocolisks and strip their hides so that he has a steady supply of raw material without abandoning his workshop.",al={"why kill young crocolisks","young crocolisk skins quest","crocolisk hides halloran"}},{q="What is Halloran's connection to Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor serves as the primary trade and supply hub for the region. Halloran relies on the harbor and its shipping lanes to export his cured hides to distant markets and keep his tanning business viable.",al={"halloran menethil","halloran port connection","does halloran live in menethil"}},{q="Where can James Halloran be found?",a="Halloran lives and works in Menethil Harbor, the busy port on the western coast of the Wetlands, with the crocolisk marshes right outside town.",al={"halloran location","where is james halloran","find halloran"}},{q="Does Halloran have an apprentice?",a="Yes, Halloran relies on help to manage the trade, tasking apprentices and traveling couriers with daily chores, errands, and delivery runs between his post and nearby settlements.",al={"halloran apprentice","apprentice duties halloran","who works for halloran"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Halloran's trade helps sustain the commercial presence of the Alliance in the rugged Wetlands, supplying valuable crafted leather to towns across the kingdom.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters navigating the sodden marshes will find common ground with Halloran, whose livelihood depends on stalking and harvesting the wetlands' aggressive reptilian predators."},kw={"crocolisk","halloran","james halloran","leatherworking","menethil harbor","swiftgear station","tanner","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","quest:484","quest:469","quest:471"},src={"James Halloran"}}
E["npc:longbraid-the-grim"] = {t="npc",n="Longbraid the Grim",z="wetlands",s="Longbraid the Grim is an Ironforge dwarf commander stationed just outside the fallen fortress of Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands. Mourning the loss of his brother and the overrun of the Thandol Span, he coordinates the surviving dwarf forces against the invading Dark Iron clan.",h="Longbraid the Grim is an Ironforge dwarf commander stationed just outside the fallen fortress of Dun Modr in...",sec={{t="A Bitter Watch",b="Positioned within sight of the bridge to the Arathi Highlands, Longbraid the Grim rallies what remains of the dwarven garrison after the Dark Iron clan seized Dun Modr. The sudden assault devastated the regional defenders and resulted in the death of Longbraid's own brother during the siege of the Thandol Span. Burdened by grief and hatred, Longbraid refuses to abandon the northern boundary, directing travelers and surviving mountaineers in surgical strikes to curb the Dark Iron advance.",sp=0},{t="Holding the Line",b="Beyond defending the approach to the bridge, Longbraid oversees broader dwarven operations across the Wetlands. He dispatched vital soldiers to escort Prospector Whelgar into the marshlands and works relentlessly to reclaim the lost fortifications of Dun Modr, vowing retribution against the Dark Iron saboteurs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Longbraid the Grim?",a="Longbraid the Grim is a dwarven commander stationed outside Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands. He leads the local Alliance resistance against the Dark Iron dwarfs who overran the area.",al={"who is longbraid","longbraid identity","dun modr dwarf"}},{q="Why is Longbraid called 'the Grim'?",a="He earned his grim demeanor after his brother was killed during the devastating Dark Iron attack on the Thandol Span. Ever since, he has been consumed by the drive to avenge his fallen kin.",al={"why is he grim","longbraid brother","longbraid backstory"}},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr was overrun and occupied by the Dark Iron clan, who ambushed the dwarven garrison and attempted to sever the Thandol Span, cutting off the main route between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands.",al={"fall of dun modr","what happened to the bridge","thandol span attack"}},{q="What is Longbraid's connection to Prospector Whelgar?",a="Longbraid assigned soldiers from his forces to accompany and protect Prospector Whelgar as the dwarven excavation team delved deeper into the hazardous Wetlands.",al={"whelgar longbraid","merrin letter"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, Longbraid embodies the fierce, enduring blood feud against their treacherous Dark Iron cousins who struck directly at their northern gateway.",["faction:Alliance"]="Longbraid holds the thin line guarding the northern gate of Khaz Modan, fighting to reopen the crucial land route across the Thandol Span into Arathi."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","longbraid","thandol span","the grim","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","topic:dark-iron-clan","quest:472","quest:304","quest:378","npc:prospector-whelgar","zone:wetlands"},src={"Longbraid the Grim"}}
E["npc:merrin-rockweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Merrin Rockweaver",z="wetlands",s="Merrin Rockweaver is a dwarven researcher representing the Explorers' League in the Wetlands. Following a violent raptor infestation that overran Whelgar's Excavation Site, she took refuge nearby alongside Prospector Whelgar at his makeshift retreat.",h="Merrin Rockweaver is a dwarven researcher representing the Explorers' League in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Displaced by the Dig",b="Merrin Rockweaver traveled to the Wetlands on behalf of the Ironforge Explorers' League to unearth ancient Titan secrets buried beneath the muck. The expedition ended in disaster when pickaxes pierced subterranean raptor nests beneath the dig. Vicious prehistoric beasts swarmed the trenches, forcing Merrin and the surviving crew to abandon their equipment, notes, and progress. She now shelters at Whelgar's Retreat, an encampment perched on the bluffs overlooking the overrun ruins.",sp=0},{t="Salvaging the Operation",b="Despite the retreat, Merrin refuses to let the expedition become an outright failure. While Prospector Whelgar plots vengeance against the beasts and searches for missing comrades, Merrin focuses on retrieving the lost expedition tools and precious archaeological findings left behind in the raptor-infested trenches. She relies on passing Alliance travelers willing to brave the talons below to bring back what remains of their work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin Rockweaver is a dwarf archaeologist affiliated with the Explorers' League of Ironforge. She was stationed at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands before raptors overran the operation.",al={"merrin rockweaver lore","who is merrin","wetlands dwarf merrin"}},{q="Why is she staying at Whelgar's Retreat?",a="The main dig site below was ambushed by subterranean Mottled raptors disturbed by the miners. Merrin and the survivors fled up to the nearby bluff, establishing Whelgar's Retreat as a safe haven while trying to recover their supplies.",al={"why is merrin at the retreat","whelgars retreat merrin","what happened to her camp"}},{q="What does Merrin need help with?",a="Merrin needs brave travelers to descend into the perilous dig site, retrieve the specialized mining and excavation tools abandoned during the panic, and help locate missing members of the expedition.",al={"merrin quests","merrin rockweaver tasks","tooling around lore"}},{q="What was the expedition trying to find?",a="Like most Explorers' League operations, the Wetlands dig was commissioned to uncover ancient artifacts related to dwarven ancestry and the mysterious Titan relics hidden throughout Khaz Modan.",al={"what are they digging for","excavation site purpose"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarven adventurers, aiding Merrin is a matter of national heritage, safeguarding the precious Titan relics and historical records that the Explorers' League risked their lives to uncover.",["faction:Alliance"]="Merrin represents Ironforge's academic presence in the Wetlands, and securing her research helps maintain the Alliance's tenuous foothold in the wild marshland."},kw={"explorers' league","merrin rockweaver","raptors","tooling around","wetlands","whelgar's excavation site","whelgar's retreat"},rel={"subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","topic:explorers-league","quest:305","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Merrin Rockweaver"}}
E["npc:ormer-ironbraid"] = {t="npc",n="Ormer Ironbraid",z="wetlands",s="Ormer Ironbraid is a dwarven archaeologist stationed at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the southern Wetlands. His team's historical research has been violently interrupted by ravenous raptors that overran the dig. Ormer seeks adventurous allies to clear out the beasts and avenge the miners driven from the site.",h="Ormer Ironbraid is a dwarven archaeologist stationed at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the southern Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Dig Derailed",b="Ormer Ironbraid arrived in the Wetlands as part of the dwarven effort to uncover Titan relics and ancient history at Whelgar's Excavation Site. Unfortunately, uncovering ancient stones also unearthed—or at least provoked—packs of fierce Wetlands raptors. Rather than cataloging ancient earthenware and tablets, Ormer spends his days watching the beasts prowl among the ruins, nursing a fierce hatred for the creatures that disrupted their work.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Feud with Claws",b="Ormer refuses to abandon the dig, but he lacks the raw muscle to purge the site alone. He directs his frustration into a systematic campaign of extermination, enlisting passing travelers to slay raptors of increasing size and ferocity. For Ormer, reclaiming the excavation is not just about the artifacts—it is a deeply personal matter of dwarven pride and vengeance against the local wildlife.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ormer Ironbraid?",a="Ormer Ironbraid is a dwarven researcher overseeing work at Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands. He represents the Explorers' League's interests in studying the ancient ruins buried in the marsh.",al={"who is ormer","ormer ironbraid","ormer wetlands"}},{q="Where can I find Ormer Ironbraid?",a="He can be found standing on the overlook above Whelgar's Excavation Site, located in the southern cliffs of the Wetlands, just east of the main road heading toward Loch Modan.",al={"ormer location","where is ormer","find ormer ironbraid"}},{q="Why does Ormer hate raptors so much?",a="The local raptor packs overran the excavation site, driving out the dwarven workers and halting all archaeological progress. Ormer took the disruption as a personal insult and seeks total payback.",al={"why raptors","ormer raptors","ormers revenge lore"}},{q="What is Whelgar's Excavation Site?",a="It is an archaeological dig site founded by Ironforge dwarves to unearth ancient Titan and earthen ruins beneath the Wetlands. However, aggressive wildlife has turned the dig into a dangerous battleground.",al={"whelgars excavation site","what is this dig site","wetlands dig site"}},{q="What quests does Ormer offer?",a="Ormer offers the three-part 'Ormer's Revenge' quest chain, tasking adventurers with culling ever-larger raptors in the excavation site.",al={"ormer quests","strike the earth","ormers revenge quest"}},{q="Is Ormer affiliated with the Explorers' League?",a="Yes. Like many dwarves excavating ancient ruins across Khaz Modan, Ormer operates on behalf of the Ironforge archaeological efforts dedicated to uncovering their race's Titan heritage.",al={"ormer explorers league","is ormer an archaeologist"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Ormer embodies dwarven tenacity—refusing to yield ancient ancestral grounds to a pack of overgrown lizards.",["faction:Alliance"]="Assisting Ormer secures the southern Wetlands road and aids Ironforge's vital archaeological endeavors.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters will find Ormer's request a familiar task, pitting their tracking and beast-slaying prowess against some of the fiercest raptors in Khaz Modan."},kw={"dwarf","excavation","explorers league","ironbraid","ormer","raptors","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","quest:294","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Ormer Ironbraid"}}
E["npc:prospector-whelgar"] = {t="npc",n="Prospector Whelgar",z="wetlands",s="Prospector Whelgar is a dwarven archaeologist stationed at an excavation site in the eastern hills of the Wetlands. His mission to uncover titan relics has stalled after vicious raptors overran the dig. He now seeks hardy adventurers willing to brave the beasts to recover ancient artifacts.",h="Prospector Whelgar is a dwarven archaeologist stationed at an excavation site in the eastern hills of the...",sec={{t="A Dig Under Siege",b="Sent into the marshy wilderness of the Wetlands to unearth the history of the dwarven race, Prospector Whelgar established an archaeological camp known as Whelgar's Excavation Site. The valley was once rich with ancient stone relics, but the local raptors quickly grew territorial and drove his team into hiding. Despite the danger, Whelgar refuses to abandon his duty. He remains focused on recovering valuable relics—including the enigmatic Goaz Stone—before wild predators or rival scoundrels ruin the site entirely.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Prospector Whelgar?",a="Prospector Whelgar is an Ironforge dwarf archaeologist tasked with leading an expedition in the Wetlands. He oversees the dig site in the eastern mountains, studying relics from the dawn of dwarven history.",al={"whelgar","who is whelgar","prospector whelgar lore"}},{q="Where can I find Prospector Whelgar?",a="He is located in the eastern reaches of the Wetlands, nestled in the rocky outcroppings of Whelgar's Excavation Site, just north of the road leading toward Dun Algaz.",al={"whelgar location","where is whelgar","whelgar wetlands map"}},{q="Why is Whelgar having trouble at the dig site?",a="Fierce native raptors have completely overrun the dig site, killing or scattering his crew and forcing Whelgar into a defensive pocket. He cannot continue unearthing relics without outside protection.",al={"raptors excavation","what happened to whelgar dig","whelgars excavation raptors"}},{q="What is the Goaz Stone?",a="The Goaz Stone is an ancient artifact uncovered among the ruins at the excavation site. Whelgar works to translate its inscriptions to better understand the forgotten origins and ancient history of the dwarven people.",al={"goaz stone","what is the goaz stone","uncovering the past relic"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Whelgar's mission directly serves the Explorers' League and King Magni Bronzebeard's ongoing search into the titan roots of the dwarven race.",["profession:Mining"]="The craggy ridges around Whelgar's dig site contain rich mineral veins, though prospectors must contend with the same raptors plaguing Whelgar's team."},kw={"dwarf","excavation site","explorers league","goaz stone","prospector whelgar","uncovering the past","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site","quest:299","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf","quest:463"},src={"Prospector Whelgar"}}
E["npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden"] = {t="npc",n="Rethiel the Greenwarden",z="wetlands",s="Rethiel the Greenwarden is an ancient, sentient bog beast residing in Greenwarden's Grove within the Wetlands. Deeply attuned to the natural balance of the marsh, he watches over the land and enlists travelers to cull threats that disrupt its harmony.",h="Rethiel the Greenwarden is an ancient, sentient bog beast residing in Greenwarden's Grove within the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Marsh",b="Standing amidst the damp thickets of Greenwarden's Grove, Rethiel is a towering creature of moss, peat, and primal plant life. While many bog beasts in the marshlands wander aimlessly as aggressive predators, Rethiel possesses a rare, conscious awareness and a sorrowful voice. He perceives the wetlands not merely as murky terrain, but as a living ecosystem that currently cries out under the weight of foreign predation and corruption.",sp=0},{t="Tending the Wounds",b="Rethiel seeks to alleviate the suffering of the Wetlands by dispatching sympathetic adventurers against its major agitators. He urges visitors to hunt down destructive Mosshide gnolls who ravage the wildlife, quench the unnatural fires stoked by Dragonmaw orc encampments, and thin out the bloated, rotting oozes that seep poison into the marsh waters. Through these cullings, he hopes to restore peace to the wounded soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is a sentient bog beast residing at Greenwarden's Grove in the Wetlands. Unlike the mindless creatures of his kind, he can communicate with mortals and acts as a protector of the marsh.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel lore","bog beast npc wetlands"}},{q="Where can I find Rethiel?",a="He can be found at Greenwarden's Grove, situated along the road in the eastern portion of the Wetlands, east of the main marsh crossroads and west of Dun Algaz.",al={"rethiel location","where is rethiel","greenwardens grove location"}},{q="Why does Rethiel want travelers to help him?",a="Rethiel senses that the marsh is actively suffering. He seeks adventurers to purge invasive threats—specifically destructive gnoll bands, unnatural Dragonmaw fire-users, and toxic oozes—to bring relief to the land.",al={"why rethiel gives quests","rethiel goal","what does rethiel want"}},{q="Are all bog beasts sentient like Rethiel?",a="Most bog beasts encountered across Azeroth act on raw, hostile instinct and lack higher intellect. Rethiel is an exceptional creature whose deep natural attunement grants him sapience and speech.",al={"can bog beasts talk","intelligent bog beasts","why can rethiel speak"}},{q="What threats does Rethiel focus on?",a="He focuses on curbing the aggressive Mosshide gnolls, extinguishing the flames of the hostile Dragonmaw orcs, and purging the foul oozes festering in the marsh.",al={"rethiel quests","rethiel enemies","threats to wetlands rethiel"}},{q="Is Rethiel aligned with the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Rethiel is friendly to the Alliance and hostile to the Horde. He is concerned with the welfare of the land and entreats Alliance travelers willing to mend the marsh.",al={"is rethiel alliance","rethiel faction","can horde talk to rethiel"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Rethiel represents an unusual expression of Azeroth's wild balance, speaking directly for a wounded ecosystem much like the ancient protectors of Kalimdor.",["class:Shaman"]="Attuned to the elemental and physical disharmony of the marsh, Rethiel echoes the distress of the land itself as it groans under contamination and fire."},kw={"bog beast","dragonmaw","greenwarden","greenwarden's grove","mosshide","nature","rethiel","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","quest:463","quest:275","quest:276","quest:277"},src={"Rethiel the Greenwarden"}}
E["npc:sida"] = {t="npc",n="Sida",z="wetlands",s="Sida is a dwarven resident of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Known for her estranged marriage to Einar Stonegrip, she spends her days in the port town while dealing with personal misadventures out in the surrounding marshes.",h="Sida is a dwarven resident of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Harbor Resident",b="Sida resides in the bustling Alliance port of Menethil Harbor, living apart from her husband, Einar Stonegrip. Their relationship is strained enough that Einar flatly refuses to travel to Menethil so long as Sida remains in town. Despite keeping to the coastal settlement, Sida occasionally ventures out into the dangers of the Wetlands, having recently suffered the misfortune of losing her personal bag during an expedition out toward Ironbeard's Tomb.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sida?",a="Sida is a dwarven woman living in Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. She gives tasks to adventurers who pass through the port.",al={"who is sida","sida npc","sida wetlands"}},{q="What happened to Sida's bag?",a="Sida lost her bag while visiting Ironbeard's Tomb, an ancient burial site nestled in the Wetlands. The area has since been overrun by foul oozes that swallowed up her belongings.",al={"where is sida's bag","lost bag","ironbeard tomb bag"}},{q="Why won't Einar Stonegrip visit Menethil Harbor?",a="Einar Stonegrip is Sida's estranged husband. Due to bad blood between them, Einar avoids Menethil Harbor entirely as long as Sida is still living there.",al={"einar and sida","sida husband","einar stonegrip drama"}},{q="Where can Sida be found?",a="Sida can be found strolling the docks and roads within Menethil Harbor on the western coast of the Wetlands.",al={"sida location","where is sida"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Sida represents everyday dwarven town life in Menethil Harbor, caught between domestic disputes and the treacherous wilderness just beyond the town gates.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers arriving on the docks of Menethil Harbor, Sida offers local errands that take adventurers inland toward Ironbeard's Tomb."},kw={"einar stonegrip","ironbeard's tomb","menethil harbor","ooze","sida","wetlands"},rel={"npc:einar-stonegrip","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb","quest:470","quest:469","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Sida"}}
E["npc:tarrel-rockweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Tarrel Rockweaver",z="wetlands",s="Tarrel Rockweaver is an anxious dwarven husband stationed on the bridge leading into Menethil Harbor. Deeply worried for his wife Merrin, an archaeologist who ventured inland with Whelgar's excavation team, he watches the road hoping for news of her safety.",h="Tarrel Rockweaver is an anxious dwarven husband stationed on the bridge leading into Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Watch on the Bridge",b="While trade and military shipments flow through Menethil Harbor, Tarrel Rockweaver keeps an anxious vigil at the bridge on the edge of town. His wife, Merrin Rockweaver, joined Prospector Whelgar's prestigious archaeological expedition deeper into the Wetlands. When violent raptors overran the excavation site and cut off regular communication, Tarrel was left stranded in town, begging passing travelers to scout east toward Whelgar's Retreat to ensure she survived the disaster.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarrel Rockweaver?",a="Tarrel is an Ironforge dwarf currently lingering near the entrance bridge of Menethil Harbor. He is waiting desperately for word regarding his wife, Merrin, who left on an inland dig.",al={"tarrel rockweaver","who is this dwarf","menethil bridge dwarf"}},{q="Why is Tarrel asking travelers for help?",a="He lost contact with his wife Merrin after her archaeological team encountered danger at their dig site. Unable to leave his post, he asks passing adventurers to head east toward Whelgar's Retreat to find her.",al={"tarrel quest","in search of the excavation team","tarrel rockweaver mission"}},{q="Who is Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin Rockweaver is Tarrel's wife and an archaeologist attached to Prospector Whelgar's excavation team. She survived an attack on their camp and took refuge with the survivors at Whelgar's Retreat.",al={"merrin rockweaver","tarrel wife","who is merrin"},sp=1},{q="Where did Tarrel's wife go?",a="Merrin traveled eastward into the Wetlands to study ancient titan and dwarven relics. After their main dig site was attacked, she and the surviving excavators fell back to a ridge known as Whelgar's Retreat.",al={"where is merrin","excavation team location","whelgar's retreat"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Tarrel's concern highlights the perilous cost of the Explorer's League's relentless drive to unearth dwarven origins across the wild frontiers of Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="For travelers arriving at Menethil's port, Tarrel offers an immediate connection to the hardships facing Alliance citizens stationed along the untamed marshes."},kw={"dwarf","excavation team","menethil harbor","merrin rockweaver","tarrel rockweaver","wetlands","whelgar's retreat"},rel={"npc:merrin-rockweaver","quest:305","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Tarrel Rockweaver"}}
E["npc:veronica-nials"] = {t="npc",n="Veronica Nials",z="wetlands",s="Captain Veronica Nials is an officer of the Stromgarde military stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands. Amid the kingdom's collapse, she coordinates defensive operations against the Syndicate and ogres that overrun the fallen capital.",h="Captain Veronica Nials is an officer of the Stromgarde military stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi...",sec={{t="Defender of a Broken Realm",b="Following the Third War, the human kingdom of Stromgarde shattered, leaving its remnants struggling to survive against invading Boulderfist ogres and the treachery of the Syndicate. Captain Veronica Nials stands as one of the central commanders of the surviving Stromgarde defenders at Refuge Pointe. Tasked with holding the line, she directs Alliance champions against key Syndicate leadership, such as Lord Falconcrest and the warlock Marez Cowl, while striving to recover fallen soldiers' badges so their grieving families can find closure.",sp=0},{t="A Plea Denied",b="Captain Nials's loyalties are strictly tied to her battered homeland. When Rhag Garmason and the dwarven defenders of Dun Modr begged for Stromgarde's assistance after Dark Iron saboteurs devastated the Thandol Span, Nials was forced to turn them away. Bound by honor and duty, her troops cannot spare a single blade beyond the Arathi Highlands while their own ancestral kingdom remains occupied.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Veronica Nials?",a="Veronica Nials is a human captain of the Stromgarde army. She is stationed at Refuge Pointe, directing the military resistance against Syndicate infiltrators and ogres occupying the Arathi Highlands.",al={"who is veronica nials","captain nials","refuge pointe captain"}},{q="Why won't Captain Nials help Dun Modr and the Thandol Span?",a="Although the dwarves holding the Thandol Span desperately need reinforcements against the Dark Iron Clan, Nials cannot spare any soldiers. Stromgarde is on the brink of total destruction, and duty obligates her forces to remain focused entirely on reclaiming their own fallen kingdom.",al={"thandol span plea","why no help for dwarfs","plea to the alliance quest"}},{q="What does Nials do with Stromgarde badges?",a="The Syndicate offers bounties for Stromgarde badges taken from slaughtered soldiers. Nials asks Alliance adventurers to retrieve these stolen badges from Syndicate cutthroats so she can confirm the deaths and notify the fallen defenders' families.",al={"stromgarde badges","why collect badges","badges quest"}},{q="What is Nials's connection to the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Brother Joseph of the Scarlet Crusade attempts to correspond with her, sending letters urging her and Stromgarde's remnants to support their cause, though Captain Nials has little interest in answering the zealots.",al={"scarlet monastery letter","crusader joseph letter"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Captain Nials represents the tragic reality of the northern Alliance: fractured, isolated kingdoms struggling for basic survival while unable to offer meaningful aid to neighboring allies.",["race:Human"]="For humans, Nials is an emblem of Stromgarde's enduring martial pride, refusing to abandon the ancestral realm of Arathor despite devastating odds."},kw={"arathi highlands","falconcrest","marez cowl","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate","thandol span","veronica nials"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","quest:634","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-modr","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance","zone:scarlet"},src={"Veronica Nials"}}
E["quest:274"] = {t="quest",n="A Dark Threat Looms",z="wetlands",s="Following the discovery of suspicious powder at the Stonewrought Dam, Ashlan Stonesmirk in Dun Modr identifies the substance as unstable Seaforium. Capable of catastrophic destruction if it comes into contact with water, the powder poses an immediate danger to the region and the nearby dwarven realm. Stonesmirk concocts a disarming colloid and sends word back to Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII to defuse the disaster.",h="Following the discovery of suspicious powder at the Stonewrought Dam, Ashlan Stonesmirk in Dun Modr...",sec={{t="A Volatile Discovery",b="Examining the samples brought from the Stonewrought Dam, Ashlan Stonesmirk immediately recognizes the telltale silver crystals and distinct odor of Seaforium. While inert in dry conditions, Seaforium reacts violently with moisture—a terrifying reality for a dam holding back the waters of Loch Modan. Ashlan warns that an unchecked explosion from such a compound could blow Ironforge out of the mountain.",sp=0},{t="Racing the Clock",b="To counteract the volatile explosive, Stonesmirk concocts a specialized disarming colloid. Neutralizing the reaction requires a specific chemical mixture: the colloid combined with marsh lurker venom, crushed Mo'Grosh crystal, and the tear of a crocolisk. Time is short, and Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII must be warned immediately before moisture triggers the disaster.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of explosive was found in the Wetlands?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk identifies the mystery substance as Seaforium powder, marked by distinct silver crystals and a pungent chemical smell.",al={"what powder is this","what is the powder","seaforium powder"}},{q="Why is Seaforium so dangerous here?",a="Seaforium is relatively harmless while kept dry, but it triggers a catastrophic explosion when exposed to water—making the Stonewrought Dam, holding back the waters of Loch Modan, an extraordinarily hazardous place for it.",al={"why is seaforium dangerous","what makes seaforium explode"}},{q="Who is Ashlan Stonesmirk?",a="Ashlan Stonesmirk is an Alliance dwarven specialist residing in the Wetlands who possesses the engineering and chemical expertise necessary to analyze mysterious powders and craft neutralizers.",al={"who is ashlan","ashlan stonesmirk identity"}},{q="Who is Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII?",a="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII oversees engineering and defense concerns in the region, operating out of the Stonewrought Dam in Loch Modan to maintain and safeguard dwarven infrastructure.",al={"who is hinderweir","chief engineer hinderweir"}},{q="How can the Seaforium be neutralized?",a="Defusing the chemical reaction requires combining Ashlan's disarming colloid with three rare local ingredients: marsh lurker venom, a crushed Mo'Grosh crystal, and a crocolisk tear.",al={"how to defuse seaforium","seaforium defusal recipe","disarming colloid recipe"}},{q="What is the danger to Ironforge?",a="Ashlan warns that an uncontrolled detonation of the explosive in the surrounding mountain systems could cause devastating seismic failure capable of blowing Ironforge right out of the mountain.",al={"is ironforge in danger","how is ironforge threatened"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers will recognize Seaforium as an extremely potent volatile compound, demanding delicate handling and precise chemical countermeasures to avoid massive shockwaves.",["race:Dwarf"]="For the dwarves of Khaz Modan, the thought of explosive saboteurs wielding volatile Seaforium near the gateway to Dun Morogh and Ironforge is an existential threat.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance defenders must act quickly to assist Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII and secure the lowlands before enemy saboteurs shatter strategic infrastructure."},kw={"ashlan stonesmirk","blast powder","chief engineer hinderweir vii","dark threat looms","disarming colloid","ironforge","seaforium","wetlands"},rel={"npc:ashlan-stonesmirk","npc:chief-engineer-hinderweir-vii","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Ashlan Stonesmirk",["end"]="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=274},src={"A Dark Threat Looms (4)"}}
E["quest:275"] = {t="quest",n="Blisters on The Land",z="wetlands",s="Blisters on The Land is an Alliance quest offered by Rethiel the Greenwarden along the eastern ridges of the Wetlands. Sensing an unnatural sickness stirring the swamp, the lone bog beast warden tasks travelers with culling the diseased Fen Creepers that stalk the waterways. Putting these shambling plant horrors to rest is Rethiel's attempt to break the swamp's rising fever.",h="Blisters on The Land is an Alliance quest offered by Rethiel the Greenwarden along the eastern ridges of the...",sec={{t="A Festering Marshes",b="From his grove amid the marshes, Rethiel the Greenwarden watches over the soggy expanse of the Wetlands. The marshes have never been gentle, but recently an unnatural sickness has begun to spread through the mire. Rethiel perceives this affliction as a growing fever in the earth itself, one that causes wild nature to warp into mindless, shambling monstrosities.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Fen",b="The primary symptom of this rot is the rise of Fen Creepers—decaying elemental masses of swamp vegetation that shamble along the waterways. Rethiel describes them as diseased blisters swelling upon the surface of the land. Because their tormented existence only spreads agitation through the marsh, the Greenwarden charges passing allies with destroying them so their tangled remnants can settle harmlessly back into the mud.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden is a bog beast residing at the Greenwarden's Grove in the eastern Wetlands. He dedicates himself to tending the natural balance of the marshlands, seeking to soothe the land's afflictions and curb corrupted elemental growths.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel greenwarden lore","who gives blisters on the land"}},{q="What are Fen Creepers?",a="Fen Creepers are hostile plant and bog elementals that wander the waterways of the Wetlands. They appear as hulking, shambling masses of animated vines, mud, and decaying marsh flora.",al={"fen creepers","what is a fen creeper","creepers wetlands"}},{q="Why does Rethiel want the Fen Creepers destroyed?",a="Rethiel views the Fen Creepers as fevered, diseased manifestations of the marsh's growing sickness. He believes that destroying them allows their form to dissolve and settle back into the earth, soothing the agitated land.",al={"why kill fen creepers","why blisters on the land"}},{q="What causes the festering in the Wetlands?",a="Rethiel admits he does not fully know what is causing the festering to grow within the Wetlands. He simply senses the land's weeping distress and treats the symptoms by calming elemental unrest wherever it surges.",al={"why are wetlands diseased","cause of wetland sickness"}},{q="Where are Fen Creepers found in the Wetlands?",a="Fen Creepers roam along the damp waterways, muddy banks, and central channels crisscrossing the Wetlands, particularly near the deeper bogs west of the Greenwarden's Grove.",al={"fen creeper locations","where to find fen creepers"}},{q="Does this quest connect to other tasks for Rethiel?",a="Yes. Blisters on The Land follows Rethiel's concerns regarding the Mosshide gnolls burning the Wetlands' trees in Fire Taboo, serving as part of his ongoing efforts to protect the balance of the marsh.",al={"greenwarden questline","rethiel quests"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Rethiel's mission directly reflects the druidic duty to heal the natural world, purging agitated elemental blights so the earth can return to balance.",["race:NightElf"]="Finding a solitary bog beast warden allied with Stormwind in the Eastern Kingdoms shows that even the land's own spirits will seek help to nurture wounded land.",["class:Shaman"]="The Fen Creepers represent twisted manifestations of earth and water, making their destruction an act of pacifying discordant elemental spirits."},kw={"blisters on the land","fen creepers","greenwarden","marshes","rethiel","wetland bogs","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:277","quest:463","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=275},src={"Blisters on The Land"}}
E["quest:276"] = {t="quest",n="Tramping Paws",z="wetlands",s="Tramping Paws is an Alliance task given by Rethiel the Greenwarden at the Greenwarden's Grove in the Wetlands. Troubled by the surging Mosshide gnoll population near the Gate of Algaz, the bog beast protector tasks adventurers with culling their numbers before their fires and trampling paws ruin the bog.",h="Tramping Paws is an Alliance task given by Rethiel the Greenwarden at the Greenwarden's Grove in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Swelling Fen Menace",b="For many years, the Mosshide gnolls inhabited the Wetlands without utterly overwhelming its natural order. Lately, however, their pack numbers have exploded south toward the pass of Dun Algaz. Their heavy boots and pawprints trample rare fen flora, and their crude logging strips vital groves to feed their campsite blazes. Left unchecked, the burgeoning packs threaten to degrade the fragile marsh ecology.",sp=0},{t="The Greenwarden's Judgment",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden watches over the marsh with an eye for balance rather than civilization. To the Greenwarden, the issue is not that gnolls exist, but that their runaway population outstrips what the Wetlands can support. By driving Mosshide gnolls and mongrels back into manageable numbers, adventurers help preserve the wetlands and earn the reluctant approval of an ancient wilderness guardian.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is a bog beast dwelling in the Wetlands along the road between Ironforge's borders and Arathi. Dedicated to preserving the marsh, she monitors the land's health and tasks travelers with keeping destructive populations in check.",al={"rethiel lore","who gives tramping paws","greenwarden wetlands"}},{q="Why are the Mosshide gnolls a problem now?",a="While the Mosshide pack once coexisted with the marsh without causing long-term harm, their recent population boom has led to heavy deforestation for firewood and widespread trampling of fragile marsh flora.",al={"why kill gnolls wetlands","mosshide gnoll threat"}},{q="Where are the gnolls causing this damage?",a="The Mosshide gnolls and mongrels gather in large numbers to the south of the Wetlands, clustered particularly near the dwarven pass of Dun Algaz.",al={"where are mosshide gnolls","tramping paws location"}},{q="What comes after culling the gnolls?",a="Once the packs are thinned, Rethiel looks deeper into the source of their unusual activity and fuel consumption, sending adventurers on the follow-up quest 'Fire Taboo'.",al={"next quest after tramping paws","tramping paws follow up"},sp=1},{q="Why does Rethiel mention having her faith tested?",a="Rethiel tells you that its faith in your people has been taxed in the past, and it views mortals and their rapid expansion with wariness. Helping her protect the wild fen proves that mortal adventurers can act as stewards of nature rather than exploiters.",al={"rethiel dialogue","faith taxed in the past"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Rethiel's mission directly mirrors the Cenarion mandate to maintain ecological equilibrium, culling unnatural population spikes to ensure the marsh does not collapse.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves share ancestral bonds with the wild spirits of nature, making Rethiel's plea to heal the marsh a familiar and honored duty.",["race:Dwarf"]="With the gnolls swarming directly outside the Gate of Algaz, culling them not only preserves the fen but also secures the vital road linking Ironforge to Menethil Harbor."},kw={"algaz","gnolls","greenwarden","mongrels","mosshide","rethiel","tramping paws","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:463","quest:277","zone:wetlands","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=276},src={"Tramping Paws"}}
E["quest:277"] = {t="quest",n="Fire Taboo",z="wetlands",s="Fire Taboo is a task assigned by Rethiel the Greenwarden along the marshy roads of the Wetlands. Tormented by the suffering of the local forest, the bog beast sends travelers to strip the Mosshide gnolls of the crude flints they use to ignite and burn living wood. By depriving the gnolls of fire, Rethiel hopes to spare the bog's ancient boughs from being consumed.",h="Fire Taboo is a task assigned by Rethiel the Greenwarden along the marshy roads of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Greenwarden's Anguish",b="Rethiel the Greenwarden watches over the wilds of the Wetlands, maintaining a profound spiritual kinship with the trees of the marsh. While the natural cycle of rot and renewal belongs in a swamp, the deliberate destruction of the timber cuts deep into her spirit. To a living spirit of the marsh, hearing the groans of living boughs chopped down and cast into hearthfires is an agony she can no longer endure in silence.",sp=0},{t="Extinguishing the Mosshides",b="The Mosshide pack ravages the wetlands for warmth and territory, felling green trees rather than gathering fallen deadwood. To curb their expansion without a prolonged war of attrition, Rethiel targets the key tool of their destruction: the crude flints used by the stronger gnolls. By stripping the pack of fire-making implements, she renders them unable to burn the felled timber. She personally shatters each collected stone and casts the dust into the sea, ensuring those sparks will never ignite the forest again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel the Greenwarden is a bog beast dwelling in the Wetlands. Bound deeply to the vitality of the local trees and plant life, she seeks to protect the wounded swamp from the depredations of the Mosshide gnolls.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel greenwarden lore","who gives fire taboo"}},{q="Why does Rethiel want crude flints instead of killing the gnoll leaders?",a="Rethiel considers burning living wood an unpardonable violation. By seizing the flints, she directly prevents the gnolls from lighting fires to consume the wetland's trees, crippling their encampments and ending the destruction of living wood.",al={"why flints","why take flints","crude flint purpose"}},{q="What happens to the flints once they are turned in?",a="Rethiel smashes the crude flints to pieces and casts the remnants into the sea so they can never again be struck to produce a spark against living timber.",al={"what does she do with flints","flint destruction"}},{q="Which gnolls carry the flints?",a="The stronger members of the Mosshide pack carry crude flints. The smaller Mosshide gnolls and the weaker mongrels are not trusted with fire-making tools and do not carry them.",al={"who drops flints","which gnolls have crude flint"}},{q="Why are the Mosshides cutting down trees?",a="The Mosshide gnolls cut down living trees to fuel their campfires and warm themselves in the damp swamp, rather than relying on dry, fallen timber.",al={"why gnolls cut trees","mosshide woodcutting"}},{q="What comes next after gathering the flints?",a="After you deprive the gnolls of fire, Rethiel sends you to deal with another blight afflicting the marshes in the follow-up quest, Blisters on The Land.",al={"what quest is after fire taboo","next quest after flints"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As guardians of the wild, druids share Rethiel's reverent bond with the trees and understand the unnatural pain of living wood subjected to gnoll firepits.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves revere the daughters of Cenarius, recognizing Rethiel's sacred duty to guard the spirits of the boughs from barbaric desecration.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Mosshide gnolls threaten travelers passing through the Wetlands; aiding the local spirits helps secure the trade routes connecting Dun Morogh and Arathi."},kw={"crude flint","fire taboo","gnolls","greenwarden","living wood","mosshide","rethiel","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:276","quest:275","topic:gnoll","zone:wetlands","quest:463"},m={start="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=277},src={"Fire Taboo"}}
E["quest:288"] = {t="quest",n="The Third Fleet",z="wetlands",s="Sitting in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, First Mate Fitzsimmons drowns his memories in dwarven mead. He is the lone survivor of Kul Tiras's Third Fleet, a proud naval force incinerated off the coast of the Wetlands by orc-enslaved red dragons during the Second War.",h="Sitting in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor, First Mate Fitzsimmons drowns his memories in dwarven...",sec={{t="A Sailor's Grief",b="First Mate Fitzsimmons spends his days slumped inside Menethil Harbor's Deepwater Tavern, nursing an unending hangover and memories he cannot shake. Once an officer aboard the Wave Mistress—a ship-of-the-line sailing under the maritime banner of Kul Tiras—he now trades his grim memories for flagons of dwarven mead. Anyone willing to buy him another drink receives an eyewitness account of one of the Second War's most devastating naval slaughters.",sp=0},{t="Fire Over the Waves",b="During the Second War, the Third Fleet sailed along the shores of Khaz Modan when disaster struck from the skies. The Dragonmaw clan, having subjugated the red dragonflight at Grim Batol, unleashed dragonfire upon the unsuspecting warships. Fitzsimmons recalls helpless wooden hulls burning beneath towering plumes of flame, dragging entire crews into the deep. Fitzsimmons alone survived to wash ashore, leaving his fallen brothers behind in the watery graveyard now known as the Doomed Fleet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons?",a="He is an old sailor drinking away his trauma in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. Formerly the first mate of the Kul Tiras warship Wave Mistress, he is the sole known survivor of the Third Fleet's destruction.",al={"fitzsimmons","who is the drunk sailor","fitzsimmons tavern"}},{q="What happened to the Third Fleet?",a="The Third Fleet of Kul Tiras was ambushed and incinerated off the coast of the Wetlands during the Second War. Dragon-riding orcs from the Dragonmaw clan rained fire from above, sending the fleet's ships and sailors to the seabed.",al={"third fleet fate","how did the fleet sink","kul tiras ships sunk"}},{q="Why were dragons attacking human ships?",a="During the Second War, the Dragonmaw clan enslaved the red dragon Alexstrasza using the Demon Soul at nearby Grim Batol. Bound by dark sorcery, the red dragons were forced to act as monstrous mounts and siege weapons for the Horde.",al={"dragonmaw dragons","red dragons wetlans","why orcs on dragons"}},{q="Where did the ships actually sink?",a="The charred wrecks lie submerged off the western coast of the Wetlands, north of Menethil Harbor, a tragic expanse now remembered as the Doomed Fleet.",al={"where is the doomed fleet","shipwreck location wetlands","third fleet wreckage"}},{q="What drink does Fitzsimmons want?",a="He needs a flagon of dwarven mead to loosen his tongue and stave off his splitting hangover, which can be bought directly from the innkeeper inside the Deepwater Tavern.",al={"fitzsimmons mead","what does fitzsimmons want","flagon of mead"}},{q="What nation did the Third Fleet serve?",a="The fleet belonged to Kul Tiras, the island maritime kingdom whose formidable navy served as the backbone of the Alliance's naval forces during the Second War.",al={"is the third fleet stormwind","kul tiras fleet","who owned the wave mistress"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="The destruction of the Third Fleet is a bitter reminder of the catastrophic naval battles fought by Kul Tiras and the Alliance against the Dragonmaw.",["faction:Alliance"]="Hearing Fitzsimmons recount the fall of the Wave Mistress reminds Alliance defenders of the lingering scars left by the Horde's dragon-riders across Khaz Modan.",["race:Dwarf"]="Grim Batol cast a shadow over all of Khaz Modan, and the dragons bred within its depths wreaked havoc on dwarf lands and human allies alike."},kw={"deepwater tavern","doomed fleet","dragonmaw","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","menethil harbor","red dragons","third fleet","wave mistress","wetlands"},rel={"npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","subzone:deepwater-tavern","quest:270","topic:kul-tiras","zone:wetlands"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=288},src={"The Third Fleet (Classic)"}}
E["quest:289"] = {t="quest",n="The Cursed Crew",z="wetlands",s="First Mate Fitzsimmons, the sole living survivor of the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras, asks for mercy on behalf of his lost brethren. Trapped by a dark relic hidden aboard their sunken ships off the Wetlands coast, the drowned sailors and marines wander the wrecks as restless undead.",h="First Mate Fitzsimmons, the sole living survivor of the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras, asks for mercy on behalf of...",sec={{t="A Restless Fleet",b="When the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras foundered along the jagged shores north of Menethil Harbor, its tragedy did not end beneath the waves. While First Mate Fitzsimmons managed to wash ashore alive, his fellow crewmen met a fate far worse than death. A mysterious and terrible treasure hidden deep within one of the hulls unleashed an eerie sorcery upon the dying sailors, binding their souls to the sea-battered timbers and denying them the peace of the grave.",sp=0},{t="Mercy by the Blade",b="Fitzsimmons, lingering in the taverns of Menethil Harbor, remains haunted by the nightly moans and cries of his former shipmates. Believing that putting down their animated corpses will offer them release, he sends adventurers into the rotting, drowned hulks to strike down the cursed sailors, the seasoned marines, and his former peer, First Mate Snellig, retrieving Snellig's personal snuffbox as grim proof that his friend has finally been laid to rest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was First Mate Snellig?",a="First Mate Snellig served aboard the ill-fated Third Fleet of Kul Tiras alongside First Mate Fitzsimmons. After the fleet wrecked off the northern coast of the Wetlands, Snellig drowned with the rest of the crew, only to be resurrected by the malevolent relic stowed aboard the ships. He now haunts the flooded hold of one of the wrecks as an undead horror.",al={"snellig","first mate snellig","who is snellig"}},{q="Why are the sailors and marines cursed?",a="According to Fitzsimmons, one of the fleet's vessels carried a concealed, malignant treasure. When the ships wrecked along the coast, the dark energies of this artifact bound the spirits of the drowned crew to their rotting hulls, preventing their souls from passing on and forcing them into undead torment.",al={"why are they undead","third fleet curse","cursed sailors cause"}},{q="Where are the sunken ships located?",a="The ruined hulks of the Third Fleet lie submerged off the coast in the northern Wetlands, north of Menethil Harbor. The cursed crew prowls both the submerged decks and the surrounding water, with Snellig himself lurking inside the cracked hull of the southern vessel.",al={"where are the ships","wreck location","where is snellig"}},{q="Why does Fitzsimmons want Snellig's snuffbox?",a="The snuffbox was a personal keepsake belonging to First Mate Snellig in life. Bringing it back to Fitzsimmons serves as tangible proof that his cursed comrade has finally been granted release from his rotting prison beneath the waves.",al={"snelligs snuffbox","snuff box","why snuffbox"}},{q="Who is First Mate Fitzsimmons?",a="Fitzsimmons is a Kul Tiran sailor and the only known living survivor of the Third Fleet. Broken by grief and guilt, he stays in Menethil Harbor, haunted by nightmares of his drowned brothers and desperately seeking travelers willing to end their suffering.",al={"fitzsimmons","first mate fitzsimmons"}},{q="Does killing the crew actually break the curse?",a="Striking down the sailors and marines grants temporary respite to their restless spirits, but it does not shatter the enchantment entirely. The root of the curse remains tied to the mysterious relic still hidden aboard the wreckage.",al={"is the curse lifted","does this end the curse"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Kul Tiras has long supplied the finest sailors to the Grand Alliance; putting their tormented spirits to rest is a somber duty of honor for any Alliance adventurer.",["class:Paladin"]="The sailors of the Third Fleet were innocent men ensnared by a profane relic; laying them to rest cleanses unholy desecration and brings light to dark waters.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers feel the weight of brotherhood with these fallen sailors, recognizing the shared naval traditions of the kingdom of Kul Tiras."},kw={"cursed crew","cursed marine","cursed sailor","fitzsimmons","kul tiras","menethil","snellig","snuffbox","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"quest:288","npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:kul-tiras"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=289},src={"The Cursed Crew (Classic)"}}
E["quest:290"] = {t="quest",n="Lifting the Curse",z="wetlands",s="First Mate Fitzsimmons believes that the restless curse binding his fallen crewmates stems from a dark artifact secured aboard their wrecked flagship, the Intrepid. To set his brethren free, an adventurer must face the ghost of Captain Halyndor, take the strongbox key, and recover the relic from the submerged hull.",h="First Mate Fitzsimmons believes that the restless curse binding his fallen crewmates stems from a dark...",sec={{t="A Captain's Burden",b="First Mate Fitzsimmons survived the tragic fate of the Third Fleet, but the memory of his comrades haunts his waking hours and his dreams. He remains convinced that the undeath gripping his shipmates is tied to a mysterious, malignant object locked away inside the strongbox of his old vessel, the Intrepid. Overseeing the wreck is the spectral remnants of Captain Halyndor, who even in death fiercely guards the key to the vessel's deepest secrets.",sp=0},{t="Unlocking the Depths",b="Off the mist-choked coast of the northern Wetlands lie the fractured hulks of the Third Fleet. Resting within the flooded hull of the Intrepid, the ship's locked strongbox holds the relic at the heart of the crew's misery. Reclaiming it requires defeating Halyndor's tortured ghost on deck, securing the rusted key, and braving the flooded interior to retrieve the dark artifact so that holy hands can cleanse it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What ship are you searching during this quest?",a="You are searching the Intrepid, the sunken flagship of the Third Fleet resting off the northeastern shore of the Wetlands.",al={"which ship","intrepid shipwreck","where is the strongbox"}},{q="Who is Captain Halyndor?",a="Captain Halyndor was the commanding officer of the Intrepid. In death, his restless spirit haunts the deck of the ruined vessel, clinging stubbornly to the key to his ship's strongbox.",al={"who is halyndor","captain halyndor lore"}},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons want the strongbox opened?",a="Fitzsimmons believes a cursed object secured inside the strongbox is responsible for trapping the spirits of his fellow sailors in torment, and opening it is the only way to recover the artifact for purification.",al={"fitzsimmons goal","why open strongbox","purpose of quest"}},{q="Where is the Intrepid's strongbox located?",a="The strongbox sits submerged inside the lower hull of the Intrepid, accessible through a breach in the side of the wrecked ship beneath the waves.",al={"strongbox location","where is the chest","how to find strongbox"}},{q="Who can cleanse the cursed object once it is recovered?",a="Fitzsimmons directs adventurers to take the recovered object to the dwarven priest Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil Harbor to have its foul taint cleansed.",al={"who cleanses the relic","who is glorin steelbrow","where take cursed thing"}},{q="What caused the shipwreck in the first place?",a="During the Second War the Third Fleet was attacked by red dragons controlled by orcs, and its ships were burned and sunk off the Wetlands coast; the cursed treasure aboard now keeps the drowned crews from rest.",al={"how did third fleet sink","third fleet wreckage cause"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="Unraveling spiritual afflictions and cleansing tainted relics requires spiritual authority, which is why Fitzsimmons entrusts the final purification of the strongbox's contents to the priesthood.",["faction:Alliance"]="The sailors of the Third Fleet served the Alliance in life, and laying their tortured souls to rest is an obligation of honor for Alliance champions traveling through Menethil Harbor."},kw={"captain halyndor","fitzsimmons","glorin steelbrow","intrepid","lifting the curse","menethil harbor","strongbox","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","npc:glorin-steelbrow","quest:288","zone:wetlands"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",["end"]="Intrepid's Locked Strongbox",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=290},src={"Lifting the Curse (Classic)"}}
E["quest:292"] = {t="quest",n="The Eye of Paleth",z="wetlands",s="This quest sees an adventurer recover a blackened, pulsating gem known as the Cursed Eye of Paleth from the flooded wreckage of the Intrepid. Recovered at the behest of the haunted sailor Fitzsimmons, the malevolent artifact must be brought to Menethil Harbor so the dwarven priest Glorin Steelbrow can divine how to purge its blight.",h="This quest sees an adventurer recover a blackened, pulsating gem known as the Cursed Eye of Paleth from the...",sec={{t="A Blighted Relic",b="Beneath the treacherous waters of the Baradin Bay, resting inside the locked strongbox of the sunken vessel Intrepid, lies no ordinary treasure. The chest yields a blackened orb pulsing with an unsettling radiance: an Eye of Paleth. Rather than gleaning sacred light, this particular stone has been warped into an engine of suffering, heavily tied to the restless spirits and doom that claimed the sailors of the Third Fleet.",sp=0},{t="Seeking the Priesthood",b="Recognizing that such dark magic exceeds common salvage, the artifact is brought directly ashore to Menethil Harbor. There, Glorin Steelbrow, a dwarven priest of the Holy Light, inspects the anomaly. While stunned that such a sacred device was ever in the possession of the Third Fleet, Glorin immediately recognizes its unnatural taint and begins preparing the rites necessary to undo its dark influence.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of Paleth?",a="The Eye of Paleth is an ancient and powerful sacred gem. Normally associated with holy energies, this particular specimen was aboard the sunken Third Fleet vessel Intrepid and has become twisted and cursed, radiating dark magic.",al={"eye of paleth lore","what is paleth","cursed eye of paleth"}},{q="Where was the Eye recovered?",a="It is recovered from a locked strongbox aboard the flooded wreck of the Intrepid, resting just off the mist-shrouded coast of the Wetlands.",al={"where do i find the eye","eye of paleth location","intrepid strongbox"}},{q="Why does Glorin Steelbrow care about the artifact?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarven priest stationed in Menethil Harbor. As a practitioner of the Holy Light, he possesses the sacred knowledge required to recognize ancient relics and begin the rituals necessary to break sinister curses.",al={"who is glorin steelbrow","why steelbrow"}},{q="How does Fitzsimmons know about the Eye?",a="Fitzsimmons is a survivor of the Third Fleet who remains haunted by the tragedy. Traumatized and taking refuge in Menethil's tavern, he knew of the dark relic hidden in the wreckage that tormented his fallen crewmates.",al={"fitzsimmons connection","why did fitzsimmons send me"}},{q="Why is the Eye cursed?",a="While its exact corruption remains tied to the supernatural demise and restless undead haunting the wrecked ships of the Third Fleet, the artifact absorbed dark energies during or after the catastrophe that sent the fleet to the ocean floor.",al={"why is it cursed","eye curse origin"}},{q="What happens after giving the Eye to Glorin?",a="Glorin examines the cursed gem and determines that it cannot be left in its blighted state, directing the adventurer to cleanse the relic of its corrupting influence.",al={"next quest","what to do with the eye"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Priest"]="Dealing with the defilement of a sacred artifact like the Eye of Paleth makes this investigation directly relevant to priests of the Holy Light.",["race:Dwarf"]="Uncovering lost artifacts off the shores of Khaz Modan touches upon the dwarven dedication to reclaiming hidden relics, aided by Ironforge clergy like Glorin Steelbrow.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Third Fleet was an Alliance expedition whose destruction left Menethil Harbor vulnerable; retrieving its remnants helps bring closure to lost comrades."},kw={"cursed eye of paleth","eye of paleth","fitzsimmons","glorin steelbrow","intrepid","menethil harbor","third fleet","wetlands"},rel={"quest:293","npc:glorin-steelbrow","quest:288","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:light"},m={start="Intrepid's Locked Strongbox",["end"]="Glorin Steelbrow",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=292},src={"The Eye of Paleth (Classic)"}}
E["quest:293"] = {t="quest",n="Cleansing the Eye",z="wetlands",s="Cleansing the Eye is an Alliance quest that sends adventurers from the murky Wetlands south to the human capital of Stormwind. After recovering the cursed scrying stone known as the Eye of Paleth, travelers must seek the aid of Archbishop Benedictus to purge its lingering taint.",h="Cleansing the Eye is an Alliance quest that sends adventurers from the murky Wetlands south to the human...",sec={{t="A Tainted Relic",b="The Eye of Paleth recovered from the marshlands does not shine with holy clarity. Instead, it is steeped in an unsettling shadow, bearing the residual sorrow and trauma of the terrible tragedy that unfolded where it was lost. The dwarf Glorin Steelbrow recognizes the power of the orb, but admits he lacks the divine craft to lift such a heavy affliction.",sp=0},{t="Journey to the Cathedral",b="Because the Eyes of Paleth were originally fashioned by human priests of the Holy Light, only their highest order possesses the knowledge to undo the defilement. Glorin directs adventurers to journey to the kingdom of Stormwind and present the darkened orb to Archbishop Benedictus, leader of the Church of the Holy Light. Benedictus recognizes the immense danger of an unpurified relic and takes it upon himself to restore its sacred luminance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of Paleth?",a="The Eyes of Paleth are sacred orbs crafted by human priests to shine with holy luminance and act as viewing or scrying focuses. When untainted, their power aligns with the Holy Light, but if corrupted, their ambient energies become volatile and perilous.",al={"eye of paleth lore","what is this orb","what is the eye of paleth"}},{q="Why can't Glorin Steelbrow cleanse the Eye himself?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarf stationed in the Wetlands who lacks the specialized liturgical craft needed to banish such a dark affliction. Since the relic was created by human priests of the Holy Light, lifting its corruption requires an authority of that exact tradition.",al={"why send me to stormwind","glorin cleansing","why benedictus"}},{q="Who is Archbishop Benedictus?",a="Archbishop Benedictus is the venerable leader of the Church of the Holy Light, residing within the grand Cathedral of Light in Stormwind. He succeeded Archbishop Alonsus Faol and serves as a pillar of spiritual guidance for the Alliance.",al={"who is benedictus","archbishop benedictus","stormwind archbishop"}},{q="Why is the Eye described as soiled or sorrowful?",a="According to Archbishop Benedictus, the orb bore witness to an immense, tragic event in the Wetlands, soaking up that agony over time. This lingering sorrow transformed into a corrupting curse that warped the relic's inherent power.",al={"why is it cursed","eye of paleth tragedy","cursed eye of paleth"}},{q="What happens once Benedictus receives the orb?",a="Benedictus agrees to perform a ritual of purification. He warns that the Eyes of Paleth are meant to shine brightly, and leaving such an artifact tainted poses a grave spiritual and physical danger to those nearby.",al={"does benedictus cleanse it","eye of paleth outcome"}},{q="Where is the Cathedral of Light located?",a="The Cathedral of Light dominates Cathedral Square in the northern district of Stormwind City. Archbishop Benedictus stands at the main altar at the heart of the sanctuary.",al={"where is cathedral of light","cathedral of light location","find benedictus"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For priests of the Holy Light, handling the Cursed Eye of Paleth demonstrates the tragic malleability of sacred crafts when exposed to despair, underscoring the importance of Archbishop Benedictus's purifying intervention.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins view the reclamation of holy relics from dark marshes as a solemn duty, seeing the corruption of the Eye as an affront to be cleansed within the hallowed halls of Stormwind.",["faction:Alliance"]="The quest highlights the cooperation between the dwarven outposts of the Wetlands and the spiritual leadership of Stormwind, binding the kingdoms together through shared faith."},kw={"archbishop benedictus","cathedral of light","cleansing the eye","cursed eye of paleth","eye of paleth","glorin steelbrow","stormwind","wetlands"},rel={"quest:292","npc:archbishop-benedictus","npc:glorin-steelbrow","subzone:cathedral-of-light","zone:wetlands","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:light"},m={start="Glorin Steelbrow",["end"]="Archbishop Benedictus",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=293},src={"Cleansing the Eye"}}
E["quest:294"] = {t="quest",n="Ormer's Revenge",z="wetlands",s="Ormer's Revenge begins the retributive campaign of Ormer Ironbraid, an explorer stranded high above the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. After unearthing ancient fossilized bones, the dwarven dig team inadvertently drew packs of ravenous mottled raptors that slaughtered their companions and trapped the survivors on a rocky bluff.",h="Ormer's Revenge begins the retributive campaign of Ormer Ironbraid, an explorer stranded high above the...",sec={{t="Unearthed Horrors",b="The Whelgar Excavation Site was meant to be a triumph for dwarven archaeology, exposing massive prehistoric remains buried beneath the Wetlands muck. Instead, unearthing the colossal bones caught the attention of the marsh's native raptors. Drawn by the disturbance, packs of mottled predators swarmed the dig site, catching the excavators off guard and tearing through their ranks.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Stand",b="Only a handful of dwarves survived the initial slaughter. Ormer Ironbraid, Merrin Rockweaver, and Prospector Whelgar managed to scramble up a bluff overlooking the pit, but they remain pinned by aggressive packs below. Driven by raw grief and boiling anger, Ormer refuses to merely hide. Bound by duty to guard the trembling Prospector and Merrin, he enlists able travelers to thin the surrounding Mottled Raptors and Mottled Screechers as the opening salvo of his vengeance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the excavators here?",a="When the dwarven archaeologists uncovered the giant bones in the basin, the commotion and scent drew the local raptor packs out of the marsh. The predators overran the camp, massacring most of the crew and trapping the three survivors atop the high bluff.",al={"why are raptors here","whelgar excavation massacre","what killed the dwarves"}},{q="Who is Ormer Ironbraid?",a="Ormer is one of the surviving dwarven excavators stranded at Whelgar's Excavation Site. While he feels bound by honor to stay and protect the shaken Prospector Whelgar and Merrin Rockweaver, his primary desire is bloody retribution against the raptors that butchered his comrades.",al={"who is ormer","ormer ironbraid backstory"}},{q="Where do these raptors come from?",a="Mottled Raptors and Mottled Screechers are native predators of the Wetlands, lurking throughout the muddy slopes and marshland west of the excavation bluff as well as the paths leading up toward the dig site's caves.",al={"where are mottled raptors","raptor locations wetlands"}},{q="Why doesn't Ormer hunt the raptors himself?",a="Although eager to shed raptor blood personally, Ormer is obligated to stand guard over the terrified Prospector Whelgar and Merrin Rockweaver to ensure their bluff refuge is not overrun.",al={"why doesn't ormer fight","why is ormer stuck"}},{q="Does culling these raptors end Ormer's grudge?",a="No. Slashing through the common Mottled Raptors and Screechers is only the first step in Ormer's plan to avenge his fallen friends, with harsher strikes against the raptor brood to follow.",al={"is this the end of ormer's revenge","what happens next with ormer"}},{q="Why did uncovering the bones attract the raptors?",a="The raptors of the Wetlands are fiercely territorial and scavenge aggressively. Blasting and excavating ancient giant remains disrupted the basin's natural balance, drawing curious and hungry predators right into the center of the dig camp.",al={"why did bones attract raptors","dinosaur bones raptors"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing dwarven brethren slain at an Explorers' League archaeological endeavor turns clearing the raptor-infested quarry into an act of ancestral honor and righteous retribution.",["class:Hunter"]="The aggressive mottled raptors prowling the slopes outside the site provide keen hunters an opportunity to study dangerous reptilian tracking behavior in marsh terrain."},kw={"mottled raptor","mottled screecher","ormer ironbraid","ormer's revenge","prospector whelgar","wetlands","whelgar excavation site"},rel={"npc:ormer-ironbraid","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Ormer Ironbraid",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=294},src={"Ormer's Revenge"}}
E["quest:295"] = {t="quest",n="Ormer's Revenge",z="wetlands",s="Ormer's Revenge is an Alliance task given by Ormer Ironbraid at the ruined Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. With the initial scout raptors culled, Ormer demands the slaughter of the heavier Mottled Scytheclaws and Razormaws that drove his expedition from the pits.",h="Ormer's Revenge is an Alliance task given by Ormer Ironbraid at the ruined Whelgar Excavation Site in the...",sec={{t="Escalating the Hunt",b="Ormer Ironbraid's grudge against the raptors running rampant over the Whelgar Excavation Site is deeply personal. After thinning out the smaller juveniles that overran the upper camp, he turns your blades against the adult predators prowling the lower dig site. The Mottled Scytheclaws and Razormaws represent the core threat to any hope of reclaiming the archaeological effort, tearing through dwarven prospectors and leaving the trenches littered with shattered crates and abandoned picks.",sp=0},{t="Blood in the Trenches",b="The excavation pits have effectively turned into a raptor nesting ground. As Ormer broods on the ridge overlooking the dig, he directs capable adventurers down into the mud to strike directly at the mature beasts. While Prospector Whelgar and his crew hope to salvage ancient relics, Ormer is entirely consumed by vengeance, demanding a hefty tally of dead scytheclaws and razormaws before he considers taking on the apex terror of the site.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Ormer so angry at these raptors?",a="The mottled raptors violently swarmed and overwhelmed the Whelgar Excavation Site, driving out the dwarven team and slaughtering anyone who couldn't escape in time. Ormer Ironbraid was left displaced and bitter, and he refuses to let the beasts control the dig without paying dearly in blood.",al={"why ormer mad","ormer revenge reason","why kill raptors wetlands"}},{q="Where are the Mottled Scytheclaws and Razormaws found?",a="Both breeds of raptors prowl the lower dig trenches and surrounding earthworks of the Whelgar Excavation Site, situated in the eastern hills of the Wetlands just south of the main road.",al={"mottled scytheclaw location","mottled razormaw location","where to find raptors ormer"}},{q="Who is Ormer Ironbraid?",a="Ormer Ironbraid is a dwarven member of the Explorers' League stationed at the Whelgar Excavation Site. Following the catastrophic overrun of the dig, he has made it his personal mission to exterminate the raptor pack infesting their work.",al={"who is ormer","ormer ironbraid lore"}},{q="What happens after culling these raptors?",a="Once you have culled the Scytheclaws and Razormaws, Ormer turns his focus to Sarltooth, the large raptor he believes leads the local pack, directing you to put an end to the prime source of the raptor infestation.",al={"what next after ormer revenge","ormer's revenge sequel","next quest after scytheclaws"},sp=1},{q="Does this quest connect to other tasks in the excavation site?",a="Yes. While hunting down the raptors throughout the lower dig site for Ormer, adventurers frequently assist Prospector Whelgar and his team with 'Uncovering the Past', collecting fragmented earthen artifacts scattered across the same trenches.",al={"whelgar excavation quests","uncovering the past connection"}},{q="Why were the dwarves digging here in the first place?",a="The Explorers' League of Ironforge established the Whelgar Excavation Site to search for titan relics and uncover the ancient history of the dwarven race, though their operations were halted when aggressive wildlife overran the dig.",al={"why excavate wetlands","whelgar excavation purpose"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Ormer's fury reflects the fierce pride of the Explorers' League, who refuse to let wild beasts permanently stall dwarven efforts to unearth their ancestral past.",["class:Hunter"]="The Mottled raptors of the Wetlands are ferociously territorial pack hunters, presenting a lethal tracking challenge inside the enclosed, muddy trenches.",["faction:Alliance"]="Reclaiming the Whelgar Excavation Site secures safe operations along the eastern road connecting the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands."},kw={"dwarf","excavation","explorers league","mottled razormaw","mottled scytheclaw","ormer ironbraid","raptors","wetlands","whelgar excavation"},rel={"quest:294","npc:ormer-ironbraid","quest:299","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Ormer Ironbraid",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=295},src={"Ormer's Revenge (2)"}}
E["quest:296"] = {t="quest",n="Ormer's Revenge",z="wetlands",s="Ormer's Revenge is the culmination of Ormer Ironbraid's campaign to avenge the dwarven excavators slaughtered at the Whelgar Excavation Site. Convinced that a cunning beast named Sarltooth spearheaded the savage raptor assault, Ormer sends an adventurer to slay the pack leader and claim his talon as proof.",h="Ormer's Revenge is the culmination of Ormer Ironbraid's campaign to avenge the dwarven excavators slaughtered...",sec={{t="A Strike at the Pack Leader",b="Following the slaughter of the Explorer's League diggers at the Whelgar Excavation Site, Ormer Ironbraid watched the teeming raptors from his ridge and observed a beast that dwarfed the rest. Known as Sarltooth, this particularly large and vicious raptor perched above the dig works, directing or leading the pack that drove the dwarves out. To Ormer, the beast was not merely wildlife, but the instigator of an attack on King Magni Bronzebeard's subjects.",sp=0},{t="Justice in the Wetlands",b="Ormer demands capital justice for the massacre, instructing adventurers to climb the high paths of the excavation walls and put an end to Sarltooth. By retrieving one of the beast's formidable talons, the fallen workers are avenged, sending a harsh message across the marshes that attacks against dwarven expeditions will not go unanswered.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sarltooth?",a="Sarltooth is a large, menacing raptor who leads the pack occupying the Whelgar Excavation Site in the Wetlands. Ormer Ironbraid believes he directed the assault that massacred the dwarven diggers.",al={"what is sarltooth","who is the raptor boss","sarltooth lore"}},{q="Where is Sarltooth located?",a="Sarltooth prowls along an elevated path running up the western wall in the northwest corner of the Whelgar Excavation Site.",al={"find sarltooth","where does sarltooth spawn","sarltooth path"}},{q="Why does Ormer want Sarltooth dead instead of just driving him away?",a="Ormer views the raptor assault as a direct crime against King Magni's subjects. Because innocent dwarven workers lost their lives doing their jobs, Ormer believes only death can redeem the memory of the fallen.",al={"ormer revenge reason","why kill sarltooth"}},{q="What proof does Ormer require?",a="Ormer demands one of Sarltooth's talons to verify that the massive predator has truly been slain.",al={"sarltooth proof","sarltooth talon"}},{q="Who were the victims at the excavation site?",a="Dwarven archaeologists and laborers sent by the Explorer's League to unearth titan artifacts were caught off guard and slaughtered when raptor packs overran the dig.",al={"who died at whelgar","excavation site victims"}},{q="Does killing Sarltooth secure the excavation site?",a="While killing Sarltooth removes the pack's deadliest threat and brings retribution for the fallen, raptors still crawl over the trenches, leaving the site dangerous and largely abandoned.",al={"is whelgar safe now","did ormer win"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, avenging the butchered Explorer's League crew at the Whelgar Excavation Site is a matter of honouring King Magni's fallen subjects.",["class:Hunter"]="Sarltooth represents one of the Wetlands' apex predators, demanding keen tracking skills to scale the ridge and take down the pack leader.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing dwarven expeditions in the marshlands ensures that Alliance footholds between Ironforge and the northern lands remain intact."},kw={"explorer's league","ormer ironbraid","raptors","sarltooth","talon","wetlands","whelgar excavation site"},rel={"npc:ormer-ironbraid","quest:299","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Ormer Ironbraid",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=296},src={"Ormer's Revenge (3)"}}
E["quest:299"] = {t="quest",n="Uncovering the Past",z="wetlands",s="Prospector Whelgar tasks adventurers with venturing into the overrun Whelgar's Excavation Site in the Wetlands to recover four missing pieces of an ancient tablet known as the Goaz Stone so its mysterious inscriptions can be translated.",h="Prospector Whelgar tasks adventurers with venturing into the overrun Whelgar's Excavation Site in the...",sec={{t="The Broken Stone",b="Before raptors swarmed the dig site in the Wetlands, Prospector Whelgar unearthed a significant relic: the Goaz Stone. Initial attempts to decipher its ancient script yielded fragmented references to a 'divine plan' and a 'doomed prophecy.' Unfortunately, key sections broke off in four distinct places, scattering critical passages across the fossil-strewn dirt.",sp=0},{t="Braving the Dig Site",b="Reconstructing the stone requires scouring the raptor-infested excavation grounds for the four missing fragments: Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru. Buried among loose soil and half-excavated relics guarded by aggressive Razormaws and Scytheclaws, finding every piece demands cutting through the apex predators of the marshland.",sp=0},{t="Chained Beneath the Land",b="Once reunited, the Goaz Stone reveals the delicate and enigmatic language of the Titans. Translating the reassembled glyphs, Whelgar uncovers a chilling inscription: 'Old Gods... Chained Beneath the Land.' Far from a simple historical oddity, the tablet hints at titanic struggles from the dawn of the world and shadowy evils buried under the crust of Azeroth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Goaz Stone?",a="The Goaz Stone is an ancient Titan relic discovered by Prospector Whelgar in the Wetlands excavation site. It contains cryptic inscriptions concerning cosmic history, a divine plan, and ancient entities bound deep underground.",al={"goaz stone lore","what is the goaz tablet","tablet fragments wetlands"},sp=1},{q="Who gives the quest Uncovering the Past?",a="Prospector Whelgar offers the quest from his vantage point overlooking Whelgar's Excavation Site in the southern hills of the Wetlands, having been driven away from his dig by feral raptors.",al={"who starts uncovering the past","where to get uncovering the past"}},{q="What fragments are needed to complete the tablet?",a="You need four specific stone fragments: Ados, Modr, Golm, and Neru. They are scattered throughout loose soil mounds and ancient urns across the raptor-infested quarry floor.",al={"which fragments","tablet piece names","ados modr golm neru"}},{q="Why can't Prospector Whelgar recover the fragments himself?",a="Whelgar is an elderly dwarven scholar. When vicious raptors suddenly invaded and overtook the quarry, he was forced to retreat and lacks the physical strength to fight through the packs alone.",al={"why doesn't whelgar get the stones","why whelgar asks you"}},{q="What do the translated Titan glyphs reveal?",a="Once the four missing pieces are set into place, Whelgar deciphers the Titan script, reading the phrase: 'Old Gods... Chained Beneath the Land.' This hints at the ancient cosmic entities locked away during the shaping of Azeroth.",al={"what does the goaz stone say","titan translation wetlands","old gods chained beneath the land"},sp=1},{q="Does this quest tie into any other nearby expeditions?",a="Yes. It directly complements Ormer Ironbraid's questline, Ormer's Revenge, which tasks adventurers with thinning the raptor population in the same excavation quarry.",al={"quests near excavation site","ormer ironbraid connection","ormer's revenge link"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Explorers' League considers every recovered relic vital to unlocking dwarven origins, and the Titan inscriptions on the Goaz Stone tie directly into that ancient heritage.",["faction:Alliance"]="Supporting League excavations throughout the Wetlands strengthens the Alliance's presence and secures valuable knowledge before it falls into wild or hostile hands."},kw={"ados","goaz stone","golm","modr","neru","prospector whelgar","titans","uncovering the past","wetlands","whelgar's excavation site"},rel={"npc:prospector-whelgar","quest:294","topic:titan","topic:old-god","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Prospector Whelgar",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=299},src={"Uncovering the Past"}}
E["quest:303"] = {t="quest",n="The Dark Iron War",z="wetlands",s="At the northern edge of the Wetlands, Motley Garmason mounts a desperate defense to reclaim Dun Modr from the Dark Iron clan. After enemy saboteurs shattered the Thandol Span and seized the town, the Ironforge Mountaineers are left holding a tenuous line while waiting for reinforcements that may never arrive.",h="At the northern edge of the Wetlands, Motley Garmason mounts a desperate defense to reclaim Dun Modr from the...",sec={{t="A Front at the Northern Gate",b="Dun Modr once stood as Ironforge's proud bastion guarding the southern end of the Thandol Span, the colossal bridge connecting Khaz Modan to Lordaeron. When Dark Iron saboteurs and demolitionists detonated the bridge's archway, they severed Alliance transit and swiftly overwhelmed the stronghold. Motley Garmason and a handful of surviving defenders managed to pull back just far enough to establish an observation camp, but without immediate counterattacks, the entire northern gateway risks permanent Dark Iron dominion.",sp=0},{t="Buying Time for the Reserves",b="With dwarven regiments deployed across Kalimdor and distant Alliance battlefields, Motley's small detachment has been largely left to fend for itself. His scouts attempt to signal Ironforge for relief, but communications have faltered and promised reserves are nowhere to be seen. In an attempt to buy time and disrupt enemy entrenchments, Motley orders surgical strikes directly into Dun Modr's ruins to thin the ranks of Dark Iron engineers, tunnelers, and front-line soldiers before they can push further south into the Wetlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Motley Garmason?",a="Motley Garmason is an Ironforge Mountaineer officer commanding the remnants of the Dun Modr garrison. Stationed just outside the occupied town, he coordinates scouting and guerrilla strikes against the occupying Dark Iron forces.",al={"motley garmason","who is motley","dun modr commander"}},{q="Why is Dun Modr so important to Ironforge?",a="Dun Modr guards the southern foot of the Thandol Span. As the sole overland highway linking Khaz Modan to the Arathi Highlands and northern Lordaeron, whoever controls Dun Modr effectively controls all ground travel and supply between the regions.",al={"why dun modr matters","dun modr importance","dun modr lore"}},{q="Why are Dark Iron dwarves fighting in the Wetlands?",a="The Dark Iron clan has long sought to undermine their Bronzebeard cousins and weaken the Alliance. By invading the Wetlands and destroying the Thandol Span, they cut off Ironforge's supply lines to the north and open a hostile second front behind Alliance borders.",al={"why are dark irons here","dark iron wetlands","dark iron war reason"}},{q="What happened to the Thandol Span?",a="Dark Iron tunnelers and demolitionists laid concentrated explosives within the Thandol Span's foundational arches, severely damaging the bridge to cut off Ironforge reinforcements from Lordaeron before overrunning Dun Modr.",al={"thandol span destroyed","who blew up the bridge","thandol span explosion"}},{q="Where are the Ironforge reserve forces?",a="Ironforge's military is heavily stretched across multiple campaigns abroad and home defenses. Garmason's scout, Roggo, has struggled to establish reliable contact with high command, leaving the Dun Modr outpost to hold the line with whatever local allies they can find.",al={"ironforge reserves","where are reinforcements","roggo reserve"}},{q="What happens after pushing back the Dark Irons in Dun Modr?",a="Clearing the foot soldiers and sappers buys crucial time, but Motley discovers that the operation is directed by a high-ranking Dark Iron commander entrenched deep in the ruins, leading to a direct hunt for their leadership.",al={"next quest after dark iron war","the fury runs deep quest","what follows the dark iron war"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard dwarves, the loss of Dun Modr is a bitter humiliation and a direct threat to Khaz Modan's sovereignty, demanding vengeance against their ancestral enemies.",["faction:Alliance"]="The destruction of the Thandol Span and the fall of Dun Modr sever overland access between Stormwind's northern allies and the southern kingdoms.",["profession:Engineering"]="The precision with which Dark Iron saboteurs deployed specialized explosives to shatter ancient dwarven stonework reveals chilling mastery of structural demolition."},kw={"bronzebeard","dark iron","demolitionists","dun modr","ironforge","motley garmason","saboteurs","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:378","quest:631","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:dwarf","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Motley Garmason",["end"]="Motley Garmason",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=303},src={"The Dark Iron War"}}
E["quest:304"] = {t="quest",n="A Grim Task",z="wetlands",s="Following the devastating Dark Iron assault on Dun Modr and the Thandol Span, Longbraid the Grim seeks vengeance for fallen kin and lost soldiers. He tasks brave travelers with tracking down and slaying the elusive Dark Iron warlock Balgaras the Foul, taking his ear as proof of the deed.",h="Following the devastating Dark Iron assault on Dun Modr and the Thandol Span, Longbraid the Grim seeks...",sec={{t="The Ruins of Dun Modr",b="The northern reaches of the Wetlands have seen intense fighting between the Mountaineers of Ironforge and infiltrators from the Dark Iron clan. During the siege, the town of Dun Modr was overtaken, and the western bridge of the Thandol Span was shattered. Longbraid the Grim lost not only many loyal soldiers in the assault, but also his own brother, leaving him determined to see the enemy paid back in kind.",sp=0},{t="A Cowardly Commander",b="Reconnaissance by scouts like Roggo revealed that the Dark Iron contingent occupying Dun Modr is commanded by a warlock known as Balgaras the Foul. Rather than meeting his foes face to face, Balgaras cowers in hiding while ordering his soldiers to carry out his dark designs. Longbraid hopes that cutting down Balgaras will break the backbone of the Dark Iron force, allowing the survivors of Ironforge to secure the vital passage northward.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Balgaras the Foul?",a="Balgaras the Foul is a Dark Iron warlock who commands the forces occupying Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands. Described by Longbraid the Grim as a coward, he avoids direct combat while sending throngs of Dark Iron troops to hold the region.",al={"balgaras","who is balgaras","dark iron leader dun modr"}},{q="Who is Longbraid the Grim?",a="Longbraid the Grim is a dwarf commander encamped outside the ruins of Dun Modr. He lost his brother and many soldiers when Dark Iron forces seized the settlement and destroyed the western crossing of the Thandol Span.",al={"longbraid","longbraid the grim","quest giver dun modr"}},{q="Why does Longbraid want Balgaras's ear?",a="Because Balgaras is an elusive target who frequently hides from open battle, Longbraid demands physical proof of the warlock's death to ensure the threat has truly been eliminated.",al={"why ear","ear of balgaras"}},{q="What happened to the Thandol Span?",a="The western bridge of the Thandol Span was destroyed by Dark Iron dwarves during their surprise offensive into Dun Modr, cutting off an essential roadway between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands.",al={"thandol span bridge destroyed","why is thandol span broken"}},{q="Where is Balgaras hiding?",a="Balgaras lurks within the captured fortifications and ruins around Dun Modr, hiding behind his soldiers rather than venturing out into the open marshlands.",al={"where is balgaras","find balgaras"}},{q="What happens after Balgaras is slain?",a="With Balgaras dead, Longbraid believes the remaining disorganized Dark Iron troops will be far easier to sweep aside before another commander can arrive to reinforce them.",al={"after a grim task","what next dun modr"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, the betrayal and violence of the Dark Iron clan at Dun Modr is a personal affront and a fresh wound in the long civil strife between the clans.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Thandol Span is the primary land route connecting Khaz Modan to Lordaeron, making the removal of Dark Iron saboteurs a critical strategic priority for the entire Alliance.",["class:Warlock"]="Balgaras the Foul wields sinister fel magic to orchestrate the slaughter of Dun Modr's defenders, showcasing the dangerous ends to which the Dark Irons turn their craft."},kw={"a grim task","balgaras the foul","dark iron","dun modr","longbraid the grim","roggo","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"npc:longbraid-the-grim","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Longbraid the Grim",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=304},src={"A Grim Task"}}
E["quest:305"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of The Excavation Team",z="wetlands",s="In Search of the Excavation Team begins with Tarrel Rockweaver in the Wetlands, who is distraught over a sudden silence from his wife, Merrin. Assigned to the prestigious Whelgar Excavation Site to the east, she has missed two weeks of regular letters, prompting fears that disaster has struck the expedition. Travelers are tasked with venturing into the marsh to locate the dig site and ascertain her safety.",h="In Search of the Excavation Team begins with Tarrel Rockweaver in the Wetlands, who is distraught over a...",sec={{t="A Husband's Dread",b="While stationed in the soggy expanse of the Wetlands, Tarrel Rockweaver anticipated steady correspondence from his wife Merrin. Operating out of the dwarven dig known as the Whelgar Excavation Site, Merrin had maintained weekly dispatches describing their work. When two full weeks passed without a single word, Tarrel grew convinced that calamity had overtaken the camp. With official dwarf authorities stretched thin, he relies on passing scouts to brave the perils of the marshes to see if the diggers still draw breath.",sp=0},{t="The Whelgar Dig",b="The Whelgar Excavation Site represents a typical dwarven endeavor to unearth ancient Titan relics and Titan-forged history buried in the muck of the Wetlands. However, digging into prehistoric strata in wild territory frequently exposes crews to untamed beasts and hostile subterranean threats. Reaching the site requires heading eastward into territory far removed from the relative safety of the main roads, where whatever disrupted the diggers' letters still lingers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tarrel Rockweaver?",a="Tarrel Rockweaver is a concerned dwarf stationed in the Wetlands. Terrified by an abrupt break in letters from his wife Merrin, who is working at the eastern excavation site, he mistakes passing adventurers for official scouts sent to investigate the camp's silence.",al={"tarrel rockweaver","quest giver","who gives in search of the excavation team"}},{q="Who is Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin Rockweaver is a dwarf archaeologist working with the Whelgar Excavation team in the eastern reaches of the Wetlands. She regularly wrote to her husband until an unexpected turn of events abruptly severed her communications.",al={"merrin rockweaver","tarrel wife","who is merrin"}},{q="Where is the Whelgar Excavation Site?",a="The Whelgar Excavation Site lies in the eastern portion of the Wetlands, nestled in the rocky ridges far off the main roadway.",al={"excavation site location","where to find merrin","where is whelgar excavation"}},{q="Why did Merrin stop sending letters?",a="The sudden silence from the excavation site was prompted by an emerging threat at the dig that cut the dwarven researchers off from normal courier routes and routine camp life.",al={"why did letters stop","what happened to excavation team","why no mail"}},{q="Who is the 'Longbraid' mentioned by Tarrel?",a="Longbraid is a dwarven authority figure who promised to deploy scouts to check on the Whelgar Excavation team if communications broke down, leading Tarrel to assume any capable adventurer arriving to help was sent on Longbraid's orders.",al={"who is longbraid","longbraid scout"}},{q="Is the excavation site safe to approach?",a="No. The site is located in the dangerous wilderness of the Wetlands, and whatever disrupted the team's weekly dispatches poses an active danger to anyone arriving at the dig.",al={"is the dig safe","whelgar dangerous"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Explorers' League takes great pride in unearthing ancient history, making the distress of kin at the Whelgar Excavation an urgent matter for any wandering dwarf.",["faction:Alliance"]="Maintaining dwarven footholds and research expeditions across the marshlands is vital to securing the Wetlands against encroaching wilderness perils."},kw={"explorers league","in search of the excavation team","longbraid","merrin rockweaver","tarrel rockweaver","wetlands","whelgar excavation"},rel={"npc:tarrel-rockweaver","npc:merrin-rockweaver","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Tarrel Rockweaver",["end"]="Merrin Rockweaver",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=305},src={"In Search of The Excavation Team"}}
E["quest:306"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of The Excavation Team",z="wetlands",s="This errand delivers word of a disastrous dinosaur attack at the Whelgar's Excavation site back to Menethil Harbor. Merrin Rockweaver writes a hasty letter to reassure her anxious husband, Tarrel, while recounting how the expedition was overrun.",h="This errand delivers word of a disastrous dinosaur attack at the Whelgar's Excavation site back to Menethil...",sec={{t="A Message from the Ruins",b="After locating the remnants of the excavation team cowering near the ridge overlooking the dig site, Merrin Rockweaver provides a hasty report. Unearthing rare artifacts alongside massive prehistoric fossils proved fatal when packs of native mottled raptors swarmed the diggers. The sudden ferocity left most of the crew dead and the survivors cut off from civilization.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Relief",b="Returning to Menethil Harbor brings grim comfort to Tarrel Rockweaver. Knowing his wife and at least two companions survived thanks to the courage of a defender named Ormer eases his mind, though the slaughter of so many colleagues weighs heavily on the town's frontier spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the excavation team in the Wetlands?",a="While unearthing rare artifacts and massive ancient bones, the dwarven expedition was caught off guard and overrun by territorial mottled raptors. Most of the diggers were slain, leaving only a handful of survivors trapped on the bluffs above the dig site.",al={"what happened to dig site","wetlands excavation disaster","why did excavation fail"}},{q="Who saved Merrin Rockweaver?",a="Merrin credits a brave defender named Ormer with fighting off the raptors and escorting her and the Prospector to relative safety up on the ridge as the lower site collapsed.",al={"who saved merrin","ormer rockweaver","who is ormer"}},{q="Who is Tarrel Rockweaver?",a="Tarrel Rockweaver is Merrin's husband, stationed back at Menethil Harbor. Anxious over the lack of communication from the dig site, he sought travelers to investigate her whereabouts.",al={"who is tarrel","tarrel rockweaver location"}},{q="Where is the dig site located?",a="The excavation site lies inland in the southern reach of the Wetlands, east of Menethil Harbor near the base of the Ironforge mountain ridges.",al={"where is excavation","whelgar excavation location"}},{q="What was the expedition digging for?",a="Under the direction of dwarven prospectors, the team was excavating rare subterranean artifacts and large prehistoric fossils buried in the marshes.",al={"what were they digging for","excavation artifacts"}},{q="Are there other survivors beside Merrin?",a="Yes, Merrin mentions that Ormer and the chief Prospector managed to escape the raptors alongside her, bringing the known survivor count to three.",al={"who else survived","excavation survivors"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The disaster at the excavation cuts deeply into dwarven archeological ambitions, highlighting the perils King Magni's explorers face far from the safety of Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="The supply roads and frontier projects across the Wetlands remain dangerously vulnerable to wild beasts, requiring constant vigilance from Alliance travelers."},kw={"excavation","menethil harbor","merrin rockweaver","mottled raptors","ormer","tarrel rockweaver","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:305","npc:merrin-rockweaver","npc:tarrel-rockweaver","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Merrin Rockweaver",["end"]="Tarrel Rockweaver",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=306},src={"In Search of The Excavation Team (2)"}}
E["quest:321"] = {t="quest",n="Lightforge Iron",z="wetlands",s="Lightforge Iron is an Alliance salvage task given by Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil Harbor. Adventurers are sent to scour the wreckage of the Flying Osprey, an elven destroyer carrying rare sacred metal that was lost alongside the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras during the Second War.",h="Lightforge Iron is an Alliance salvage task given by Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Sacred Cargo",b="While most of the sunken hulls littering the Wetlands coastline belonged to the famed Third Fleet of Kul Tiras, one vessel was distinct: an elven destroyer christened the Flying Osprey. Bound from Lordaeron, the ship sought safety in numbers alongside the naval fleet, carrying a precious cargo of Lightforge iron. Unfortunately, convoying with war galleys did little to spare it when the Dragonmaw clan's enslaved red dragons descended from the sky, setting the fleet ablaze and plunging both soldiers and sanctified metal beneath the tides.",sp=0},{t="Plundered by the Tides",b="Reaching the shattered remains of the Flying Osprey south of Menethil Harbor reveals that time and the sea have not been the only forces at work. The waterlogged chest holding the shipment has been battered open and clawed through. Coastal murlocs, always eager scavengers of wrecks, have ransacked the hold and scattered the ingots, leaving behind barely a trace of the precious ore Glorin Steelbrow seeks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Flying Osprey?",a="The Flying Osprey was an elven destroyer sailing out of Lordaeron during the Second War. It carried a shipment of rare Lightforge iron and traveled alongside the Third Fleet of Kul Tiras for protection, only to be burned and sunk along with the rest of the fleet by orc-enslaved red dragons.",al={"flying osprey lore","elven destroyer wetlands","what ship had the iron"}},{q="Who is Glorin Steelbrow?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarf stationed at Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. He is interested in recovering historical salvage and valuable materials from the sunken ships along the coastline, particularly legendary metals like Lightforge iron.",al={"glorin steelbrow","dwarf in menethil","who gives lightforge iron"}},{q="What is Lightforge iron?",a="Lightforge iron is an exceptionally rare, sanctified metal used to forge consecrated arms and armor. It is prized by smiths and champions of the Holy Light for its purity and resilient spiritual properties.",al={"lightforge metal","what is lightforge iron","lightforge ingots"}},{q="Why were the ships sunk in the Wetlands?",a="During the Second War, the Horde's Dragonmaw clan used the Demon Soul to enslave the Red Dragonflight. Dragonriders attacked Kul Tiras's Third Fleet off the coast of the Wetlands, burning the ships and sending them to the ocean floor.",al={"who sunk the third fleet","why are ships wrecked wetlands","red dragons wetlands fleet"}},{q="Why is the chest nearly empty?",a="The waterlogged chest aboard the Flying Osprey bears fresh claw marks from coastal murlocs. The creatures pried it open and plundered the cargo, making off with most of the ingots and scattering them along the marshy shore.",al={"where are the ingots","why claw marks on chest","who stole the lightforge iron"}},{q="Where is the wreckage of the Flying Osprey located?",a="The wreckage lies among the coastal shoals just south of Menethil Harbor along the western shore of the Wetlands, split across the shallows near local murloc settlements.",al={"flying osprey location","where is the chest","wetlands shipwreck location"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Smiths of all disciplines revere Lightforge iron as a holy grail of materials, known for holding powerful blessings and retaining unmatched structural integrity.",["class:Paladin"]="Weapons wrought from Lightforge iron are deeply attuned to the Holy Light, making the recovery of even a single lost ingot of spiritual importance.",["faction:Alliance"]="The sunken vessels off Menethil Harbor are somber memorials to the Second War, where brave sailors from Kul Tiras and Lordaeron fell to dragonfire."},kw={"flying osprey","glorin steelbrow","ingot","kul tiras","lightforge iron","menethil harbor","murloc","third fleet","waterlogged chest","wetlands"},rel={"npc:glorin-steelbrow","quest:270","quest:324","quest:288","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:murloc","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Glorin Steelbrow",["end"]="Waterlogged Chest",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=321},src={"Lightforge Iron (quest)"}}
E["quest:324"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Ingots",z="wetlands",s="The Lost Ingots is an Alliance task in the Wetlands to recover consecrated metal from a shipwreck. After finding only a single bar in a sunken chest, travelers must hunt down the local Bluegill murlocs who looted the remaining shipment.",h="The Lost Ingots is an Alliance task in the Wetlands to recover consecrated metal from a shipwreck.",sec={{t="A Plundered Shipwreck",b="Off the misty shores of the Wetlands lies the shattered wreckage of the Flying Osprey. Sent to retrieve precious Lightforge iron for the dwarven priest Glorin Steelbrow, seekers discovered that the cargo hold's waterlogged chest was nearly empty. The ravenous local Bluegill murlocs had already scavenged the rest of the vessel, taking the gleaming ingots for themselves.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Sacred Metal",b="Lightforge iron is no ordinary ore; it is rare, specialized metal attuned to work sacred smithing craft. Allowing it to rot in murloc encampments is unthinkable for a dwarf of the Light. By hunting down the Bluegill raiders swarming the shallows near the broken hull, adventurers prise back the scattered bars so Glorin Steelbrow can see the iron hammered into a weapon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What ship carried the Lightforge iron?",a="The cargo arrived aboard the Flying Osprey, an unfortunate vessel that met its demise off the coast of the Wetlands. Its broken timbers now lie partially submerged in the shallows.",al={"which ship","flying osprey","shipwreck name"}},{q="Why were the ingots not in the chest?",a="Only a single ingot remained locked within the waterlogged chest. The coastal Bluegill murlocs had already pried into the sunken wreckage and scavenged the rest of the shipment to scatter among their coastal raiders.",al={"where are the ingots","why are murlocs holding iron","chest empty"}},{q="Who is Glorin Steelbrow?",a="Glorin Steelbrow is a dwarven priest of the Church of the Holy Light, found in the Deepwater Tavern in Menethil Harbor. A colleague of Bishop Farthing, he seeks Lightforge iron so a weapon can be forged against the necromancer Morbent Fel.",al={"glorin","who is glorin steelbrow","quest giver"}},{q="What is special about Lightforge iron?",a="Lightforge iron is a rare, sanctified metal uniquely receptive to holy enchantments and smithing. It is prized by artisans crafting armaments aligned with the Holy Light.",al={"lightforge iron lore","what is lightforge iron","why is the iron important"}},{q="Which murlocs took the iron?",a="The Bluegill tribe, specifically the murloc raiders that prowl the shallows and beaches around the wreckage of the Flying Osprey, seized the missing bars.",al={"who stole the ingots","which tribe","bluegill raiders"}},{q="What comes next after returning the ingots?",a="Once Glorin Steelbrow receives the full set of ingots, he packs the sanctified metal into a crate and sends you to the weaponsmith Grimand Elmore in Stormwind to have it forged, continuing in Blessed Arm.",al={"next quest","what does glorin do","blessed arm quest"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Recovering lost masterwork ore and putting it into the hands of a dwarven priest like Glorin Steelbrow honors the long tradition of dwarven craftsmanship and reclaimers.",["class:Paladin"]="Reclaiming Lightforge iron from primitive murlocs ensures holy materials are preserved to fashion consecrated weaponry fit to champion the Light.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Every metalworker knows the tragedy of seeing superior stock like Lightforge iron end up as curios in a coastal murloc nest instead of an anvil."},kw={"bluegill","flying osprey","glorin steelbrow","ingots","lightforge iron","murloc","waterlogged chest","wetlands"},rel={"quest:321","quest:322","npc:glorin-steelbrow","zone:wetlands","topic:murloc","topic:light"},m={start="Waterlogged Chest",["end"]="Glorin Steelbrow",level="29",faction="Alliance",id=324},src={"The Lost Ingots"}}
E["quest:463"] = {t="quest",n="The Greenwarden",z="wetlands",s="\"The Greenwarden\" is an Alliance breadcrumb quest directing travelers deeper into the marshes of the Wetlands. Sent by First Mate Fitzsimmons from Menethil Harbor, adventurers venture northeast into the swamp to seek out a mysterious entity rumored to dwell among the beasts.",h="\"The Greenwarden\" is an Alliance breadcrumb quest directing travelers deeper into the marshes of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Tavern Rumors and Bog Tales",b="Around the docks of Menethil Harbor, sailors and wanderers trade breathless stories of a beast lurking out in the swamp. First Mate Fitzsimmons paints the Greenwarden as an appetite with legs, warning gullible seekers that stepping off the dry road means being bitten in two by 'ol' Greenie.' To the dockside folk, anything massive lurking out in the murky waters is just another man-eating hazard of the marsh.",sp=0},{t="The Guardian of the Marsh",b="Those brave enough to heed the directions east of the fork toward Dun Modr find that the tavern tales missed the mark entirely. The Greenwarden is no mindless carnivore, but Rethiel, a towering ancient protector bound to the wild growth of the wetlands. Far from devouring wandering fools, Rethiel watches the sorrow of the spoiled land and enlists willing mortals to cleanse the blighted marsh.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Greenwarden?",a="The Greenwarden is Rethiel, an ancient nature guardian residing in the Wetlands. While coastal sailors think he is a savage monster, he is actually a wise protector attuned to the plants and wildlife.",al={"who is greenwarden","greenwarden identity","who is rethiel"}},{q="Where can I find the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is located in the marshlands east of the main road, near the fork that branches toward Dun Modr in the northern Wetlands.",al={"greenwarden location","where is rethiel","greenwarden coordinates"}},{q="Why does First Mate Fitzsimmons think the Greenwarden is dangerous?",a="Fitzsimmons only knows the tavern rumors and superstitions of Menethil Harbor. Because the Wetlands are overrun with beasts, sailors assume any giant entity dwelling among crocodiles and predators is simply another man-eating brute.",al={"why is fitzsimmons scared","is the greenwarden evil"}},{q="What does Rethiel want with travelers?",a="Rethiel seeks champions to tend to the Wetlands, which he describes as weeping from festered wounds. He directs visitors to protect the wildlife and quell threats destabilizing the local ecosystem.",al={"what does the greenwarden do","rethiel purpose","why meet the greenwarden"}},{q="What happens after finding the Greenwarden?",a="Once you speak with Rethiel, he acknowledges that nature speaks well of you and gives you the quest 'Tramping Paws' to help address the troubles afflicting the marsh.",al={"next quest after greenwarden","tramping paws quest"}},{q="Does this quest require fighting anything to complete?",a="No. The quest simply requires surviving the trek through the Wetlands and speaking directly with Rethiel at his grove in the marsh.",al={"greenwarden combat","do i fight greenwarden"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="While common dockworkers view Rethiel as a swamp monster, druids immediately recognize the presence of an ancient guardian attuned to the natural balance.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves traveling far from Kalimdor find a familiar, comforting echo of nature's ancient wardens residing even in the damp, muddy soils of Khaz Modan."},kw={"dun modr","fitzsimmons","greenwarden","menethil","rethiel","tramping paws","wetlands"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","quest:276","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr"},m={start="First Mate Fitzsimmons",["end"]="Rethiel the Greenwarden",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=463},src={"The Greenwarden"}}
E["quest:464"] = {t="quest",n="War Banners",z="wetlands",s="Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor tasks Alliance champions with striking an encampment of Dragonmaw orcs northeast of the town and claiming their war banners. The remnant orcs, broken and scattered after the Second War, have begun gathering strength once again in the bogs of the Wetlands.",h="Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor tasks Alliance champions with striking an encampment of Dragonmaw orcs...",sec={{t="Remnants of the Dragonmaw",b="During the Second War, the Dragonmaw clan subjugated the red dragonflight from the mountain fortress of Grim Batol. When their foul control broke, the liberated dragons turned upon their captors with ferocious vengeance, hunting the orcs nearly to extinction. What few survived fled Grim Batol into the high mountains east of Whelgar's Excavation, hidden away from the red flight's wrath.",sp=0},{t="A Rising Encampment",b="Though long believed broken beyond repair, the Dragonmaw have resurfaced. Northeast of Menethil Harbor, these savage survivors have raised an active war camp and planted their crimson standards in the marsh. Recognizing the danger of an aggressive orc force so close to the harbor town, Captain Stoutfist wants their ranks culled and their proud war banners torn down as proof of their defeat.",sp=0},{t="The Legacy of Nekros",b="Upon claiming the banners, Stoutfist reveals that these regrouped orcs are led by Nek'rosh, the son of the infamous warlock Nekros. Nekros had commanded the captive red dragons through dark sorcery until that magic collapsed, leaving him to be torn apart by his former captives. His vengeful son now commands the survivors, consumed by an obsessive vendetta against the great beasts that slew his father.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands?",a="They are remnants of an orc clan that enslaved the red dragonflight during the Second War. After losing their hold over the dragons, they were ruthlessly hunted and scattered, with survivors fleeing Grim Batol to hide in the mountains and marshes.",al={"dragonmaw orcs wetlands","who are dragonmaw","wetlands orcs"}},{q="Why does Captain Stoutfist want their war banners?",a="Stoutfist considers the newly fortified encampment northeast of Menethil Harbor a severe threat to the town. He demands their war banners as physical proof that Alliance soldiers have raided the camp and weakened their fighting strength.",al={"why collect banners","captain stoutfist banners"}},{q="What happened to the Dragonmaw clan's dragons?",a="When the dark magic holding the dragons captive failed, the red dragonflight turned on their captors. The dragons fiercely hunted down the Dragonmaw across Khaz Modan, utterly decimating the clan.",al={"what happened to the dragons","dragonmaw dragons"}},{q="Who leads the Dragonmaw clan now?",a="They are led by Nek'rosh, the son of the former Dragonmaw leader Nekros. Nek'rosh has rallied the survivors and sworn revenge against the red dragons who killed his father.",al={"dragonmaw leader","who is nek'rosh"},sp=1},{q="Where did the Dragonmaw hide before setting up this camp?",a="After fleeing Grim Batol, the surviving orcs hid in the rugged mountains east of Whelgar's Excavation before venturing into the Wetlands marsh to construct their encampment.",al={"where did dragonmaw hide","dragonmaw refuge"}},{q="Are these Dragonmaw orcs affiliated with Thrall's Horde?",a="No. These Dragonmaw remnants are independent renegades driven by vengeance and survival, operating completely outside of the new Horde founded by Warchief Thrall in Kalimdor.",al={"are dragonmaw in horde","dragonmaw thrall horde"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor serves as the vital lifeline between Stormwind, Ironforge, and the northern realms; allowing a hostile orc encampment to dig in nearby endangers the entire shipping corridor.",["race:Dwarf"]="The Dragonmaw desecrated the ancient dwarven stronghold of Grim Batol and stained the surrounding mountains with war, making every dead Dragonmaw warrior a measure of long-delayed justice.",["class:Warrior"]="Striking the war camp directly tests your mettle against hardened Second War veterans who fight with reckless ferocity, even stripped of their draconic mounts."},kw={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw","grim batol","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","nekros","war banners","wetlands"},rel={"npc:captain-stoutfist","quest:465","quest:473","subzone:grim-batol","zone:wetlands","topic:second-war"},m={start="Captain Stoutfist",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=464},src={"War Banners"}}
E["quest:465"] = {t="quest",n="Nek'rosh's Gambit",z="wetlands",s="Nek'rosh's Gambit is an urgent strike mission commissioned by Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor. Learning that Chieftain Nek'rosh has constructed siege engines to bombard the vulnerable port town while reinforcements remain cut off at Dun Algaz, the Alliance sends brave volunteers deep into the marshes to burn the Dragonmaw catapults before an assault can begin.",h="Nek'rosh's Gambit is an urgent strike mission commissioned by Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Looming Siege",b="While Alliance adventurers were clashing with Dragonmaw raiding parties, dwarven scouts uncovered the clan's true ambition. Chieftain Nek'rosh has overseen the construction of full-scale siege catapults in the wetlands encampments. His goal is bold and catastrophic: to march his war engines to Menethil Harbor and batter down the fortress walls, wiping out the Alliance's primary shipping hub on the western coast.",sp=0},{t="Cut Off at Dun Algaz",b="Menethil Harbor's peril is magnified by the choke point at Dun Algaz. Heavy skirmishes and greenskin activity in the mountain pass effectively isolate the lowlands from Ironforge's main garrisons. Without immediate aid from Khaz Modan, Captain Stoutfist cannot spare a defensive detachment to guard the perimeter, making a preemptive sabotage of the catapults the harbor's sole chance for survival.",sp=0},{t="Fire in the Encampment",b="Armed with Dwarven Tinder, scouts must push directly into the heart of the Dragonmaw encampment. Setting the bulky timber engines ablaze robs Nek'rosh of his artillery, leaving his warriors exposed and denying them the firepower needed to crack Menethil's defenses before the warlord himself can be confronted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nek'rosh?",a="Nek'rosh is the ruthless chieftain leading the remnants of the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. He is orchestrating a direct military campaign to besiege Menethil Harbor.",al={"nekrosh","chieftain nek'rosh","who is nek rosh"}},{q="Why is Menethil Harbor in such danger?",a="The town relies heavily on naval trade and is physically separated from Ironforge. Because the passes at Dun Algaz are congested with fighting, no reinforcements can arrive by land, leaving the town unable to withstand a concentrated siege.",al={"menethil danger","why harbor vulnerable","threat to menethil"}},{q="What is the goal of this mission?",a="You are tasked with taking Dwarven Tinder into the Dragonmaw encampment to ignite and destroy their siege catapults before they can be rolled out against Menethil Harbor.",al={"gambit objective","what do i do","catapult mission"}},{q="Who issues this assignment?",a="Captain Stoutfist, the dwarf officer coordinating the harbor's local defense and the campaign against the Dragonmaw, hands down the orders.",al={"quest giver","who gives nekrosh gambit","stoutfist role"}},{q="What follows the destruction of the catapults?",a="Once their siege engines are reduced to ash, the threat must be extinguished permanently by tracking down and executing Chieftain Nek'rosh himself.",al={"after catapults","next quest","what next"},sp=1},{q="Why can't Ironforge send troops to help Menethil?",a="The road linking Loch Modan to the Wetlands runs through Dun Algaz, which is heavily contested and ambushed by hostile forces, severing reliable ground transit.",al={"dun algaz block","why no reinforcements","ironforge help"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Menethil Harbor serves as Bronzebeard dwarfdom's gateway to the western sea; losing it to Dragonmaw siege weapons would cripple Ironforge's maritime connections.",["faction:Alliance"]="With Dun Algaz locked down in combat, the Alliance must rely on brave volunteers rather than standing armies to disrupt the Dragonmaw war machine.",["class:Warrior"]="Storming an entrenched enemy war camp to destroy heavy siege artillery requires aggressive frontline tactics and brutal hand-to-hand fighting."},kw={"captain stoutfist","catapults","dragonmaw","dun algaz","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","nek'rosh's gambit","wetlands"},rel={"quest:464","quest:474","npc:captain-stoutfist","subzone:dun-algaz","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Captain Stoutfist",["end"]="Dragonmaw Catapult",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=465},src={"Nek'rosh's Gambit"}}
E["quest:469"] = {t="quest",n="Daily Delivery",z="wetlands",s="Daily Delivery is an errand on behalf of the dwarven hunter Einar Stonegrip, who asks travelers heading toward Menethil Harbor to deliver cured crocolisk hides to the local tanner. Rather than facing domestic friction at home, Einar relies on passing adventurers to keep his supply line moving.",h="Daily Delivery is an errand on behalf of the dwarven hunter Einar Stonegrip, who asks travelers heading...",sec={{t="A Reluctant Courier",b="Out in the marshlands, Einar Stonegrip makes his living hunting the local wildlife, particularly the aggressive crocolisks that lurk along the waterways. While he gathers plenty of valuable skins, delivering them requires a trip home to Menethil Harbor. Reluctant to confront his wife Sida during a rough patch in their marriage, Einar prefers to stay in the field and hand his parcels off to passing travelers instead.",sp=0},{t="Commerce in Menethil",b="The destination for these hides is James Halloran, a tanner operating within Menethil Harbor. Halloran relies on regular deliveries from local hunters to craft boots and cure leather for merchants and sailors passing through the port. Having noticed Einar's week-long absence, the tanner easily deduces the marital spat behind the proxy delivery, musing that his own wife might need to intervene and smooth things over with Sida.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why doesn't Einar Stonegrip deliver the skins himself?",a="Einar admits that his wife, Sida, has been in foul humor lately. To avoid facing her temper, he lingers out in the Wetlands and hires passing travelers to run his deliveries into town.",al={"why einar hiding","einar wife problem","why won't einar go home"}},{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a tanner and leather crafter stationed in Menethil Harbor. He buys raw pelts and hides from local trappers to cure and sell as boots and finished leather goods.",al={"halloran tanner","who is james halloran"}},{q="Who is Sida?",a="Sida is Einar Stonegrip's wife, residing in Menethil Harbor. Her recent sour mood is the primary reason Einar spends his days out in the marshes avoiding coming home.",al={"einar wife","who is sida"}},{q="What kind of skins are being transported?",a="The delivery consists of a bundle of crocolisk skins, harvested from the large reptiles that infest the bogs and waterways of the Wetlands.",al={"what skins","daily delivery items"}},{q="Does Halloran know why Einar is avoiding Menethil Harbor?",a="Yes. When you hand over the bundle, Halloran remarks that Einar has not visited in nearly a week and immediately guesses that trouble with Sida is the cause.",al={"does halloran know","tanner reaction"}},{q="Where does this delivery take place?",a="The delivery begins with Einar Stonegrip out along the road in the Wetlands and finishes at James Halloran's workshop in Menethil Harbor on the western coast.",al={"where turn in","daily delivery location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor serves as the primary maritime gateway connecting Ironforge's domain to the northern continents, making basic trade goods like crocolisk leather vital for outfitting local guards and dockhands.",["race:Dwarf"]="Even far from Ironforge, dwarves make their trade in the wet lowlands, though domestic disputes apparently prove harder to face than marsh beasts."},kw={"crocolisk skins","einar stonegrip","james halloran","menethil harbor","sida","tanner","wetlands"},rel={"npc:einar-stonegrip","npc:james-halloran","npc:sida","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Einar Stonegrip",["end"]="James Halloran",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=469},src={"Daily Delivery"}}
E["quest:470"] = {t="quest",n="Digging Through the Ooze",z="wetlands",s="While paying her regular respects at Ironbeard's Tomb, Sida was startled by the foul oozes prowling the barrows and threw her bag to distract them. Unable to face the creeping sludge again, she asks brave adventurers in Menethil Harbor to track down the creature that swallowed her belongings.",h="While paying her regular respects at Ironbeard's Tomb, Sida was startled by the foul oozes prowling the...",sec={{t="A Panicked Retreat",b="Sida, a traveler residing in Menethil Harbor, regularly ventures northeast into the Wetlands to pay homage at Ironbeard's Tomb. On her latest visit, she found the ancient barrow crawling with foul, dripping oozes. Panicking at the sight of the shapeless horrors, she hurled her satchel at one of them. The creature simply engulfed the bag whole, though the distraction gave Sida just enough time to flee back to the safety of the port town.",sp=0},{t="Sludge of Ironbeard's Tomb",b="The burial site of the storied dwarven hero Ironbeard rests near the contested stronghold of Dun Modr. Despite its historical reverence, the surrounding marshland is prone to corruption, drawing amorphous acidic slimes that consume anything unfortunate enough to cross their path. Sida cannot remember which specific monstrosity swallowed her prized belongings, leaving travelers to scour the tomb grounds and carve through the creeping blight to recover her drenched satchel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Sida?",a="Sida is an Alliance traveler located in Menethil Harbor. She makes regular pilgrimages out into the Wetlands to visit Ironbeard's Tomb, a habit that recently landed her in serious danger when hostile oozes ambushed her.",al={"sida","who gives quest","who is sida"}},{q="Where is Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Ironbeard's Tomb is located in the northeastern reaches of the Wetlands, south of Dun Modr. The area around the stone barrow has become infested with corrosive wetland oozes.",al={"ironbeard tomb location","where is ironbeard","where are the oozes"}},{q="Which ooze swallowed Sida's bag?",a="Sida panicked during the attack and cannot tell the creatures apart. Any of the wandering slimes lurking outside Ironbeard's Tomb could be the one harboring her digested belongings.",al={"which ooze","ooze with bag","where is the bag"}},{q="Why was Sida visiting Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Sida makes a weekly visit to the tomb to pay respects to the ancient dwarf buried there, though her peaceful tradition was cut short by the unexpected presence of the oozes.",al={"why sida visit tomb","sida weekly visit"}},{q="What happens after the bag is recovered?",a="Upon returning the slimy satchel to Menethil Harbor, Sida dumps its contents out onto the ground to retrieve her personal items. Finding the ruined container itself too repulsive to keep, she offers the cleaned-off bag to the adventurer who recovered it.",al={"what was in the bag","bag reward"},sp=1},{q="Is this related to the Dark Iron dwarves nearby?",a="While Dun Modr just to the north is embroiled in conflict with the Dark Iron clan, the slimes infesting Ironbeard's Tomb are wild marsh predators native to the damp, rotting corners of the Wetlands rather than dwarven soldiers.",al={"dark iron connection","dun modr connection"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Ironbeard's Tomb holds the remains of an honored dwarven ancestor, making the defilement of the barrows by foul oozes an affront to any Bronzebeard loyalist.",["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor serves as the Alliance's primary lifeline through the treacherous Wetlands, and aiding rattled citizens keeps the vital port secure and orderly."},kw={"dun modr","ironbeard's tomb","menethil harbor","ooze","ooze-covered bag","sida","sida's bag","wetlands"},rel={"npc:sida","subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr"},m={start="Sida",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=470},src={"Digging Through the Ooze"}}
E["quest:471"] = {t="quest",n="Apprentice's Duties",z="wetlands",s="Apprentice's Duties is an Alliance contract offered by tanner James Halloran in Menethil Harbor. After sending his young apprentice into the marshes only for the boy to be mauled by giant crocolisks, Halloran hires a capable adventurer to finish the dangerous harvesting job and settle the score.",h="Apprentice's Duties is an Alliance contract offered by tanner James Halloran in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Harsh Apprenticeship",b="Tradesmen in frontier ports like Menethil Harbor must rely on local raw materials, but the surrounding bogs are unforgiving. James Halloran sent his young apprentice into the marshes to skin giant Wetlands crocolisks. When the youth failed to return, Halloran tracked him down and found him horribly mauled by the predatory beasts.",sp=0},{t="Skins and Retribution",b="Although the local midwife believes the apprentice will survive, the boy was maimed and lost a leg in the attack. Needing his stock replenished and seeking a measure of retribution against the beasts that tore into someone he considers like a son, Halloran enlists traveling adventurers to venture north along the coast, clear past the murloc hovels, and hunt down the giant crocolisks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a leatherworker and tanner based in Menethil Harbor. He relies on hides gathered from the local wildlife across the Wetlands to sustain his craft.",al={"james halloran","who gives apprentice duties","menethil tanner"}},{q="What happened to Halloran's apprentice?",a="Halloran dispatched his apprentice into the marsh to harvest hides from giant crocolisks. The boy was attacked by the predators and mauled severely, ultimately losing a leg, though the town midwife expects him to survive.",al={"what happened to apprentice","who got mauled","apprentice leg"}},{q="Where are the giant crocolisks located?",a="The giant crocolisks prowl the marshes and northern coast of the Wetlands, just beyond the coastal murloc settlements north of Menethil Harbor.",al={"where are giant crocs","crocolisk location wetlands","giant crocolisk spot"}},{q="What prerequisite quest leads to this task?",a="This quest is preceded by 'Young Crocolisk Skins,' where Halloran first has adventurers hunt smaller crocolisks before escalating to the giant variety that wounded his apprentice.",al={"prereq for apprentice duties","previous quest","crocolisk quest chain"}},{q="Why does Halloran still want the skins after the tragedy?",a="Halloran still has a trade to run and orders to fill, but he is also motivated by anger. He welcomes having an adventurer hunt and kill the beasts responsible for maiming the boy he loves like a son.",al={"why need skins","halloran motivation"}},{q="Does Halloran offer you an apprenticeship?",a="Halloran briefly jokes about taking you on as his new apprentice after seeing your work, but dismisses the idea immediately, noting you are far too old and clearly bound for a different destiny.",al={"can i become apprentice","apprentice offer"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor serves as a lifeline between Khaz Modan and the rest of the Alliance, making the safety and self-sufficiency of its local craftsmen vital to the port's survival.",["class:Hunter"]="The marshland apex predators are formidable targets, and tracking down mature giant crocolisks tests a tracker's ability to navigate murky waters and aggressive wildlife."},kw={"apprentice's duties","crocolisk","giant crocolisk","james halloran","leatherworking","menethil harbor","murloc hovels","wetlands","young crocolisk skins"},rel={"npc:james-halloran","quest:484","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","topic:murloc"},m={start="James Halloran",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=471},src={"Apprentice's Duties"}}
E["quest:472"] = {t="quest",n="Fall of Dun Modr",z="wetlands",s="Dun Modr, the northern dwarf fortress overlooking the Thandol Span, has succumbed to a violent assault by the Dark Iron dwarves. A severely wounded survivor in Menethil Harbor seeks an Alliance adventurer to venture north and discover if commander Longbraid the Grim and any remnant of the garrison survived.",h="Dun Modr, the northern dwarf fortress overlooking the Thandol Span, has succumbed to a violent assault by the...",sec={{t="A Northern Bulwark Broken",b="Dun Modr has long anchored northern Khaz Modan, guarding the vital road and bridge connecting the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands across the Thandol Span. Following an ambush at the bridge itself, the garrison scrambled back to regroup within the fortress walls. Before defensive lines could be reestablished, Dark Iron forces struck in overwhelming numbers, slaughtering the defenders and forcing a desperate evacuation.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Flight",b="Harlo Barnaby, a young soldier among the defenders, fell gravely injured when a stray axe struck his back during the chaotic retreat. Believing his wounds fatal, Longbraid the Grim and the remaining troops strapped Barnaby to their last surviving horse and dispatched him south to Menethil Harbor. Barnaby survived the ordeal, but awoke in the harbor tavern racked by survivor's guilt, entirely unaware of whether any of his comrades made it out of the massacre alive.",sp=0},{t="The Grim Remnant",b="Deep in the northern marshes near the captured fortress, Longbraid the Grim still lives, holding together a battered handful of survivors. Though relieved to learn that young Harlo survived his grievous wound, the veteran commander faces a dire tactical reality: Dun Modr is firmly under Dark Iron control, its halls occupied by cutthroats and saboteurs who threaten the entire corridor between Khaz Modan and the human lands to the north.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr was overrun and captured by hostile Dark Iron dwarves. The garrison had already suffered an ambush at the nearby Thandol Span, and before they could consolidate their defenses inside the town, the Dark Irons assaulted and wiped out most of the defending regiment.",al={"why is dun modr destroyed","who attacked dun modr","dun modr lore"}},{q="Who is Harlo Barnaby?",a="Harlo Barnaby is an Ironforge soldier stationed at Dun Modr who barely survived its fall. Struck in the back by a thrown axe during the retreat, he was strapped to the garrison's sole surviving horse by his commander and sent south to Menethil Harbor to receive medical care.",al={"who is harlo","harlo barnaby lore","wounded soldier in menethil"}},{q="Where is Longbraid the Grim located?",a="Commander Longbraid the Grim took refuge in the wilderness just outside the occupied town of Dun Modr, near the northern highway leading up toward the Thandol Span.",al={"where is longbraid","longbraid location","find longbraid"},sp=1},{q="Why is Dun Modr strategically important?",a="Dun Modr stands as the northernmost settlement and fortification in the Wetlands. It guards the southern approach to the Thandol Span, the only terrestrial bridge that links Khaz Modan with the Arathi Highlands and Lordaeron.",al={"why care about dun modr","thandol span connection"}},{q="Who are the attackers at Dun Modr?",a="The attackers are Dark Iron dwarves, members of the treacherous clan from the south who have pushed north into the Wetlands to destroy infrastructure like the Thandol Span and harass Ironforge's territory.",al={"who took dun modr","dark irons in wetlands"}},{q="What happens after finding Longbraid?",a="Once you confirm Longbraid is alive and deliver news of Barnaby's survival, Longbraid enlists you in a grim mission of vengeance and retribution against the Dark Iron forces occupying the ruins of Dun Modr.",al={"fall of dun modr follow up","what comes after fall of dun modr"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The slaughter of Ironforge mountaineers and the desecration of Dun Modr by clan kin from the south is a bitter, personal insult that demands blood in return.",["faction:Alliance"]="The fall of Dun Modr severs safe overland transit between Ironforge and the northern Alliance operations in the Arathi Highlands, leaving the northern corridor vulnerable to sabotage."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","harlo barnaby","longbraid the grim","menethil harbor","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"npc:harlo-barnaby","npc:longbraid-the-grim","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","quest:304","quest:631","zone:wetlands"},m={start="Harlo Barnaby",["end"]="Longbraid the Grim",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=472},src={"Fall of Dun Modr"}}
E["quest:473"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Captain Stoutfist",z="wetlands",s="Report to Captain Stoutfist is an Alliance military directive in Menethil Harbor. Following initial skirmishes against the Dragonmaw clan at Dun Algaz, Mountaineer Valstag Ironjaw sends proven combatants inside the harbor's keep to coordinate deeper defense efforts. Captain Stoutfist commands the local garrison and is organizing direct strikes against the entrenched orcs across the Wetlands.",h="Report to Captain Stoutfist is an Alliance military directive in Menethil Harbor.",sec={{t="A Widening Threat",b="While dwarven mountaineers have long monitored the narrow mountain passes of Dun Algaz, the resurgence of the Dragonmaw clan cannot be contained to the borders of Loch Modan alone. Valstag Ironjaw recognizes that these orcs are pressing outward, establishing encampments and threatening the entirety of the marshlands. Securing the pass is merely the opening move in a larger campaign to safeguard the road to Ironforge.",sp=0},{t="The War Room of Menethil",b="Deep inside Menethil Keep sits the war room, where Captain Stoutfist oversees the defenses of the Alliance port. Facing attacks from Dark Iron saboteurs, local beasts, and marsh murlocs, the captain relies on capable volunteers to counter external military threats. Valstag's recommendation confirms that you are hardened enough to take on direct orders against the Dragonmaw war machine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to Captain Stoutfist?",a="Valstag Ironjaw, stationed in Menethil Keep in Menethil Harbor, sends you to report to Captain Stoutfist after you prove yourself in battle against the local Dragonmaw orcs.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","valstag ironjaw"}},{q="Where is Captain Stoutfist located?",a="Captain Stoutfist is inside Menethil Keep, located at the heart of Menethil Harbor in the western Wetlands. He can be found standing over tactical maps within the keep's war room.",al={"captain stoutfist location","where is stoutfist","menethil war room"}},{q="Why are the Dragonmaw orcs a priority for Menethil Keep?",a="The Dragonmaw clan holds ancient strongholds throughout the Wetlands and poses an aggressive threat to the trade roads connecting Menethil Harbor with Ironforge. With their forces pressing beyond Dun Algaz, the garrison cannot ignore their growing encampments.",al={"why fight dragonmaw","dragonmaw threat","orcs in wetlands"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Captain Stoutfist?",a="Once you report to Captain Stoutfist, he enlists you directly into the offensive against the Dragonmaw clan, dispatching you to target their encampments and strike down their war banners in the marsh.",al={"what next","followup quest","after report to stoutfist"}},{q="Who are the Dragonmaw orcs in the Wetlands?",a="The Dragonmaw are remnants of the old Horde who famously enslaved red dragons at Grim Batol during the Second War. Though Grim Batol was broken, surviving warbands remain entrenched across the marshlands, raiding travelers and defying Alliance authority.",al={"dragonmaw lore","who are dragonmaw","wetlands orcs"}},{q="Why is Menethil Harbor stretched so thin?",a="Menethil Harbor contends with constant marsh wildlife, encroaching murlocs, and hostile Dark Iron dwarves attempting to undermine the port. With garrison forces occupied defending the walls and docks, Captain Stoutfist relies on outside champions to strike distant orc outposts.",al={"menethil defense","why are troops busy","harbor problems"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Defending the trade line between Menethil Harbor and the gates of Ironforge is vital to the security of Khaz Modan, making this assignment essential dwarf business.",["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor serves as the primary gateway for storming goods and reinforcements between the southern kingdoms and Khaz Modan; losing the road to orc raiding parties would cripple Alliance trade.",["class:Warrior"]="Valstag Ironjaw recognizes raw combat prowess, dispatching seasoned front-line fighters directly to Captain Stoutfist's tactical command."},kw={"captain stoutfist","dragonmaw","dun algaz","menethil harbor","menethil keep","valstag ironjaw","war room","wetlands"},rel={"npc:captain-stoutfist","npc:valstag-ironjaw","quest:464","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-algaz","subzone:war-room"},m={start="Valstag Ironjaw",["end"]="Captain Stoutfist",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=473},src={"Report to Captain Stoutfist"}}
E["quest:474"] = {t="quest",n="Defeat Nek'rosh",z="wetlands",s="Defeat Nek'rosh marks the culmination of the Alliance campaign against the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. With their siege engines sabotaged, adventurers are ordered to strike down Chieftain Nek'rosh directly to secure Menethil Harbor. Bringing his severed head back to Captain Stoutfist shatters the orcish threat to the coastal port.",h="Defeat Nek'rosh marks the culmination of the Alliance campaign against the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Decapitating the Dragonmaw",b="The Dragonmaw orcs have long plagued the marshlands of Khaz Modan, entrenched within their fortified encampments and threatening the sea lanes of Menethil Harbor. After discovering and burning the clan's catapults, the defenders of the marsh strike straight at the head of the serpent. Chieftain Nek'rosh, commander of the local warband, stands as the final obstacle to breaking the siege. His demise strips the remaining Dragonmaw raiders of their tactical coordination.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Harbor",b="Returning Nek'rosh's severed head to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Harbor marks an enormous victory for Ironforge's garrison. Deprived of both their heavy siege weaponry and their chieftain, the Dragonmaw are dealt a blow from which they are unlikely to quickly recover. For the beleaguered port, which serves as the Alliance's primary lifeline between Lordaeron and Khaz Modan, the chieftain's fall ensures the docks and trade vessels remain safe from sudden assault.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Nek'rosh?",a="Nek'rosh is the ruthless chieftain leading the remnants of the Dragonmaw clan in the Wetlands. Operating out of their encampments, he organized a planned assault on Menethil Harbor using siege catapults before Alliance adventurers intervened.",al={"chieftain nek'rosh","who is nekrosh","nekrosh wetlands"}},{q="Why does Menethil Harbor want Nek'rosh dead?",a="Nek'rosh posed a direct existential threat to Menethil Harbor. Under his command, the Dragonmaw constructed war catapults aimed at bombarding the port and crippling the vital shipping lanes connecting Khaz Modan to other Alliance territories.",al={"why kill nekrosh","captain stoutfist motives"}},{q="Who orders the death of Nek'rosh?",a="The command arises directly after setting fire to the Dragonmaw catapults. The severed head of the chieftain is ultimately delivered to Captain Stoutfist, the commander overseeing the defense of Menethil Harbor.",al={"who gives defeat nekrosh","where to turn in nekrosh head"}},{q="What happens to the Dragonmaw clan after Nek'rosh is defeated?",a="With their catapults destroyed and their chieftain slain, the Dragonmaw warband suffers a crippling loss of leadership and morale. While stragglers still haunt the marshlands, their immediate campaign against Menethil Harbor is effectively crushed.",al={"dragonmaw after nekrosh","what happens to wetlands orcs"},sp=1},{q="What is the Dragonmaw clan doing in the Wetlands?",a="The Dragonmaw clan settled in the Wetlands and the adjacent highlands of Grim Batol during the Second War. Following the Horde's defeat, renegade remnants lingered in the swamps, raiding trade routes and harboring deep hatred for the Alliance and the dwarves of Khaz Modan.",al={"why are dragonmaw in wetlands","dragonmaw wetlands lore"}},{q="Why is Menethil Harbor so crucial to the Alliance?",a="Menethil Harbor is the kingdom of Ironforge's sole major seaport on the western coast. It serves as the primary hub for ferrying troops, trade goods, and travelers across the Great Sea to Kalimdor and north toward Lordaeron.",al={"importance of menethil","menethil harbor strategic value"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the dwarves of Khaz Modan, the Dragonmaw are a lingering scar upon their ancestral borders. Eliminating Nek'rosh directly safeguards dwarven roads and Ironforge's western sea trade.",["faction:Alliance"]="Securing Menethil Harbor protects the primary naval artery linking Ironforge and Stormwind to Kalimdor and the northern waters.",["class:Warrior"]="Facing Chieftain Nek'rosh within his own fortified war camp offers an ultimate test of martial grit against one of the marsh's fiercest orc commanders."},kw={"captain stoutfist","catapult","chieftain","dragonmaw","ironforge","menethil harbor","nek'rosh","wetlands"},rel={"quest:465","npc:captain-stoutfist","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Dragonmaw Catapult",["end"]="Captain Stoutfist",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=474},src={"Defeat Nek'rosh"}}
E["quest:484"] = {t="quest",n="Young Crocolisk Skins",z="wetlands",s="James Halloran, a prominent tanner based in Menethil Harbor, contracts travelers to supply fresh skins from the marsh's juvenile crocolisks. His cured hides enjoy international maritime demand, making reliable hunting essential to his trade. Supplying these softer materials earns his trust and opens the way to further leatherworking chores.",h="James Halloran, a prominent tanner based in Menethil Harbor, contracts travelers to supply fresh skins from...",sec={{t="A Harbor's Export",b="Menethil Harbor is an essential maritime hub connecting the Eastern Kingdoms to distant continents, but it also supports a bustling local economy built around the resources of the surrounding marshland. James Halloran has established an international trade by tanning and curing the tough hides of the region's abundant reptilian predators. Merchants and ships sailing out of Menethil carry Halloran's leather goods to distant ports, creating constant pressure on his workshop to maintain a steady inventory.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Young Marsh Lurkers",b="While veteran trappers like Einar provide regular hauls of mature hides, tanning specialized luxury goods requires far softer leather than fully grown marsh crocolisks can yield. To fill this shortage, Halloran relies on passing adventurers to wade into the shallow bogs right outside Menethil's palisades. Sourcing intact skins from juvenile beasts requires careful hunting, ensuring the hides remain intact enough to endure Halloran's meticulous curing process.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is James Halloran?",a="James Halloran is a master tanner operating in Menethil Harbor. His cured crocolisk skins are famed across the world and regularly shipped out across the Great Sea to foreign ports.",al={"james halloran lore","who is the tanner","halloran menethil"}},{q="Why does Halloran need young crocolisk skins specifically?",a="While adult crocolisks yield durable, heavy armor-grade leather, juvenile crocolisks have much softer and more pliable hides. These delicate skins are vital for specific luxury goods and fine leatherwork that adult hides are too rigid to produce.",al={"why young crocs","softer skins","crocolisk hides use"}},{q="Who is Einar?",a="Einar is a local hunter stationed in the Wetlands who works directly with James Halloran. He regularly treks into the marshes to cull wild crocolisks and supply the harbor workshop with raw skins.",al={"einar wetlands","hunter einar","einar lore"}},{q="Where are these young crocolisks found?",a="Young crocolisks inhabit the waterways, reeds, and marshy shallows immediately surrounding Menethil Harbor, just beyond the town gates and docks.",al={"croc locations","where are the young crocs","wetlands young crocs"}},{q="What happens after bringing the skins to Halloran?",a="Impressed by the quality of the hides, Halloran immediately asks for assistance handling other chores around his tanning operation, delegating typical apprentice tasks to help keep his workshop moving.",al={"quest followup","next quest after young crocolisk skins","halloran next task"}},{q="Why is crocolisk leather valuable in Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor serves as a bustling trading port connecting Ironforge and Stormwind to overseas territories like Kalimdor. Exotic waterproof marsh skins cured by skilled artisans find high value among merchants and sailors docking in town.",al={"menethil leather trade","crocolisk skin value"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For hunters passing through the Wetlands, Halloran's request is routine field work, harvesting clean hides from native predators without spoiling the leather.",["faction:Alliance"]="Supporting the maritime commerce of Menethil Harbor keeps vital supply lines and trade exports flowing smoothly across the Great Sea."},kw={"crocolisk","einar","james halloran","leather","menethil harbor","skins","tanning","wetlands"},rel={"npc:james-halloran","quest:471","subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands"},m={start="James Halloran",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=484},src={"Young Crocolisk Skins"}}
E["quest:631"] = {t="quest",n="The Thandol Span",z="wetlands",s="Following a devastating explosion that rocked northern Wetlands, Rhag Garmason asks travelers to search the ruined bridges of the Thandol Span for a missing dwarf scout. The Dark Iron clan has launched a brutal assault against Dun Modr, cutting off communication and leaving local defenders stranded without reinforcements. Finding Ol' Rustlocke is the first step toward uncovering the full scale of the sabotage.",h="Following a devastating explosion that rocked northern Wetlands, Rhag Garmason asks travelers to search the...",sec={{t="Thunder Over the Span",b="A catastrophic blast recently tore through the Thandol Span, shattering the massive stone bridge connecting the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands. Bronzebeard soldiers stationed at the border were caught in the devastation as Dark Iron dwarves ambushed Dun Modr. With their ranks thinned and their strongholds besieged, the survivors under Commander Longbraid have been forced into a desperate defensive holdout against the attackers.",sp=0},{t="A Scout Sent East",b="Hoping to salvage a crossing and determine whether any path northward remains usable, Longbraid dispatched the veteran scout Ebenezer Rustlocke to inspect the eastern span. Days passed without a single report, but with Dun Modr actively under siege, Rhag Garmason and the garrison lack the soldiers to launch a rescue expedition into enemy-controlled rubble.",sp=0},{t="Grim Discovery",b="Venturing out onto the shattered span reveals the cost of the Dark Iron assault. Far from returning with reconnaissance, Ol' Rustlocke was slain amidst the debris of the eastern bridge. His recovered body and belongings confirm the worst: the crossing is entirely compromised, and the Dark Irons are actively fortifying their hold on the vital artery between Khaz Modan and Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Thandol Span?",a="The Thandol Span is a colossal dwarven bridge structure that spans the chasm between the northern Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. It serves as the primary land route connecting Khaz Modan to the northern lands of Lordaeron.",al={"thandol span","what is thandol bridge","wetlands bridge"}},{q="Who attacked the Thandol Span?",a="The Dark Iron dwarf clan attacked the bridge and the nearby outpost of Dun Modr. They detonated explosives to sever the span, crippling Alliance transit and catching the Bronzebeard defenders off guard.",al={"who blew up the bridge","thandol span explosion","who attacked dun modr"}},{q="Who is Ol' Rustlocke?",a="Ebenezer Rustlocke was a trusted dwarven scout serving Commander Longbraid. He was sent to assess the condition of the eastern bridge following the explosion, but he was overwhelmed and killed by Dark Iron forces during his mission.",al={"ebenezer rustlocke","who is rustlocke","missing scout"},sp=1},{q="Where is Rhag Garmason located?",a="Rhag Garmason is stationed near the beleaguered settlement of Dun Modr, just south of the Thandol Span in northern Wetlands. He helps coordinate defense efforts while the garrison is cut off from Ironforge.",al={"rhag garmason location","where is rhag","quest giver dun modr"}},{q="Why hasn't Ironforge sent help to Dun Modr?",a="The suddenness of the attack, combined with the destruction of the bridge and the siege of Dun Modr, has left the garrison isolated. The defenders are stretched too thin to send couriers or divert troops, leaving them dependent on passing adventurers to deliver word.",al={"why no reinforcements","ironforge help wetlands","dun modr reinforcement"}},{q="What happens after finding Rustlocke's corpse?",a="Investigating Rustlocke's remains reveals notes and supplies detailing the extent of the Dark Iron sabotage. This begins an effort to disrupt the Dark Iron demolition operations on the bridge and ultimately seek broader aid through a plea to the Alliance leadership.",al={"next quest after rustlocke","thandol span continuation","after the thandol span"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The destruction of the Thandol Span is an affront to dwarven stonework and a direct strike against Khaz Modan by their hated Dark Iron kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Thandol Span is the sole overland supply corridor linking Stormwind and Ironforge to Alliance forces holding out in Arathi and Hillsbrad."},kw={"dark iron","dun modr","garmason","longbraid","rustlocke","span","thandol","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-modr","quest:634","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Rhag Garmason",["end"]="Ebenezer Rustlocke's Corpse",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=631},src={"The Thandol Span"}}
E["quest:632"] = {t="quest",n="The Thandol Span",z="wetlands",s="Rhag Garmason tasks adventurers with checking on Ol' Ebenezer Rustlocke, a scout sent to inspect the massive stone crossing of the Thandol Span after contact with him is lost. Investigating beneath the arches of the crossing reveals the circumstances surrounding his disappearance and threats to the northern supply lines.",h="Rhag Garmason tasks adventurers with checking on Ol' Ebenezer Rustlocke, a scout sent to inspect the massive...",sec={{t="A Scout's Final Stand",b="Commander Longbraid originally sent Ebenezer Rustlocke to keep watch over the structural integrity and security of the Thandol Span. When contact with the scout ceased, foul play was immediately feared. Exploring the recesses beneath the arches reveals Rustlocke lying dead, having succumbed to a vicious ambush sprung from the shadows by Dark Iron invaders.",sp=0},{t="Deepfury's Orders",b="Pried from the vicinity of Rustlocke's clenched fingers is a set of written orders bearing the name Deepfury. Far from a random robbery or isolated border skirmish, the parchment outlines deliberate Dark Iron operations aimed at destabilizing the crossing. Delivering this evidence back to Garmason shifts the garrison's posture from a routine search to an urgent wartime defense.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Ebenezer Rustlocke?",a="Ebenezer 'Ol' Rustlocke was an Alliance dwarf dispatched to scout and maintain watch over the Thandol Span. He was caught off guard and slain by Dark Iron dwarves prowling beneath the bridge.",al={"who is rustlocke","ol rustlocke","ebenezer rustlocke"},sp=1},{q="Who killed Rustlocke?",a="He was ambushed by Dark Iron operatives operating beneath the Thandol Span, carrying out directives issued by Kam Deepfury.",al={"who killed rustlocke","who ambushed rustlocke","rustlocke corpse"},sp=1},{q="What is found on Rustlocke's body?",a="Beside his clenched fist lies a parchment containing Deepfury's Orders, documenting covert Dark Iron plots against the vital northern bridge.",al={"what was in his hand","deepfury's orders","parchment on rustlocke"},sp=1},{q="Who is Rhag Garmason?",a="Rhag Garmason is an Alliance officer stationed on the southern side of the Thandol Span in the Wetlands, responsible for securing traffic between the dwarven territories and the north.",al={"rhag garmason","who is garmason"}},{q="Why is the Thandol Span so heavily contested?",a="The Thandol Span represents the sole overland bridge connecting the dwarven lands of Khaz Modan and the Wetlands to the Arathi Highlands and Lordaeron. Securing it is vital for Alliance logistics.",al={"why thandol span matters","thandol span importance"}},{q="What happens after giving the orders to Rhag Garmason?",a="Recognizing the gravity of the threat, Rhag Garmason sends you to destroy a cache of Dark Iron explosives stashed just across the span in the Arathi Highlands to thwart their sabotage.",al={"what happens next","thandol span follow up"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The discovery of Dark Iron forces operating this far north of the Searing Gorge demonstrates how deeply their insidious infiltration reaches, threatening fellow Ironforge kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Thandol Span is the artery tying Ironforge and Stormwind to northern Alliance strongholds, making Rustlocke's discovery critical to continental security."},kw={"arathi","dark iron","deepfury","ebenezer rustlocke","rhag garmason","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:631","subzone:thandol-span","zone:wetlands","quest:634","topic:alliance"},m={start="Ebenezer Rustlocke's Corpse",["end"]="Rhag Garmason",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=632},src={"The Thandol Span (2)"}}
E["quest:633"] = {t="quest",n="The Thandol Span",z="wetlands",s="This critical Alliance mission tasks champions with defending the sole surviving bridge across the Thandol Span. Following the tragic murder of Ebenezer Rustlocke, Rhag Garmason discovers a plot by the traitorous Kam Deepfury to detonate hidden explosives and sever Ironforge's vital connection to the north.",h="This critical Alliance mission tasks champions with defending the sole surviving bridge across the Thandol...",sec={{t="A Plot Revealed",b="After discovering the grim fate of Ebenezer Rustlocke within the Thandol Span's substructure, a recovered document brings darker intentions to light. The Dark Iron agitator Kam Deepfury, architect of the bridge's initial destruction, was not finished. Having already collapsed one of the grand stone crossings, his sabotage network planted a second cache of heavy munitions just across the northern border in the Arathi Highlands, poised to finish the job.",sp=0},{t="Saving the Lifeline",b="The Thandol Span is the primary overland corridor linking the southern kingdoms of Khaz Modan and Stormwind to the war-torn territories of the north. To safeguard this route, Rhag Garmason orders an immediate preemptive strike against the sabotage cache in Arathi before Deepfury's conspirators can deploy it. Detonating the munitions neutralizes the immediate peril, preserving Ironforge's access to the north, though Garmason remains desperately short of troops to defend the gap.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kam Deepfury?",a="Kam Deepfury is the Dark Iron dwarf mastermind who orchestrated the sabotage of the Thandol Span. Not satisfied with collapsing the first arch, he cached additional explosives across the chasm in the Arathi Highlands to bring down the remaining bridge.",al={"kam deepfury","who bombed thandol span","thandol span mastermind"}},{q="Why is the Thandol Span so strategically vital?",a="The Span is the sole terrestrial bridge spanning the immense chasm between the Wetlands and the Arathi Highlands. If severed, the Alliance would lose its primary overland supply route between Ironforge, Stormwind, and their allies holding ground in northern Lordaeron.",al={"why is thandol span important","thandol span lore"}},{q="What happened to Ebenezer Rustlocke?",a="Ebenezer Rustlocke was an Ironforge defender murdered in the depths beneath the bridge. It was from his investigation and the papers recovered from his demise that Rhag Garmason uncovered Deepfury's hidden explosive cache.",al={"ebon rustlocke death","who was rustlocke"},sp=1},{q="Where is the cache of explosives hidden?",a="The explosives were hidden in a cache just across the span on the Arathi Highlands side, placed close enough for Deepfury's conspirators to quickly transport them to the surviving span structure.",al={"explosives location","where are the explosives","cache location"}},{q="Who gives the order to destroy the explosives?",a="Rhag Garmason, a dwarf officer stationed at the Thandol Span on the Wetlands side, gives the order to locate and demolish the cache to honor Rustlocke's sacrifice and protect the remaining bridge.",al={"who starts this quest","rhag garmason"}},{q="What happens after the munitions are destroyed?",a="While the immediate sabotage is thwarted, Rhag Garmason realizes his garrison cannot hold the damaged bridge indefinitely without help. While awaiting Ironforge's reserves, he sends a plea for reinforcements to Captain Nials of the Alliance camp at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"what next after thandol span","plea to the alliance quest"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the sons of Ironforge, defending the Thandol Span protects King Magni's lifeline to northern allies while striking a blow against traitorous Dark Iron infiltrators.",["faction:Alliance"]="Holding the Span is essential for continental security; if this crossing falls, moving Alliance armies and resources into Arathi and Lordaeron becomes exponentially more dangerous.",["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers can appreciate the sheer destructive power of Deepfury's munitions cache, built to demolish colossal titan-style dwarven stonework."},kw={"arathi highlands","dark iron","ebon rustlocke","explosives","kam deepfury","magni bronzebeard","rhag garmason","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"quest:631","quest:634","subzone:thandol-span","npc:kam-deepfury","zone:arathi","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Rhag Garmason",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=633},src={"The Thandol Span (3)"}}
E["quest:634"] = {t="quest",n="Plea To The Alliance",z="wetlands",s="Plea to the Alliance carries a desperate request for reinforcements from the surviving dwarven defenders of Dun Modr across the Thandol Span into Arathi. Faced with the slaughter of their garrison by Dark Iron infiltrators, the dwarves seek aid from the human forces stationed at Refuge Pointe, only to find the Alliance stretched beyond its limits.",h="Plea to the Alliance carries a desperate request for reinforcements from the surviving dwarven defenders of...",sec={{t="A Cry Across the Chasm",b="Following the devastation of Dun Modr and the sabotage of the Thandol Span by Dark Iron dwarves, the dwarven survivors hold a precarious foothold at the northern rim of the Wetlands. With Ironforge's main reserves yet to arrive, Rhag Garmason and Commander Longbraid look north toward the Arathi Highlands. Learning of an Alliance encampment established at Refuge Pointe, Garmason dispatches an emissary across the shattered bridge to appeal to Captain Nials for urgent military aid.",sp=0},{t="The Plight of Stromgarde",b="Upon reaching Refuge Pointe, the grim reality of the northern Alliance becomes apparent. Captain Nials offers heartfelt sympathies to Longbraid's soldiers, but he cannot spare a single fighter. Stromgarde itself has fallen into ruin, overwhelmed by Syndicate rogues, Boulderfist ogres, and Witherbark trolls. The surviving Stromgarde defenders are entirely committed to reclaiming their ancestral capital. Bound by honor and desperate circumstances of their own, Nials is forced to send word back that the dwarves at the Span must stand alone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the plea to Refuge Pointe?",a="Rhag Garmason, stationed near the ruined bridgehead of the Thandol Span on the Wetlands border, sends the plea on behalf of Commander Longbraid and the remnants of Dun Modr's defense.",al={"who gives plea to the alliance","rhag garmason quest","who asks for help"}},{q="Why do the dwarves need help from Refuge Pointe?",a="Dun Modr fell to a sudden and brutal assault by Dark Iron clan infiltrators, who also sabotaged the Thandol Span. While the survivors await heavy reserves from Ironforge, their immediate numbers are too few to retake their settlement and secure the crossing alone.",al={"why need alliance help","why ask refuge pointe","dun modr reinforcements"}},{q="Why does Captain Nials refuse to send soldiers?",a="Captain Nials cannot spare any troops because the Kingdom of Stromgarde has itself collapsed into ruins. The human forces at Refuge Pointe are wholly engaged in a desperate campaign to retake Stromgarde from the Syndicate, ogres, and forest trolls.",al={"why no help from nials","why refuge pointe refuses","captain nials answer"}},{q="Where is Refuge Pointe located?",a="Refuge Pointe lies just off the main road in the central Arathi Highlands, north of the Thandol Span crossing between the Wetlands and Arathi.",al={"refuge pointe location","where is captain nials","how to find refuge pointe"}},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr was overwhelmed and sacked by the Dark Iron clan, who infiltrated through the mountains to sever the land route between the southern dwarven lands and the northern Alliance territories.",al={"dun modr lore","what happened dun modr","who attacked dun modr"}},{q="What happens after Captain Nials turns down the request?",a="Captain Nials sends his regrets to Commander Longbraid, confirming that no human reinforcements are coming. The dwarven survivors at the bridge must rely on their own wits, wandering adventurers, and distant Ironforge reinforcements.",al={"what next plea to the alliance","next quest after plea","chain continuation"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, this mission highlights the painful isolation of northern garrisons like Dun Modr, proving that even longtime human allies are too besieged to lend a hand.",["race:Human"]="Human travelers witness the bitter sorrow of Captain Nials, who is torn between honoring Alliance brotherhood and fighting for the survival of fallen Stromgarde.",["faction:Alliance"]="The exchange underscores how fractured the Alliance remains in the northern Eastern Kingdoms, where local garrisons fight separate, desperate battles with no shared reserves."},kw={"arathi highlands","captain nials","dark iron","dun modr","longbraid","refuge pointe","rhag garmason","stromgarde","thandol span"},rel={"subzone:thandol-span","quest:631","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","quest:472","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},m={start="Rhag Garmason",["end"]="Captain Nials",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=634},src={"Plea To The Alliance"}}
E["quest:647"] = {t="quest",n="MacKreel's Moonshine",z="wetlands",s="MacKreel's Moonshine is a fast-paced errand run on behalf of Foggy MacKreel, a dwarf stranded on the broken part of the Thandol Span. Having overindulged on his own potent brew and slept through his watch, Foggy entrusts an Alliance traveler with rushing a fresh batch to Hillsbrad to settle a lingering debt with Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore.",h="MacKreel's Moonshine is a fast-paced errand run on behalf of Foggy MacKreel, a dwarf stranded on the broken...",sec={{t="A Guard's Hangover",b="Life on watch atop the shattered Thandol Span is wet, cold, and notoriously dull. Foggy MacKreel manages the damp chill by imbibing his own homemade moonshine, a concoction so fierce he compares its aftermath to an entire brigade of siege engines rolling across his skull. Unfortunately for Foggy, one drink too many caused him to pass out during his shift. With Longbraid the Grim commanding the dwarves defending the Span, Foggy cannot afford any further lapses in discipline.",sp=0},{t="A Race Against the Clock",b="Compounding Foggy's troubles is a longstanding debt owed to Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore. Foggy promised Bilger a batch of his personal brew to balance the books, but between his hangover and his shift duties, he finds himself minutes away from default. Relying on gryphons and swift feet, travelers must race across the Arathi Highlands to Southshore to deliver the jug before Bilger decides Foggy has skipped out on his tab once again.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foggy MacKreel?",a="Foggy MacKreel is a dwarf found on the broken part of the Thandol Span, reached from the Arathi Highlands side. Known for brewing extremely stout homemade moonshine, he tends to sample his own product a little too freely while on duty.",al={"foggy mackreel","who is foggy","quest giver mackreel"}},{q="Why is this delivery so urgent?",a="Foggy ran severely behind schedule after passing out drunk during his watch. He has a strict deadline to deliver the moonshine to Brewmeister Bilger to settle an overdue tab, leaving barely a quarter of an hour to make the journey from the Thandol Span to Southshore.",al={"why is there a timer","why 15 minutes","mackreel moonshine timer"}},{q="Who is Brewmeister Bilger?",a="Brewmeister Bilger is a master dwarven brewer who plies his trade in the coastal settlement of Southshore within the Hillsbrad Foothills. He appreciates stout alcohol and has an outstanding business agreement with Foggy MacKreel.",al={"brewmeister bilger","who is bilger","bilger southshore"}},{q="How does one get the moonshine to Southshore in time?",a="There is no boat from the Span to Southshore. The quickest route is to head into the Arathi Highlands and take a gryphon from Refuge Pointe to Southshore if you know that flight path, then find Brewmeister Bilger in town before the timer expires.",al={"how to deliver moonshine","fastest way southshore mackreel","moonshine delivery route"}},{q="Who is Longbraid?",a="Longbraid the Grim is the dwarf commander stationed outside Dun Modr in the Wetlands, leading the defenders of the Thandol Span. Foggy lives in absolute dread of Longbraid discovering that he drank himself unconscious while supposed to be on watch.",al={"captain longbraid","longbraid menethil"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarves will immediately understand the double jeopardy of an agonizing hangover and an unpaid brewing debt owed to a fellow kinsman.",["faction:Alliance"]="This quick overland run highlights the vital connection between the Thandol Span and Alliance-held Southshore in Hillsbrad."},kw={"bilger","foggy","longbraid","mackreel","menethil","moonshine","southshore"},rel={"npc:foggy-mackreel","npc:brewmeister-bilger","zone:wetlands","subzone:southshore"},m={start="Foggy MacKreel",["end"]="Brewmeister Bilger",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=647},src={"MacKreel's Moonshine (quest)"}}
E["subzone:angerfang-encampment"] = {t="subzone",n="Angerfang Encampment",z="wetlands",s="The Angerfang Encampment is the primary stronghold of the Dragonmaw clan in the central Wetlands. Led by Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, these renegade orcs use the sprawling camp as a staging ground to threaten nearby dwarven settlements and plot the destruction of Menethil Harbor.",h="The Angerfang Encampment is the primary stronghold of the Dragonmaw clan in the central Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Bogs",b="Sprawling across the muck of the central Wetlands, the Angerfang Encampment serves as the fortified heart of Dragonmaw power in the region. Unlike the scattered raiding parties found wandering the marshes, this compound boasts heavily defended barricades, watchtowers, and a formidable host of warriors, bonewarders, and dark spellcasters loyal to the old ways. From here, the Dragonmaw project military force across the marshlands, raiding travelers along the roads and menacing nearby dwarven digs like Whelgar's Excavation Site.",sp=0},{t="Nek'rosh's Ambition",b="The encampment is commanded by Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, son of the infamous warlock Nekros who once enslaved the red dragonflight at Grim Batol. Harboring a deep hatred for the Alliance, Nek'rosh has marshaled catapults and raised war banners in preparation for an all-out assault against Menethil Harbor. Aware of the looming siege, Alliance commanders in the port city dispatch champions into the belly of Angerfang to capture their banners, smash their war machines, and claim Nek'rosh's head before his offensive can drown the harbor in fire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules the Angerfang Encampment?",a="The camp is ruled by Chieftain Nek'rosh Skullcrusher, the son of the notorious Dragonmaw warlock Nekros Skullcrusher. From his command tent deep within the encampment, Nek'rosh directs regional raiding parties and plans the conquest of Menethil Harbor.",al={"who leads angerfang","angerfang boss","who is in charge here","nekrosh camp"}},{q="Are the orcs here allied with Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The Dragonmaw clan here remains independent of Thrall's New Horde. They cling to the dark heritage of the Old Horde, remaining hostile to Alliance and Horde travelers alike. Thrall's warriors view them as feral outcasts, even hunting them down for armor crafting materials.",al={"are dragonmaw horde","are angerfang friendly to horde","is angerfang part of thralls horde"}},{q="Why is the Alliance focused on destroying this camp?",a="Captain Stoutfist and the dwarven defenders of Menethil Harbor discovered that Nek'rosh has assembled catapults and massive forces at Angerfang to bombard and conquer the harbor. The Alliance attacks preemptively to crush the siege before it begins.",al={"why attack angerfang","captain stoutfist angerfang","why kill nekrosh"}},{q="Why do warlocks seek out this encampment?",a="The dark spellcasters among the Dragonmaw at Angerfang carry Rods of Channeling, dark ritual implements coveted by practitioners of the demonic arts seeking to complete the Tome of the Cabal.",al={"warlock quest angerfang","tome of the cabal wetlands","rod of channeling angerfang"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the defenders of Menethil Harbor, Angerfang is a clear and present danger; bringing down Nek'rosh's war banners and taking his head is vital to securing the coastal trade routes.",["class:Warlock"]="The dark shadowwarders within the encampment carry Rods of Channeling, essential artifacts sought for the bindings written within the Tome of the Cabal."},kw={"angerfang","dragonmaw","menethil","nek'rosh","skullcrusher","stoutfist","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"quest:465","quest:474","quest:464","zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","quest:1758","quest:1846"},src={"Angerfang Encampment"}}
E["subzone:baradin-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Baradin Bay",z="wetlands",s="Baradin Bay is the expansive body of water lying between the shores of Khaz Modan, the Wetlands, the Arathi Highlands, and southern Lordaeron. Once vigorously patrolled by the powerful navy of Kul Tiras during the Second War, its waters now conceal treacherous reefs, sunken warships, and hostile aquatic predators.",h="Baradin Bay is the expansive body of water lying between the shores of Khaz Modan, the Wetlands, the Arathi...",sec={{t="A Strategic Waterway",b="Framed by the coasts of Dun Morogh to the south and Lordaeron to the north, Baradin Bay serves as a vital maritime passage connecting the harbors of the Eastern Kingdoms. The bay is anchored by busy ports like Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands and Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills. However, navigating these waters is perilous: shallow sandbanks, jagged shoals, and dangerous fauna like murlocs, crocolisks, and deep-sea sharks pose constant threats to sailors and travelers alike.",sp=0},{t="Graveyard of the Fleets",b="During the Second War, Baradin Bay witnessed heavy naval conflict as the fleets of Kul Tiras clashed with the Horde. Today, grim reminders of those battles litter the coast and the seabed. The shattered hulls of the Kul Tiran Third Fleet—known locally as the Lost Fleet—rest half-submerged along the Wetlands coast, while other vessels have plummeted down to Drowned Reef. Hostile spirits, opportunistic salvagers, and ravenous sea beasts now haunt the waters surrounding these decaying timber ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What major ports are located along Baradin Bay?",a="The most prominent settlements on the bay's coast are Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands and Southshore in the Hillsbrad Foothills, which sustain vital naval transit across the sea.",al={"baradin bay ports","harbors in baradin bay","where does baradin bay lead"}},{q="Why are there so many shipwrecks along the bay's coast?",a="Many of the wrecks, including the Lost Fleet along the Wetlands shore and those resting on Drowned Reef, were ships of the Kul Tiras navy sunk during intense naval clashes in the Second War.",al={"wetlands shipwrecks","why are ships sunken here","lost fleet origin"}},{q="What threats can be found in the waters of Baradin Bay?",a="The shallows are crawling with aggressive murlocs and swamp crocolisks, while the deeper waters are infested with predatory crabs, sharks, and the restless spirits of drowned sailors.",al={"baradin bay monsters","murlocs in baradin bay","is it safe to swim in baradin bay"}},{q="Which territories border Baradin Bay?",a="Baradin Bay is enclosed by northwestern Dun Morogh, the marshy shores of the Wetlands, the cliffs of the Arathi Highlands, and the coasts of southern Hillsbrad and Gilneas.",al={"what zones border baradin bay","baradin bay geography"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Baradin Bay serves as the maritime lifeline connecting Alliance operations in Khaz Modan with their outposts in Arathi and Hillsbrad, though naval hazards and sunken wreckage make every crossing risky.",["race:Human"]="For humans, especially those tracing lineage back to Kul Tiras or Lordaeron, the bay is hallowed and somber ground holding the watery graves of Second War sailors."},kw={"baradin bay","drowned reef","great sea","kul tiras","lost fleet","menethil harbor","southshore","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","subzone:lost-fleet","subzone:drowned-reef","subzone:southshore","topic:kul-tiras","topic:second-war","subzone:faldir-s-cove"},src={"Baradin Bay"}}
E["subzone:black-channel-marsh"] = {t="subzone",n="Black Channel Marsh",z="wetlands",s="Black Channel Marsh is a murky mire situated in the southwestern Wetlands, flanking the main road leading toward Menethil Harbor. Infested with aggressive raptors, the soggy terrain poses an immediate threat to unwary travelers and supply couriers traversing the coastal lowlands.",h="Black Channel Marsh is a murky mire situated in the southwestern Wetlands, flanking the main road leading...",sec={{t="Peril on the Menethil Road",b="Stretching across the swampy low ground southwest of the main thoroughfare, Black Channel Marsh is infamous among caravan drivers and couriers heading to Menethil Harbor. While the raised road offers the illusion of safety, the stagnant channels and thick reeds are home to territorial raptor packs. Hungry beasts frequently stray directly into traffic, ambushing fresh recruits and weary wayfarers who stray even a pace or two from the beaten path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Black Channel Marsh located?",a="Black Channel Marsh occupies the southwestern corner of the Wetlands. It borders the southern side of the major roadway leading into Menethil Harbor.",al={"where is black channel marsh","black channel marsh location","wetlands black channel"}},{q="Why is this marsh considered dangerous for travelers?",a="The marsh is teeming with raptor lairs. Because these predators hunt along the fringes of the swamp, they regularly prowl right up to the edges of the road, catching unsuspecting travelers and low-level adventurers off guard.",al={"why is it dangerous","threats in black channel marsh","raptors on road"}},{q="Who travels through here most often?",a="Alliance messengers, dwarven merchants, and travelers journeying between Ironforge and the docks of Menethil Harbor frequently traverse the road running directly past the marsh.",al={"who uses this road","travelers here"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The marsh provides a hazardous proving ground for hunters seeking to tame or track fierce Wetlands raptors right off the main road.",["faction:Alliance"]="This corridor is a vital lifeline connecting the port of Menethil Harbor to the rest of Khaz Modan, making raptor incursions a constant headache for travelers."},kw={"black channel marsh","marsh","menethil harbor","raptors","swamp","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor"},src={"Black Channel Marsh"}}
E["subzone:bluegill-marsh"] = {t="subzone",n="Bluegill Marsh",z="wetlands",s="Bluegill Marsh is a sodden mire in the western Wetlands that serves as the sprawling settlement for the hostile Bluegill murloc tribe. The waterways and huts are fiercely guarded by these aquatic humanoids under the rule of the brute known as Gobbler. Travelers heading through the western fens must navigate carefully to avoid being surrounded in the shallows.",h="Bluegill Marsh is a sodden mire in the western Wetlands that serves as the sprawling settlement for the...",sec={{t="A Swarming Hazard",b="Situated amidst the boggy flats of the western Wetlands, Bluegill Marsh is thick with mud, reeds, and the squawking war cries of its resident murlocs. The Bluegill tribe has erected crude primitive camps throughout the stagnant water, claiming this territory as their own. Unlike more isolated beasts of the swamp, these murlocs live and hunt in tightly knit packs. Wary wanderers and scouts from Menethil Harbor know that wading into their territory invites swift ambushes from every direction, especially with the formidable chieftain Gobbler prowling the murky shallows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Bluegill Marsh?",a="Bluegill Marsh is a boggy subzone in the western region of the Wetlands. It is the primary dwelling and nesting ground of the aggressive Bluegill tribe of murlocs.",al={"where is bluegill marsh","what is this place","wetlands murloc swamp"}},{q="Who rules over the marsh?",a="The Bluegill tribe is led by a powerful and vicious murloc known as Gobbler, who keeps watch over the clustered encampments and strikes down any land-walkers who encroach upon their waters.",al={"murloc leader wetlands","gobbler","who leads the bluegill murlocs"}},{q="Why is it dangerous to travel here alone?",a="The murlocs here rarely roam solo. They congregate around huts and shorelines in close-knit bands of two or three, making it very easy for lone travelers to be overwhelmed in the deep, slowing mud.",al={"why are there so many murlocs","is bluegill marsh hard","murloc aggro"}},{q="Why do travelers venture into Bluegill Marsh?",a="Scouts and adventurers from nearby settlements like Menethil Harbor are regularly directed into the marsh to thin the aggressive murloc population and recover stolen goods carried off into their camps.",al={"why go here","bluegill marsh quests","reasons to visit"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Positioned not far from Menethil Harbor, the aggressive Bluegill murlocs pose a constant nuisance to travelers and supply lines moving through the western Wetlands."},kw={"bluegill","bluegill marsh","gobbler","menethil","murloc","swamp","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:murloc"},src={"Bluegill Marsh"}}
E["subzone:deepwater-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Deepwater Tavern",z="wetlands",s="The Deepwater Tavern is the bustling seaside inn of Menethil Harbor, nestled in the damp marshlands of the Wetlands. It serves as the primary meeting spot, resupply point, and resting place for travelers and mariners navigating the busy port town. Between hearty drinks and harbor rumors, patrons frequently find work or run into volatile tavern brawls.",h="The Deepwater Tavern is the bustling seaside inn of Menethil Harbor, nestled in the damp marshlands of the...",sec={{t="Heart of Menethil Harbor",b="Standing within the sodden streets of Menethil Harbor, the Deepwater Tavern offers travelers a welcome shelter from the perpetually drizzly, treacherous marshlands outside. Sailors, dockworkers, merchants, and weary adventurers gather beneath its timber beams to trade news, share a warm fire, and patch their wounds. Beyond the usual amenities of a harbor inn, it houses a resident first aid trainer and local merchants catering to those bound for the perils of the marsh or embarking across the Great Sea. The atmosphere is boisterous and occasionally hazardous; disputes flare up quickly over spilled ale, with notorious troublemakers like Tapoke 'Slim' Jahn known to spark the occasional tavern-wide brawl.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Deepwater Tavern located?",a="The Deepwater Tavern is situated near the waterfront of Menethil Harbor, the primary port town of the Wetlands on the western coast of Khaz Modan.",al={"deepwater tavern location","where is deepwater tavern","menethil harbor inn"}},{q="What services are available inside the tavern?",a="Besides typical innkeeper lodging and refreshments, the tavern houses merchants and a first aid trainer, making it a critical resupply and healing point for adventurers traveling through the marshlands.",al={"deepwater tavern services","menethil tavern trainers","what can i find at deepwater tavern"}},{q="Who frequently starts brawls in the tavern?",a="The tavern is famous for spontaneous fights, with a shifty troublemaker named Tapoke 'Slim' Jahn frequently instigating brawls among the rowdy patrons and sailors.",al={"bar brawl menethil","tapoke slim jahn","who starts fights at deepwater tavern"}},{q="Why is the tavern so busy?",a="Menethil Harbor is the major shipping and naval gateway linking Khaz Modan to Kalimdor and northern ports. As the sole major inn in town, it gathers a steady flow of sailors, mercenaries, and Alliance adventurers heading into the Wetlands.",al={"why visit deepwater tavern","why is deepwater tavern popular"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Deepwater Tavern serves as an indispensable rallying point and rest haven for Alliance members passing between Ironforge and the open sea."},kw={"deepwater tavern","first aid trainer","innkeeper","menethil harbor","tapoke slim jahn","tavern brawl","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},src={"Deepwater Tavern"}}
E["subzone:direforge-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Direforge Hill",z="wetlands",s="Direforge Hill is a rugged highland nestled in the northeastern Wetlands, situated between the Green Belt and the mountains bordering the Arathi Highlands. Under the command of the dark warlock Balgaras the Foul, a contingent of treacherous Dark Iron dwarves has fortified these slopes. Their fiery sorcery and encampments pose an immediate peril to the surrounding wetlands and the ancient guardians watching over them.",h="Direforge Hill is a rugged highland nestled in the northeastern Wetlands, situated between the Green Belt and...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Dark Sorcery",b="Perched southeast of the contested stronghold of Dun Modr, Direforge Hill serves as a strategic staging ground for the Dark Iron clan within the Wetlands. Rather than merely mining or fortifying the hills, the dwarves under Balgaras the Foul practice dark magics that threaten to scorch the surrounding bogs. From crude wooden stockades and bonfires, these hostile dwarves launch raids and guard their encampment fiercely, defying both the Ironforge patrols guarding the roads and the primal caretakers seeking to keep the marshland alive.",sp=0},{t="The Threat to the Wetlands",b="The presence of Balgaras and his followers atop Direforge Hill extends far beyond normal border skirmishes. Dark Iron warlock magic defiles the natural balance of the Wetlands, drawing the ire of protectors such as Rethiel the Greenwarden down in the marsh. Left unchecked, the defilement and burning camps upon the hillside could spread unchecked into the Green Belt and down toward Raptor Ridge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Direforge Hill located?",a="Direforge Hill is located in the northeastern portion of the Wetlands. It lies southeast of Dun Modr, just northeast of the lush Green Belt, and northwest of the rocky bluffs of Raptor Ridge.",al={"direforge hill location","where is direforge hill","direforge wetlands"}},{q="Who controls Direforge Hill right now?",a="The hill is occupied by hostile Dark Iron dwarves commanded by the warlock Balgaras the Foul. They have fortified the high ground with barricades, watchtowers, and open flame pits.",al={"who is at direforge hill","who lives at direforge hill","direforge hill mobs"}},{q="Why is Direforge Hill significant to the Wetlands?",a="The Dark Iron encampment acts as a staging area for subversive activity in northern Wetlands. Their foul warlock sorcery and fires threaten the surrounding nature, drawing the attention of local nature guardians and Ironforge scouts alike.",al={"why is direforge hill important","direforge threat","what is happening at direforge hill"}},{q="Who is Balgaras the Foul?",a="Balgaras the Foul is a Dark Iron dwarf warlock who commands the forces encamped at Direforge Hill. His corrupted arts and aggressive presence in the hills make him a priority target for those defending the marsh.",al={"balgaras","balgaras the foul lore","who is balgaras"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge, seeing the treachery of the Dark Iron clan creep into the Wetlands—especially under warlocks like Balgaras—is an outrage that must be answered with cold steel.",["class:Druid"]="The dark, burning magic wielded by the warlocks of Direforge Hill threatens the primordial balance of the Wetlands, directly disturbing guardians like Rethiel the Greenwarden."},kw={"balgaras","balgaras the foul","dark iron dwarves","direforge","direforge hill","dun modr","green belt","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:green-belt","subzone:raptor-ridge","npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:463"},src={"Direforge Hill"}}
E["subzone:dragonmaw-gates"] = {t="subzone",n="Dragonmaw Gates",z="wetlands",s="The Dragonmaw Gates are a series of imposing fortifications along the mountain road leading up from the eastern Wetlands. Built to guard the steep ascent to the mountain fortress of Grim Batol, these heavy barricades bar entry into the cursed heights of the dwarven ruins.",h="The Dragonmaw Gates are a series of imposing fortifications along the mountain road leading up from the...",sec={{t="Sentinels of Grim Batol",b="Carved into the rugged peaks bordering the eastern Wetlands, the Dragonmaw Gates seal the winding road that climbs into the mountains toward Grim Batol. Named after the Dragonmaw clan of orcs who held the dwarven mountain city during the Second War, these defensive barriers remain deeply fortified checkpoints. Anyone attempting to ascend toward the heights must contend with the lingering perils of the pass, where powerful drakes and grim reminders of the clan's dark history still cast a long shadow.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Threshold",b="Though the Dragonmaw orcs were broken and scattered following the destruction of the Demon Soul, the mountain path remains exceptionally dangerous. Powerful red dragons have been seen watching over the winding slopes and perches around the gates. Between monstrous drakes and remnants of the Dragonmaw clan lurking in the nearby hills, the gates stand as a firm barrier against any travelers bold enough to venture up the heights.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the Dragonmaw Gates lead?",a="The gates seal the winding mountain path ascending east from the Wetlands directly into the cursed fortress-city of Grim Batol and the surrounding mountain heights.",al={"path past dragonmaw gates","what is behind dragonmaw gates","road past gates"}},{q="Why are they called the Dragonmaw Gates?",a="They take their name from the Dragonmaw clan of orcs, who occupied the nearby dwarven stronghold of Grim Batol during the Second War and used foul sorcery to enslave red dragons.",al={"why called dragonmaw gates","dragonmaw gate name","dragonmaw orcs wetlands"}},{q="Can travelers pass through the gates?",a="The massive gates are firmly shut and heavily defended, barring any normal passage into the high mountains.",al={"can you open dragonmaw gates","getting through dragonmaw gates"}},{q="Who guards the road around the gates?",a="The road and the rugged passes nearby are haunted by fierce red dragonspawn and drakes, along with scattered orcs and dark threats still clinging to the slopes of the mountains.",al={"who is at dragonmaw gates","dragons at dragonmaw gates","axtroz dragonmaw gates"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the gates represent the sealed threshold to Grim Batol—an ancestral home abandoned after the War of the Three Hammers and later desecrated by the Dragonmaw orcs.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance keeps a wary eye on the gates, knowing that anything emerging from the high road threatens the stability of the entire Wetlands."},kw={"axtroz","dragonmaw clan","dragonmaw gates","grim batol","mountain pass","red dragonflight","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:grim-batol","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Dragonmaw Gates"}}
E["subzone:dun-algaz"] = {t="subzone",n="Dun Algaz",z="wetlands",s="Dun Algaz is the fortified mountain pass and network of tunnels connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands. Historically contested during the Second War, this vital trade artery has recently fallen under siege by Dragonmaw orcs, cutting off easy transit between Ironforge's territories and Menethil Harbor.",h="Dun Algaz is the fortified mountain pass and network of tunnels connecting Loch Modan to the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Chokepoint Between Realms",b="Dun Algaz predates the War of the Three Hammers, originally serving as the passage the Wildhammer clan used to migrate north after being driven out of Ironforge. Carved deep into the jagged peaks separating Loch Modan and the Wetlands, the pass consists of sweeping stone tunnels, bastions, and watchposts. Its strategic value cannot be overstated: whoever holds Dun Algaz commands the only overland highway linking the dwarven heartlands to the western sea at Menethil Harbor.",sp=0},{t="The Dragonmaw Resurgence",b="During the Second War, the Old Horde retreated to Dun Algaz after their defeat at Dun Modr, turning it into their final southern bulwark against Sir Anduin Lothar's forces. Years later, Nekros Skullcrusher sheltered the Dragonmaw clan in the surrounding caves. Though the Alliance reclaimed the pass for a time, Dragonmaw orcs have once again overrun the stronghold, forcing the dwarven Mountaineers to retreat to the upper tunnels and turning the mountain corridor into a deadly gauntlet for travelers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Dun Algaz so dangerous right now?",a="Dragonmaw orcs have descended from the surrounding mountains and seized control of the lower pass and stronghold. Dwarven Mountaineers have been pushed back to the upper pass near Algaz Station, leaving the main road swarming with hostile orcs who ambush travelers attempting to pass between Loch Modan and the Wetlands.",al={"why are there orcs in dun algaz","dun algaz orcs","who controls dun algaz"}},{q="Why is this pass so important to the dwarves?",a="Dun Algaz is the primary overland route connecting Ironforge and Loch Modan to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Menethil Harbor serves as the main shipping gateway between Khaz Modan and the rest of the Alliance territories, making Dun Algaz an essential corridor for supplies, troops, and trade.",al={"dun algaz importance","why does ironforge need dun algaz"}},{q="Did Dun Algaz play a role in the Second War?",a="Yes. Following their loss at Dun Modr, the Orcish Horde fell back across the Thandol Valley to make Dun Algaz a defensive stronghold. Sir Anduin Lothar ordered an assault to dislodge them and drive them from Khaz Modan, but the Alliance was unable to fully root out the Horde, leaving it as one of their final strongholds in the region.",al={"dun algaz second war","anduin lothar dun algaz"}},{q="What is the history between Dun Algaz and the Wildhammer dwarves?",a="Long before the Second War, during the ancient War of the Three Hammers, the Wildhammer dwarves were driven out of Ironforge. They traveled through Dun Algaz to migrate north into the Wetlands and eventually settle in Grim Batol.",al={"wildhammer dun algaz","war of the three hammers pass"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Dun Algaz is an ancestral highway cut through the spine of Khaz Modan. Seeing Dragonmaw orcs occupy dwarven bastions and threaten supply lines to Menethil Harbor is an ongoing insult and security crisis.",["faction:Alliance"]="The route through Dun Algaz is critical for Alliance logistics, securing the overland road that joins the port of Menethil Harbor with Loch Modan and Ironforge."},kw={"algaz gate","algaz station","dragonmaw","dun algaz","loch modan","menethil harbor","mountain pass","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","zone:lochmodan","subzone:algaz-station","topic:dragonmaw-clan","quest:455","topic:second-war","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:dun-modr"},src={"Dun Algaz"}}
E["subzone:dun-modr"] = {t="subzone",n="Dun Modr",z="wetlands",s="Dun Modr is an ancient fortified dwarven town in northern Wetlands, guarding the southern approach to the Thandol Span. Once a critical fortress held and contested across multiple wars, it has recently fallen to a hostile force of Dark Iron dwarves.",h="Dun Modr is an ancient fortified dwarven town in northern Wetlands, guarding the southern approach to the...",sec={{t="A Contested Bastion",b="Situated at the northern edge of the Wetlands, Dun Modr commands the primary overland highway linking Khaz Modan with the northern human kingdoms. Because of this vital location, the stronghold has seen heavy bloodshed over the decades. During the Second War, the Orcish Horde captured and entrenched themselves within the dwarven fortress, using it as a forward staging ground to launch raids and repel Alliance armies. Stromgarde warriors launched a brutal amphibious assault from Tol Barad to reclaim it, only for the Orcs to strike back in a bloody tug-of-war. Alliance forces led by Lord Anduin Lothar ultimately drove the invaders south across the Thandol Span, restoring dwarven custody over the bastion.",sp=0},{t="The Dark Iron Incursion",b="With Ironforge's attention divided and many of its finest mountaineers committed to Alliance duties abroad, Dun Modr was left vulnerable. Seizing the opportunity, Dark Iron invaders pushed north and sabotaged the Thandol Span with explosives before swarming the fortress. Under the command of the Dark Iron warlock Balgaras the Foul, these infiltrators overran the town's defenders, driving out the Bronzebeard garrison and transforming the strategic outpost into a hostile den. Surrounding Mountaineers now maintain a grim perimeter just down the road, desperately seeking aid to dislodge the occupiers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Dun Modr so important?",a="Dun Modr sits directly along the major northern road in the Wetlands leading to the Thandol Span. Controlling the fortress means controlling all overland traffic, supply lines, and military movement between Khaz Modan and the northern continent of Lordaeron.",al={"why does dun modr matter","importance of dun modr","dun modr strategic value"}},{q="Who controls Dun Modr right now?",a="The stronghold has fallen to the Dark Iron clan, led on-site by a warlock named Balgaras the Foul. Bronzebeard Mountaineers loyal to Ironforge maintain a watchful camp nearby, hoping to reclaim it.",al={"who is in dun modr","who runs dun modr","who lives in dun modr"}},{q="What happened to Dun Modr during the Second War?",a="The Orcish Horde overran the town and turned it into a forward military base. Stromgarde forces struck from the island of Tol Barad to retake the ruins, sparking fierce clashes until Anduin Lothar's Alliance forces finally swept the Horde out of the region.",al={"second war dun modr","orcs in dun modr","did horde take dun modr"}},{q="Who is Balgaras the Foul?",a="Balgaras the Foul is the Dark Iron warlock leading the occupation of Dun Modr. Under his command, the Dark Irons managed to damage the Thandol Span and drive the local Ironforge defenders out of the fortress.",al={"balgaras the foul lore","balgaras who","dark iron leader dun modr"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a storied Bronzebeard mountain settlement fall into the hands of the treacherous Dark Iron clan is a bitter insult that demands vengeance.",["faction:Alliance"]="The fall of Dun Modr threatens the critical transit route across the Thandol Span, severing easy travel between Ironforge and the northern Alliance remnants."},kw={"balgaras the foul","dark iron","dun modr","ironforge","mountaineers","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:thandol-span","quest:303","zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-algaz","topic:second-war","topic:anduin-lothar","quest:631","zone:ironforge"},src={"Dun Modr"}}
E["subzone:green-belt"] = {t="subzone",n="Green Belt",z="wetlands",s="The Green Belt is a wild stretch of marshland in the eastern Wetlands, sprawling below the ridges of Grim Batol. It is overrun by roaming bog beasts, predatory crocolisks, and toxic oozes, guarded primarily by the solitary night elf Rethiel the Greenwarden.",h="The Green Belt is a wild stretch of marshland in the eastern Wetlands, sprawling below the ridges of Grim...",sec={{t="A Wild and Contested Fen",b="Stretching across the eastern interior of the Wetlands, the Green Belt is one of the sodden region's untamed hollows. The local wildlife—ranging from massive crocolisks to shifting oozes and shambling bog beasts—makes travel through the mossy waters hazardous. Deep within its reaches sits a solitary watch post manned by Rethiel the Greenwarden, a lone night elf dedicated to studying the fen's ecology and keeping its hostile denizens in check.",sp=0},{t="Remnants of the Second War",b="Scattered amidst the muck lies the wreckage of a Dragonmaw clan caravan, left behind after the catastrophic battle at nearby Grim Batol. Crimson whelplings still linger around the broken carts and crushed cages, haunting reminders of the orcish clan's past enslavement of Alexstrasza and her red dragon brood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Green Belt located?",a="The Green Belt occupies the eastern half of the Wetlands, lying along the soggy lowlands between the main road and the foothills rising toward Grim Batol.",al={"green belt location","where is green belt","green belt wetlands map"}},{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is an enigmatic night elf standing watch in the Wetlands marsh. Far from his ancestral home of Kalimdor, he seeks to preserve nature's balance in the swamp and enlists travelers to deal with corrupting beasts and oozes.",al={"who is rethiel","rethiel the greenwarden","night elf in green belt"}},{q="Why are there red whelps and broken wagons here?",a="They are the ruins of a Dragonmaw clan supply caravan caught in the aftermath of the Second War, when the orcs were routed from Grim Batol and their hold over the red dragonflight shattered.",al={"dragonmaw caravan","why are there whelps in wetlands","red whelps wetlands"}},{q="What threats wander the Green Belt?",a="Travelers through the belt frequently encounter dangerous wetland crocolisks, toxic living oozes, and towering bog beasts that blend seamlessly into the sodden vegetation.",al={"green belt mobs","dangers in green belt","what monsters live here"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Finding Rethiel the Greenwarden stationed alone in an Eastern Kingdoms swamp is an unexpected sight, serving as a reminder of the Cenarion circle and night elven devotion to healing wild lands wherever they lie.",["class:Druid"]="The twisted oozes and unchecked bog beasts of the fen disrupt the natural harmony of the marsh, making the region a point of concern for keepers of the wild."},kw={"bog beasts","dragonmaw","green belt","grim batol","oozes","rethiel","wetlands","whelps"},rel={"npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","zone:wetlands","subzone:grim-batol","topic:dragonmaw-clan","quest:463"},src={"Green Belt"}}
E["subzone:grim-batol"] = {t="subzone",n="Grim Batol",z="wetlands",s="Grim Batol is an ancient, ruined dwarven mountain fortress looming over the eastern edge of the Wetlands. Built by the Wildhammer clan, abandoned after a dark curse during the War of the Three Hammers, and later occupied by the Dragonmaw orcs as a dragon breeding lair, its sealed gates remain an ominous blight upon the highlands.",h="Grim Batol is an ancient, ruined dwarven mountain fortress looming over the eastern edge of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Fortress Twice Cursed",b="Following the ancient civil war of the three clans, Thane Khardros Wildhammer carved Grim Batol out of the jagged mountains east of the marsh. During the subsequent War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron sorceress Modgud laid siege to the fortress. Although Khardros struck her down, Modgud cast a foul shadow across the stones before her death. The lingering taint rendered the halls uninhabitable, forcing the surviving Wildhammer dwarves to abandon their magnificent kingdom and migrate north into the Hinterlands.",sp=0},{t="Chains of the Dragon Queen",b="Centuries later during the Second War, the fortress found a darker purpose when Orgrim Doomhammer dispatched the Dragonmaw clan to claim it. Led by the warlock Nekros Skullcrusher, the orcs utilized the ancient artifact known as the Demon Soul to enslave the red Dragonqueen Alexstrasza deep within the mountain's roots. Forced to hatch broods for the Horde's war effort, Alexstrasza remained chained until a small band of heroes shattered the artifact. Once freed, the enraged Dragon Aspect incinerated the orcs within, leaving Grim Batol a smoldering, desolate ruin watched closely by surviving red dragons.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can players enter Grim Batol?",a="No. The colossal stone gates at the end of the mountain road remain firmly barred and inaccessible to travelers. Only its imposing gates and exterior battlements in the eastern mountains of the Wetlands can be visited.",al={"can i go inside grim batol","is grim batol open","grim batol gate"}},{q="Why did the Wildhammer dwarves abandon it?",a="During the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron sorceress Modgud infused the stronghold with a vile shadow curse before she was slain. The taint left behind rendered the fortress unlivable for the Wildhammers, driving them to abandon it and build Aerie Peak in the Hinterlands.",al={"why did dwarves leave grim batol","wildhammer curse","modgud curse"}},{q="What happened to the Dragonmaw orcs who lived here?",a="When the mage Rhonin and his companions shattered the Demon Soul, the captive Dragonqueen Alexstrasza was freed from her chains. Enraged by her cruel captivity, she and her brood incinerated Nekros Skullcrusher and shattered the Dragonmaw presence in the fortress.",al={"dragonmaw grim batol","what happened to the orcs here","nekros skullcrusher"}},{q="Who controls Grim Batol right now?",a="Presently, Grim Batol is an abandoned ruin. While remnants of the Dragonmaw clan and wild beasts linger in the surrounding crags, the Red Dragonflight maintains a watchful eye over the cursed mountain to ensure its dark history never repeats.",al={"who owns grim batol","who lives in grim batol now"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Grim Batol stands as a bitter testament to the War of the Three Hammers—a once-proud sister city to Ironforge rendered permanently unlivable by Dark Iron sorcery.",["faction:Horde"]="The mountain represents the grim heights of the Second War, where the Dragonmaw clan harnessed enslaved dragons to conquer the skies before their violent ruin."},kw={"alexstrasza","demon soul","dragonmaw","grim batol","modgud","nekros","wetlands","wildhammer"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:wildhammer-clan","topic:dragonmaw-clan","topic:second-war","zone:hinterlands","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:dun-algaz"},src={"Grim Batol"}}
E["subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironbeard's Tomb",z="wetlands",s="Ironbeard's Tomb is a defiled dwarven burial site situated west of the road leading north toward Dun Modr in the Wetlands. Marked by an outdoor graveyard and a stone statue of its namesake, the crypt has fallen into disuse as acidic oozes swarm the grounds. Travelers rarely set foot in the hollow unless searching for lost possessions swallowed by the slime.",h="Ironbeard's Tomb is a defiled dwarven burial site situated west of the road leading north toward Dun Modr in...",sec={{t="A Befouled Resting Place",b="Overlooking the marshes along the road north to Dun Modr, Ironbeard's Tomb stands as a testament to the dwarven presence in the Wetlands. A monumental stone statue, presumed to depict Ironbeard himself, watches over the surrounding burial plot. Yet solemn peace no longer keeps vigil here. The subterranean crypt has been completely overrun by oozes of various black and crimson strains, leaving the tomb contaminated. Dwarves no longer bring their dead to this ruined sanctuary, and those brave enough to disturb the vaults do so primarily to hunt through the remains digested by the lurking slimes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Ironbeard?",a="Very little is recorded about Ironbeard himself, though the massive statue and crypt grounds suggest he was an honored dwarven figure of note in the Wetlands. The monument erected in his likeness watches over the hillside above the cemetery.",al={"ironbeard lore","who is ironbeard","statue identity"}},{q="Why is the tomb abandoned?",a="The crypt has been completely overrun by acidic black and crimson oozes. With the burial grounds defiled and infested with dangerous slimes, mourning families have ceased bringing their dead here.",al={"why abandoned","oozes in tomb","what happened to the crypt"}},{q="Why do adventurers explore Ironbeard's Tomb?",a="Beyond fighting back the foul infestation, travelers frequently search the tomb's slimes hoping to recover swallowed items, most notably Sida's lost bag.",al={"why go here","sida bag","tomb quests"}},{q="Where is Ironbeard's Tomb located?",a="The tomb sits in north-central Wetlands, nestled into the hill just west of the main road heading north toward the dwarven redoubt of Dun Modr.",al={"tomb location","how to get to ironbeard tomb","ironbeard wetlands map"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a clan hero's final resting place infested by mindless marsh oozes is a bitter disgrace for any dwarf traveling the road toward the Thandol Span."},kw={"crypt","dun modr","graveyard","ironbeard","ironbeard's tomb","oozes","sida","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:dun-modr","npc:sida","zone:stormwind"},src={"Ironbeard's Tomb"}}
E["subzone:lost-fleet"] = {t="subzone",n="Lost Fleet",z="wetlands",s="The Lost Fleet consists of the shattered wooden hulks of the Kul Tiras Third Fleet, sunken off the northern coast of the Wetlands along Baradin Bay. Decimated during the Second War by Dragonmaw-enslaved red dragons, the wreckage is now haunted by restless, cursed undead sailors bound to a dark artifact left rotting in a ruined hold.",h="The Lost Fleet consists of the shattered wooden hulks of the Kul Tiras Third Fleet, sunken off the northern...",sec={{t="A Tragic End in the Second War",b="During the Second War, the Kul Tiras Third Fleet was under the command of Derek Proudmoore, elder son of the Lord Admiral. While clashing with the Orcish Armada, the Alliance vessels were ambushed from above by red dragons enslaved by the Dragonmaw clan. Sheets of dragonflame quickly engulfed the fleet, sending proud vessels like the Wave Mistress and the Intrepid crashing onto the shallows and reefs of northern Bluegill Marsh. Almost the entire contingent drowned or burned, with First Mate Fitzsimmons standing as the lone living survivor of the disaster.",sp=0},{t="The Curse of Paleth",b="A watery grave was not the end for the sailors of the Third Fleet. Locked deep in the sunken cargo hold of the Intrepid lay a forbidden artifact known as the Cursed Eye of Paleth, hoarded by the ship's greedy commander, Captain Halyndor. The dark relic corrupted the drowned crews, binding their spirits to the splintered timbers as raving, cursed undead. Only the ghost of First Mate Snellig retains any semblance of sanity, wandering the marshy shore while his former crewmates violently lash out at any trespassers who venture near the wrecks.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Lost Fleet?",a="The Lost Fleet is the wreckage of several Kul Tiras warships from the Third Fleet, resting off the northern coast of the Wetlands in Baradin Bay. They were destroyed during the Second War and are now haunted by their undead crews.",al={"lost fleet","what is this place","wetlands shipwrecks","third fleet"}},{q="How were these ships destroyed?",a="During the Second War, the fleet was ambushed and burned by enslaved red dragons fielded by the orcish Dragonmaw clan. The intense dragonflame reduced the ships to burning hulks that foundered along the coast.",al={"who sank the ships","how did they sink","what destroyed the fleet"}},{q="Why are the sailors here undead?",a="The crew was cursed by a foul artifact called the Cursed Eye of Paleth, which was secretly kept in the cargo hold of the Intrepid by its captain, Halyndor. The relic's dark magic denied the drowned sailors a peaceful rest.",al={"why are they ghosts","undead sailors","curse of paleth"}},{q="Did anyone survive the destruction of the fleet?",a="First Mate Fitzsimmons of the Wave Mistress is the only known living survivor of the catastrophe. He managed to reach safety and now resides at Menethil Harbor.",al={"any survivors","did anyone live","fitzsimmons"}},{q="Who was in charge of the Third Fleet?",a="The Third Fleet was commanded by Derek Proudmoore, the eldest son of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. Derek was killed atop the crow's nest of his flagship when dragons engulfed the fleet in flame.",al={"who commanded the fleet","fleet captain","derek proudmoore"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The hulks are a somber reminder of the heavy toll Kul Tiras and the Alliance paid during the Second War, demanding respect for the fallen and an end to their cursed torment.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Alliance smiths often hear tales of the sunken fleet, as another vessel from the same squadron, the Flying Osprey, went down carrying rare ingots of Lightforge iron."},kw={"baradin bay","bluegill marsh","derek proudmoore","doomed fleet","eye of paleth","fitzsimmons","halyndor","intrepid","lost fleet","snellig","third fleet","wave mistress","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:baradin-bay","subzone:bluegill-marsh","npc:first-mate-fitzsimmons","quest:270","quest:288","quest:290","quest:292"},src={"Lost Fleet"}}
E["subzone:menethil-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Menethil Bay",z="wetlands",s="Menethil Bay is the sheltered body of water along the western coast of the Wetlands, nestled between Menethil Harbor and the steep northern cliffs of Dun Morogh. Opening outward into the wider Baradin Bay, these waters are home to aggressive crocolisks and the remains of sunken vessels. It serves as the primary maritime approach for Alliance traffic journeying between the Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor.",h="Menethil Bay is the sheltered body of water along the western coast of the Wetlands, nestled between Menethil...",sec={{t="Sheltered Waters of the Wetlands",b="Part of the larger Baradin Bay along the Great Sea, Menethil Bay forms a natural inlet bordered by Menethil Harbor to the north, Black Channel Marsh to the east, and the towering coastal bluffs of Dun Morogh to the south. Its shallow margins and marshy shores crawl with crocolisks of various ages and sizes, making the shallows treacherous for unguided travelers even though the bay serves as the lifeblood of Alliance maritime travel. Near the mouth of the bay lies the ruined wreckage of the Flying Osprey, a silent reminder of the dangers lurking beneath the surface.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where exactly is Menethil Bay located?",a="Menethil Bay is situated on the western coast of the Wetlands. It sits within the larger expanse of Baradin Bay, bounded by Menethil Harbor to the north, Black Channel Marsh to the east, and the northern mountain cliffs of Dun Morogh to the south.",al={"where is menethil bay","menethil bay location","wetlands bay"}},{q="What creatures live in Menethil Bay?",a="The bay's marshy shores and shallow inlets are heavily populated by crocolisks of various sizes. They are known to ambush unwary swimmers and are often hunted by leatherworkers seeking valuable hides.",al={"menethil bay mobs","what is in the bay","crocolisks in menethil bay"}},{q="What is the sunken ship in the bay?",a="The wreckage located near the entrance of Menethil Bay belongs to the Flying Osprey, a lost vessel resting beneath the coastal waters near the harbor approaches.",al={"shipwreck menethil bay","flying osprey","sunken ship wetlands"}},{q="Why is the bay important to the Alliance?",a="The bay shelters Menethil Harbor, which is the primary naval gate connecting Ironforge and the northern lands of Khaz Modan to Kalimdor and the south. Transport ships navigating to and from Theramore and Darkshore must traverse these waters.",al={"importance of menethil bay","alliance port wetlands","menethil harbor water"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Bay is the vital sea approach to Menethil Harbor, securing the fragile sea lane that connects Ironforge and Stormwind to Kalimdor."},kw={"baradin bay","crocolisk","dun morogh","flying osprey","menethil bay","menethil harbor","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","zone:wetlands","subzone:baradin-bay","subzone:black-channel-marsh","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Menethil Bay"}}
E["subzone:menethil-harbor"] = {t="subzone",n="Menethil Harbor",z="wetlands",s="Menethil Harbor is a heavily fortified dwarven port town perched on an island off the western shore of the Wetlands. Built over an old Orcish shipyard and named after King Terenas Menethil II, it acts as the primary maritime lifeline connecting the Eastern Kingdoms to the distant shores of Kalimdor. Sheltered behind massive stone battlements and the sturdy towers of Menethil Keep, it is a bustling hub for merchants, off-duty soldiers, and salty adventurers.",h="Menethil Harbor is a heavily fortified dwarven port town perched on an island off the western shore of the...",sec={{t="A Port Carved from War",b="The site of Menethil Harbor first served Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer during the Second War, when the Horde constructed an invasion armada out of timber and iron ransacked from Khaz Modan. After the orcs were routed, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore oversaw the rebuilding of the anchorage into a premier Alliance haven, naming it in tribute to the late King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron. Despite its remote marshland setting, it remains a heavily defended bastion, reinforced by massive walls, a single bridged causeway, and the four stone watchtowers of Menethil Keep.",sp=0},{t="Gateway Across the Great Sea",b="Today, the harbor is the grand crossroads of the Alliance. Ships steam continually across the ocean toward Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh and Auberdine in darkshore, carrying trade, diplomats, and off-duty Kul Tiran marines blowing their wages at the Deepwater Tavern. Yet peace is fragile here: inland supply paths through Dun Algaz are regularly contested by the Dragonmaw clan, while hostile Dark Iron raiders pressure the northern marshes, leaving Captain Stoutfist and the harbor garrison on constant alert.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the ships in Menethil Harbor sail to?",a="Vessels departing the docks of Menethil Harbor cross the Great Sea to the continent of Kalimdor. Scheduled passenger ships run regular routes to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh and north to the night elven haven of Auberdine.",al={"menethil harbor boat","where does the boat go","menethil ferries","kalimdor boats"}},{q="Who rules Menethil Harbor?",a="Menethil Harbor operates as an Alliance settlement under the authority of Ironforge. Captain Stoutfist commands the town guard and coordinates harbor defense out of Menethil Keep, keeping the docks secure from swamp beasts, renegade orcs, and inland raiders.",al={"who is in charge of menethil","menethil harbor leader","who leads menethil"}},{q="Why is the town named Menethil?",a="The harbor was named by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore after the Second War in tribute to King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron, whose leadership united the human, dwarven, and elven realms into the original Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"why menethil harbor","menethil name origin","who is menethil"}},{q="What threats does the harbor face right now?",a="The harbor faces persistent danger from the Dragonmaw clan lurking in the Wetlands hills, who regularly try to cut off the pass through Dun Algaz to starve the port of reinforcements. Dark Iron incursions to the north near Dun Modr and marauding raptors add to the garrison's troubles.",al={"is menethil harbor in danger","menethil threats","wetlands orcs menethil"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For any Alliance traveler journeying west, Menethil Harbor is the vital staging ground and sole maritime bridge linking the Eastern Kingdoms to Theramore and Kalimdor.",["race:Dwarf"]="Though bearing a human king's name, this port is maintained primarily by dwarven stonework and manned by Ironforge guards holding the outer threshold of Khaz Modan."},kw={"auberdine","boat","deepwater","docks","ferry","harbor","menethil","stoutfist","theramore","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-keep","subzone:deepwater-tavern","subzone:theramore-isle","subzone:auberdine","npc:captain-stoutfist","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","subzone:dun-algaz"},src={"Menethil Harbor"}}
E["subzone:menethil-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Menethil Keep",z="wetlands",s="Menethil Keep is the stone stronghold dominating the skyline of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands. Marked by four sturdy watchtowers, it serves as the administrative heart and defensive bastion of the Alliance port, housing the local militia commander, Captain Stoutfist.",h="Menethil Keep is the stone stronghold dominating the skyline of Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands.",sec={{t="Bastion of the Harbor",b="Rising above the wooden docks and soggy marshes of the Wetlands, Menethil Keep is the central military strongpoint of Menethil Harbor. With four stone watchtowers gazing out over the town and the bay, the fortress offers a commanding view against seaward raiders, renegades, and the encroaching swamp beasts. Inside, Captain Stoutfist oversees the defense of the port, directing the town militia and organizing patrols to safeguard Alliance interests throughout the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Menethil Keep used for?",a="Menethil Keep serves as the headquarters of the Menethil Harbor town militia and the main Alliance command post in the Wetlands. Captain Stoutfist commands the local garrison from within its stone walls, directing defense efforts and organizing adventurers to address threats throughout the marsh.",al={"purpose of menethil keep","menethil keep role","what is this castle"}},{q="Who is in charge of Menethil Keep?",a="Captain Stoutfist commands the keep and the Menethil militia. He coordinates the defense of the harbor against local threats such as Dark Iron dwarf raiders, marsh beasts, and pirates.",al={"who leads menethil keep","keep commander","captain stoutfist"}},{q="Where is the keep located?",a="The keep stands conspicuously inside Menethil Harbor on the western coast of the Wetlands, looming directly over the settlement with its four tall stone towers.",al={"where is menethil keep","menethil keep location","how to find menethil keep"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers arriving by ship from Kalimdor or journeying north toward Ironforge and Arathi, Menethil Keep represents the principal military stronghold ensuring the safety of this vital transport hub."},kw={"captain stoutfist","menethil harbor","menethil keep","militia","towers","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","npc:captain-stoutfist","zone:wetlands","topic:alliance"},src={"Menethil Keep"}}
E["subzone:mosshide-fen"] = {t="subzone",n="Mosshide Fen",z="wetlands",s="Mosshide Fen is a swampy, treacherous tract in the eastern Wetlands overrun by the Mosshide gnoll tribe. Dotted with primitive encampments, it is one of the most perilous regions for travelers venturing off the main trade roads.",h="Mosshide Fen is a swampy, treacherous tract in the eastern Wetlands overrun by the Mosshide gnoll tribe.",sec={{t="Territory of the Pack",b="Sprawling across the murky eastern reaches of the Wetlands, Mosshide Fen serves as the primary domain of the aggressive Mosshide gnolls. The swamp here is dense and tangled, dotted with rough lean-tos and bone-strewn camps. Under the vicious command of pack leaders like Gnawbone, the gnolls fiercely guard their muddy claims, readily ambushing and devouring any travelers, scouts, or prospectors foolish enough to wander into their hunting grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mosshide Fen?",a="Mosshide Fen is a subzone situated in the eastern Wetlands. It consists of sodden marshland entirely claimed and settled by the Mosshide gnolls.",al={"mosshide fen lore","what is this place","mosshide swamp"}},{q="Who rules Mosshide Fen?",a="The Mosshide gnoll tribe occupies the fen, taking orders from brutal leaders such as Gnawbone, who commands his pack to capture and devour any outsiders trespassing on their land.",al={"who leads the gnolls here","gnawbone","mosshide leader"}},{q="Why is this area dangerous to travelers?",a="The gnolls of Mosshide Fen are notorious for their aggression and carnivorous appetite. Travelers straying off established pathways or searching the sodden brush for supplies face sudden ambushes from roving hunting packs.",al={"why is it dangerous","fen dangers"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The Ironforge mountaineers must continually keep an eye on Mosshide Fen, as the aggressive gnoll packs threaten prospectors scouring the marshes and scouts securing the eastern paths."},kw={"gnawbone","gnolls","marshlands","mosshide","mosshide fen","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:gnoll","subzone:marshlands"},src={"Mosshide Fen"}}
E["subzone:raptor-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Raptor Ridge",z="wetlands",s="Raptor Ridge is an elevated, rugged expanse in the eastern Wetlands, sitting northwest of the fortified Dragonmaw Gates. It serves as the primary hunting and nesting grounds for packs of ferocious Razormaw raptors, overseen by a particularly vicious matriarch deep within its caverns.",h="Raptor Ridge is an elevated, rugged expanse in the eastern Wetlands, sitting northwest of the fortified...",sec={{t="A Den of Predators",b="Rising above the sodden marshes of the eastern Wetlands, Raptor Ridge is among the most perilous wilderness areas in the region. Vicious Razormaw raptors prowl its crags and rocky trails in large packs, making travel near the foothills of Khaz Modan hazardous for wanderers. At the heart of the ridge lies a brooding cavern dominated by the Razormaw Matriarch, whose aggressive brood aggressively defends their nests against any encroaching predators or foolish travelers wandering too close to the Dragonmaw Gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Raptor Ridge located?",a="Raptor Ridge lies in the far eastern reaches of the Wetlands, directly northwest of the Dragonmaw Gates that guard the road up toward Grim Batol.",al={"raptor ridge location","where is raptor ridge","how to get to raptor ridge"}},{q="What creatures live here?",a="The ridge is crawling with Razormaw raptors. Deep within its cavern, travelers will also find the Razormaw Matriarch guarding her nests and hatchlings.",al={"what mobs are at raptor ridge","raptors in wetlands","raptor ridge beasts"}},{q="Who is the Razormaw Matriarch?",a="The Razormaw Matriarch is the massive, deadly leader of the local raptor packs, brooding over her clutch inside the ridge's central cave.",al={"razormaw matriarch","raptor matriarch wetlands","raptor boss wetlands"}},{q="Why is the area so dangerous to traverse?",a="Aside from dense packs of aggressive, fast-moving raptors that swarm trespassers, the ridge sits right in the shadow of hostile Dragonmaw orc territory near the mountain passes.",al={"is raptor ridge dangerous","raptor ridge threat"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The fierce Razormaw raptors of the ridge make potent, aggressive beasts for any hunter seeking a swift and tenacious marshland companion."},kw={"dragonmaw gates","raptor ridge","razormaw","razormaw matriarch","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:dragonmaw-gates","subzone:grim-batol","subzone:menethil-harbor"},src={"Raptor Ridge"}}
E["subzone:saltspray-glen"] = {t="subzone",n="Saltspray Glen",z="wetlands",s="Saltspray Glen is a windswept expanse in the northwestern Wetlands hugging the shores of Baradin Bay. Strong coastal gales regularly fling briny seawater across the mossy lowland, which is overrun by aggressive wild raptors. It forms a treacherous natural corridor between neighboring murloc-infested marshes and ancient dwarven ruins.",h="Saltspray Glen is a windswept expanse in the northwestern Wetlands hugging the shores of Baradin Bay.",sec={{t="Brine and Claws",b="Tucked away in the far northwestern reach of the Wetlands, Saltspray Glen takes its name from the sea spray driven inland off Baradin Bay whenever coastal gales kick up. Bordered by the murloc-haunted waters of Bluegill Marsh to the south and the quiet bluffs of Ironbeard's Tomb to the east, the glen offers little comfort to passing travelers. Packs of cunning wild raptors nest throughout the marshy grass, hunting along the brackish flats alongside their kin from nearby Raptor Ridge and Black Channel Marsh.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Saltspray Glen?",a="The glen sits directly along the open coast of Baradin Bay. Whenever fierce maritime winds whip across the bay from the north and west, ocean water is tossed far inland across the low-lying terrain as a dense, salty mist.",al={"saltspray glen name meaning","why saltspray","origin of name"}},{q="What creatures live in Saltspray Glen?",a="The glen is thoroughly overrun by aggressive wild raptors that use the coastal brush and marshy hollows as prime nesting grounds. They readily ambush anyone wandering off the beaten path.",al={"monsters in saltspray glen","saltspray raptors","what is here"}},{q="Where does Saltspray Glen lead?",a="Saltspray Glen lies in the northwestern Wetlands. It borders Baradin Bay to the north and west, the murloc territory of Bluegill Marsh to the south, and the rocky rise of Ironbeard's Tomb to the east.",al={"saltspray glen location","where is saltspray glen","borders"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The vicious raptors prowling the glen's damp sea-grass provide hearty quarry and dependable, fierce beasts for trackers stalking the coast."},kw={"baradin bay","bluegill marsh","ironbeard's tomb","raptors","saltspray glen","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:baradin-bay","subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb","subzone:bluegill-marsh","subzone:raptor-ridge","subzone:black-channel-marsh","subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site"},src={"Saltspray Glen"}}
E["subzone:sundown-marsh"] = {t="subzone",n="Sundown Marsh",z="wetlands",s="Sundown Marsh marks the deepest, westernmost reaches of the Wetlands where stagnant waters meet treacherous wildlife. Despite the prowling raptors, oozes, and gnolls, an eccentric pair maintains a solitary homestead along its muddy borders.",h="Sundown Marsh marks the deepest, westernmost reaches of the Wetlands where stagnant waters meet treacherous...",sec={{t="A Wild and Murky Sinkhole",b="Sundown Marsh sits tucked into the northwest of the Wetlands, characterized by deep water, thick mud, and a dense population of predators. Giant crocolisks, shifting oozes, roaming raptors, and territorial Mosshide gnolls roam freely through the mist. The hazardous terrain keeps most passing travelers strictly to the main cobblestone road connecting Menethil Harbor to Ironforge, leaving this deep corner largely untamed.",sp=0},{t="Life at the Edge of the Mire",b="Amid the hazards of the marsh stands a lonely stone cottage topped with a churning windmill. There, the gnome Fradd Swiftgear and the dwarf Wenna Silkbeard make an unlikely living scavenging the bog. They peddle curiosities and rare trade recipes recovered from the mire to travelers brave enough to navigate the marsh's aggressive denizens.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Sundown Marsh located?",a="Sundown Marsh is situated in the northwestern area of the Wetlands. It represents one of the lowest and deepest portions of the marshland, lying off the beaten track of the primary royal roads.",al={"sundown marsh location","where is sundown marsh","wetlands marsh location"}},{q="Who lives in Sundown Marsh?",a="An odd pair, the gnome Fradd Swiftgear and the dwarf Wenna Silkbeard, live here in a small stone dwelling equipped with a windmill. They scour the bog for oddities and sell rare goods to passing travelers.",al={"who lives here","sundown marsh npcs","swiftgear cottage"}},{q="What threats can be found in Sundown Marsh?",a="The marsh is thick with dangerous wildlife and monsters, including giant crocolisks, foul oozes, bog beasts, raptors, and hostile Mosshide gnolls that discourage casual exploration.",al={"monsters in sundown marsh","sundown marsh dangers","enemies sundown marsh"}},{q="Why would an adventurer travel into Sundown Marsh?",a="Beyond dealing with local beasts, travelers make the trek to the windmill cottage to trade with Fradd Swiftgear and Wenna Silkbeard, who offer uncommon recipes and peculiar curiosities found in the surrounding swamp.",al={"why visit sundown marsh","reasons to go to sundown marsh","sundown marsh vendors"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Seeing Fradd Swiftgear and Wenna Silkbeard thriving with their windmill outpost out in the dangerous mud proves that gnomish ingenuity can carve out a comfortable home anywhere."},kw={"crocolisks","fradd swiftgear","mosshide","oozes","sundown marsh","swiftgear station","wenna silkbeard","wetlands"},rel={"zone:wetlands","topic:gnoll"},src={"Sundown Marsh"}}
E["subzone:thelgen-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Thelgen Rock",z="wetlands",s="Thelgen Rock is an extensive cavern system cut into the southern mountain wall of the Wetlands. Infested with venomous spiders, it is notorious for harboring rare veins of volatile Incendicite Ore.",h="Thelgen Rock is an extensive cavern system cut into the southern mountain wall of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Web-Choked Cavern",b="Nestled against the southern mountains separating the Wetlands from Loch Modan, Thelgen Rock is a deep subterranean cave network overrun by aggressive arachnids. The passages are thick with webs and crawling with poisonous spiders that make entering the caverns extremely hazardous for travelers. Despite the infestation, miners and adventurers brave its depths for the valuable deposits of Incendicite Ore found embedded in the rocky tunnels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes Thelgen Rock dangerous?",a="The caverns of Thelgen Rock are densely inhabited by large, poisonous spiders. Travelers who venture into the winding tunnels can easily find themselves cornered and overwhelmed by venomous bites amidst the webs.",al={"thelgen rock dangers","why is thelgen rock dangerous","spiders in thelgen rock"}},{q="Why do prospectors and miners come here?",a="The cave system contains rich seams of Incendicite Ore, a fiery and volatile mineral sought after by dwarven prospectors and engineers. Despite the spider infestation, daring miners enter to harvest samples from the cave walls.",al={"why visit thelgen rock","ore in thelgen rock","incendicite ore"}},{q="Where is Thelgen Rock located?",a="Thelgen Rock lies along the southern mountain ridge of the Wetlands, south of the main road that connects Menethil Harbor to the Dun Algaz mountain pass.",al={"thelgen rock location","where is thelgen rock"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The deep tunnels of Thelgen Rock house rare deposits of Incendicite Ore, drawing prospectors into danger beneath the mountain."},kw={"cave","incendicite ore","spider cave","spiders","thelgen rock","wetlands"},rel={"quest:466","zone:wetlands"},src={"Thelgen Rock"}}
E["subzone:whelgar-s-excavation-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Whelgar's Excavation Site",z="wetlands",s="Whelgar's Excavation Site is a dwarven archaeological dig in the eastern hills of the Wetlands. Intended to unearth ancient Titan relics and prehistoric secrets, the expedition ended in disaster when vicious mottled raptors overran the quarry. The surviving excavators are now trapped on a ridge overlooking the dig, cut off from their findings.",h="Whelgar's Excavation Site is a dwarven archaeological dig in the eastern hills of the Wetlands.",sec={{t="A Ruined Expedition",b="Spearheaded by dwarven prospectors searching for ancient fossils and earthen mysteries, the excavation carved out a massive quarry between Menethil Harbor and Dun Modr. However, unearthing prehistoric remnants drew the wrath of native mottled raptors. Overwhelmed and under-equipped, the archaeologists retreated to a ridge overlooking the dig site, leaving their tents, tools, and unearthed relics scattered among prowling predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was the excavation site abandoned?",a="The dwarven excavators accidentally disturbed the territory of aggressive mottled raptors. Overrun by these ferocious creatures, the surviving crew took refuge on a ridge overlooking the dig site.",al={"why is it abandoned","what happened to the digsite","why leave the dig"}},{q="What were the dwarves looking for here?",a="The dwarves were digging for prehistoric fossils and subterranean artifacts in hopes of uncovering ancient clues about their Titan heritage and the world's distant past.",al={"what are they digging for","purpose of the excavation","whelgar digsite goal"}},{q="What threats roam the digsite now?",a="The quarry floor and surrounding ridges are swarming with mottled raptors, including the feared raptor matriarch Sarltooth.",al={"what is in the excavation site","digsite mobs","raptors in wetlands"}},{q="Where did the surviving excavators go?",a="The surviving dig crew, including Prospector Whelgar, are trapped atop a ridge overlooking the dig site, where they seek brave adventurers to recover their lost research.",al={"where is whelgar","where are the dwarves","digsite survivors location"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Every dig abandoned to feral beasts is an insult to the Explorers' League. Reclaiming Whelgar's research means defending your heritage and taking back stolen Titan secrets.",["profession:Mining"]="The massive exposed quarry walls and unearthed bedrock offer prime veins for miners daring enough to work beneath the snarls of hungry raptors."},kw={"digsite","excavation","fossils","raptors","sarltooth","wetlands","whelgar"},rel={"zone:wetlands","subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:dun-modr"},src={"Whelgar's Excavation Site"}}
E["zone:wetlands"] = {t="zone",n="Wetlands",z="wetlands",s="The Wetlands is a vast, mist-shrouded swamp nestled between the mountains of Khaz Modan and the shores of Baradin Bay. Historically battered by dwarven wars and orcish invasions, it serves as a rugged buffer zone between Ironforge and the northern lands of Lordaeron. The fortified port of Menethil Harbor stands as the Alliance's primary lifeline in a sodden wilderness overrun by Dragonmaw orcs, murlocs, and gnolls.",h="The Wetlands is a vast, mist-shrouded swamp nestled between the mountains of Khaz Modan and the shores of...",sec={{t="A Land of Water and Ruin",b="Spreading out beneath the towering precipice of the Stonewrought Dam, the Wetlands is a cold, waterlogged expanse cloaked in perpetual fog and uniform gray skies. While once home to thriving dwarven settlements, the marshlands are now scattered with sunken stone ruins, sodden bogs, and treacherous mires. Adventurers entering the region must navigate narrow passes, either coming north through the barricaded defile of Dun Algaz from Loch Modan or crossing the towering arches of the Thandol Span from the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="The Scars of Grim Batol",b="The eastern reaches of the swamp are dominated by the brooding presence of Grim Batol, the former Wildhammer stronghold. After its defilement during the War of the Three Hammers, it became the fortified redoubt of the Dragonmaw clan during the Second War. When the red dragonflight broke free from orcish captivity, their fiery vengeance shattered the orcish forces and laid waste to the surrounding slopes. Today, red wyrmkin guard the Dragonmaw Gates against all trespassers, while feral remnants of the Dragonmaw clan dwell in scattered hill camps, continuing to harass travellers across the swamp.",sp=0},{t="Port of the West Coast",b="Perched on the rim of Baradin Bay, Menethil Harbor is the beating heart of Alliance trade and logistics in Khaz Modan. Named in honor of King Terenas Menethil II, this stalwart port connects the Eastern Kingdoms to distant Kalimdor through regular transport ships sailing to Auberdine and Theramore Isle. Despite its strategic military importance and solid dwarven architecture, the harbor is perpetually under threat from coastal murlocs, swamp creatures, and coastal raiders who prey on vessels navigating the rocky channels.",sp=0},{t="Besieged Frontiers",b="The Wetlands is an active war zone on multiple fronts. In the far north, Dark Iron dwarves under the warlock Balgaras the Foul have sabotage-bombed the Thandol Span and overrun the town of Dun Modr, cutting off overland supply trains. Meanwhile, Mosshide gnolls run rampant through the central fens, threatening even ancient protectors like Rethiel the Greenwarden. Between rogue orc warbands, Dark Iron infiltrators, and cursed shipwrecks along the coast, holding the swamp requires constant vigilance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I travel to the Wetlands on foot?",a="Alliance adventurers generally travel north from Loch Modan through the mountain pass of Dun Algaz. Horde travelers journeying from the north can cross the Thandol Span from the Arathi Highlands. Take care, as both passageways are contested by hostile forces like Dragonmaw orcs and Dark Iron dwarves.",al={"how to get to wetlands","path to wetlands","run to wetlands"}},{q="Where do the boats at Menethil Harbor go?",a="The docks at Menethil Harbor operate two major ferry routes to Kalimdor: one ship sails across the Great Sea to Auberdine on the shores of Darkshore, while the other sails south to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"menethil boats","menethil harbor ships","where does the boat go in wetlands"}},{q="What is Grim Batol and why is it guarded?",a="Grim Batol is an ancient dwarven fortress abandoned after the War of the Three Hammers and later occupied by the Dragonmaw clan. Following the Second War, the liberated red dragonflight drove out the orcs and sealed the mountain. Powerful red dragonspawn and wyrmkin patrol the Dragonmaw Gates to prevent anyone from entering the cursed halls.",al={"why are there dragons at grim batol","grim batol red dragons","dragonmaw gates"}},{q="What happened to Dun Modr?",a="Dun Modr was a northern dwarven stronghold guarding the Thandol Span. It was recently attacked and overrun by Dark Iron dwarves led by Balgaras the Foul. The survivors, led by Rhag Garmason, maintain an embattled encampment nearby while fighting to reclaim their town.",al={"who destroyed dun modr","dun modr ruins","dark irons in dun modr"}},{q="Who is Rethiel the Greenwarden?",a="Rethiel is an ancient keeper residing in Greenwarden's Grove along the Green Belt. He seeks help from travelers to stem the tide of aggressive Mosshide gnolls and heal his corrupted bog beast kin who wander the fen.",al={"greenwardens grove","rethiel wetlands","who is the greenwarden"}},{q="Where did all the orcs in the swamp come from?",a="The orcs belong to the Dragonmaw clan, who originally fortified themselves in Grim Batol during the Second War. After being devastated by the freed red dragonflight, the surviving orcs fled down into the swamp and hills, where they still launch raids on roadways and travelers.",al={"why are there orcs in wetlands","wetlands dragonmaw","dragonmaw clan wetlands"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the Wetlands is a bittersweet place marked by the loss of Dun Modr, the ancient tragedy of Grim Batol, and the ongoing labor of defending King Magni's trade route to the north.",["faction:Alliance"]="Menethil Harbor serves as the Alliance's primary deep-water gateway across the Great Sea, linking the kingdoms of the east with expeditionary outposts in Kalimdor.",["profession:Mining"]="The hills and cavernous depths of Thelgen Rock hold rich mineral veins, including rare deposits of Incendicite ore coveted by dwarven miners and engineers."},kw={"baradin bay","dragonmaw","dun algaz","dun modr","grim batol","menethil","menethil harbor","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:menethil-harbor","subzone:grim-batol","subzone:dun-modr","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:dun-algaz","topic:dragonmaw-clan","npc:rethiel-the-greenwarden","quest:455"},m={levels="20-30"},src={"Wetlands (Classic)","Wetlands"}}
